        "1668": {"synopsis":"Characters & to / become symbols $06-$0F; others are looked up in SYM_CHARS.","comment":"Below \"&\"?"},
        "1672": {"comment":"Above \"/\"?"},
        "1676": {"comment":"& to / = $06-$0F"},
        "1680": {"synopsis":"Looks the character up in SYM_CHARS; its code is the byte 7 places on, in SYM_CODES. Error\n20000 when it is not there.","comment":"SYM_CHARS"},
        "1687": {"comment":"Search the seven"},
        "1690": {"comment":"($0204) = 1 before a possible error"},
        "1695": {"comment":"Not there: error 20000, not understood"},
        "1698": {"comment":"Its code, 7 bytes on"},
        "1701": {"synopsis":"Stores symbol code A in ($0203) and ($0204); a nonzero code moves ($0214) past the\ncharacter.","comment":"Code"},
        "1707": {"comment":"Code 0 (text's end): ($0214) stays"},
        "1709": {"comment":"Past the character"},
        "1716": {"synopsis":"The seven characters SCAN_SYM_TABLE searches: ! \\ # ^ : ; and the zero that ends the text."},
        "1723": {"synopsis":"Their symbol codes, in the same order: $01 (\"!\", a comment), $19, $03, $1B, $10, $11, $00."},
        "1730": {"synopsis":"Moves ($0214) past spaces and TABs.\nExit: HL = ($0214) = the first other character."},
        "1733": {"synopsis":"Steps over spaces and TABs."},
        "1735": {"comment":"Space?"},
        "1739": {"comment":"TAB?"},
        "1743": {"comment":"Back to the other character"},
        "1747": {"synopsis":"Tokenises one statement of a typed line whose first item TEXT_SCAN_TOKEN has just scanned.\n1. The statement word is the scanned name (or \"!\" at the line's end or a \"!\"); it is looked\n   up\nin the keyword tables (KEYWORD_FIND). A name that is no keyword starts an implied LET\n(keyword\n$28).\n2. Error 20072 when the keyword's flags (descriptor +4) lack bit 1.\n3. The word's text becomes the two bytes $60, keyword number.\n4. With carry on entry and flag bit 6, the operands are tokenised too (TOKENISE_REST).\n5. The keyword's check routine runs (KW_CALL_CHECK).\n6. A \":\" after it: with flag bit 4 the next statement is tokenised the same way (no carry)\n   and\nmust have flag bit 4 too; otherwise error 20074 (invalid multi-statement line).\nEntry: HL = the statement's place in the buffer, carry = tokenise operands.","comment":"Carry kept"},
        "1749": {"comment":"Symbol: line's end or \"!\"?"},
        "1756": {"comment":"The word is \"!\" (one character at $0749)"},
        "1768": {"synopsis":"A name starts the statement: it must be a numeric or a string name.","comment":"A numeric name?"},
        "1773": {"comment":"Nor a string name: error 20000"},
        "1778": {"synopsis":"Looks the word up in the keyword tables; a miss is LET (flags $53, keyword $28) from the\nstatement's start.","comment":"Keyword? NZ: C = number, HL = its flags"},
        "1781": {"comment":"B = flags"},
        "1783": {"comment":"Found"},
        "1785": {"comment":"Not a keyword: rescan from the start"},
        "1788": {"comment":"As LET: flags $53, keyword $28"},
        "1791": {"synopsis":"Writes the keyword's token over its word, after checking it may appear here (flag bit 1).","comment":"Flag bit 1 clear: error 20072, command in program"},
        "1796": {"comment":"Two bytes of room for the token"},
        "1799": {"comment":"Fit the word into them"},
        "1803": {"comment":"Keyword number"},
        "1806": {"comment":"Class $60: a keyword"},
        "1808": {"comment":"Operands too?"},
        "1811": {"comment":"Flag bit 6: tokenise them"},
        "1818": {"synopsis":"Runs the keyword's check routine, then deals with a \":\" after the statement."},
        "1819": {"comment":"Keyword C's check routine (descriptor +2)"},
        "1823": {"comment":"Flag bit 4: may be followed by another"},
        "1827": {"comment":"A \":\" next?"},
        "1834": {"comment":"Tokenise the next statement, operands untouched"},
        "1841": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "1846": {"comment":"Its keyword number"},
        "1848": {"comment":"Its flags"},
        "1851": {"comment":"Flag bit 4 too?"},
        "1853": {"synopsis":"Returns while the test says no \":\" problem; otherwise falls into error 20074."},
        "1854": {"comment":"Error 20074, invalid multi-statement line"},
        "1858": {"synopsis":"Without flag bit 4 a \":\" after the statement is error 20074.","comment":"A \":\" next?"},
        "1865": {"synopsis":"The one-character name \"!\" (and a zero) that STMT_TOKENISE points ($0347) at for a line's\nend or a \"!\"."},
        "1867": {"synopsis":"Enters a typed line whose number TEXT_SCAN_TOKEN has read into ($0218).\n1. Line number 0: returns C (the line is a command to run).\n2. LINE_FIND it. Empty text: a line that exists is deleted (LINE_DELETE_DE); otherwise\n   nothing.\n3. Builds the line in the buffer at $0248: the text moves to $024C, then the number and\n   indent 0 go\nbefore it, and STMT_TOKENISE tokenises it (carry: operands too).\n4. An existing line of that number is removed (LINE_DELETE), PROG_OPEN_GAP opens room for\n   the new\none, the buffer is copied in, and RUN_STATE_RESET runs.","comment":"Line number"},
        "1870": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "1872": {"comment":"Zero: C, a command"},
        "1874": {"comment":"LINE_FIND ($03FA): Z found, C not"},
        "1877": {"comment":"DE = the line or the next one"},
        "1878": {"comment":"A = $FF when not found, 0 when found"},
        "1879": {"comment":"Text after the number"},
        "1882": {"comment":"Found and empty: delete it"},
        "1886": {"comment":"Not found and empty: nothing to do"},
        "1889": {"comment":"A = found flag again (Z when found)"},
        "1892": {"comment":"The text goes to $024C"},
        "1896": {"comment":"Move it there"},
        "1900": {"comment":"Indent byte 0"},
        "1903": {"comment":"Line number before it"},
        "1910": {"comment":"Scan the first item"},
        "1914": {"comment":"Carry: tokenise operands too"},
        "1915": {"comment":"Tokenise the statement(s)"},
        "1918": {"comment":"Found flag"},
        "1921": {"comment":"Remove the old line of that number"},
        "1925": {"comment":"BC = the new line's length"},
        "1931": {"comment":"Open room for it in the program"},
        "1935": {"comment":"Copy it from the buffer"},
        "1940": {"comment":"Reset variables and stack"},
        "1943": {"synopsis":"EDIT statement's action (keyword descriptor at $367D): reads which program (PROG_ARG_READ)\nand\nfalls into EDIT_SELECT."},
        "1946": {"synopsis":"Makes the program chosen by PROG_ARG_READ current: a number ($0212) is switched to directly\n(PROG_SWITCH); a name is searched for in programs 0-127 whose segment exists (SEG_TAG_FIND):\neach\nis\nswitched to and its PROGRAM line compared (PROG_NAME_TEST). If none matches, the current\nprogram\nnumber (ix+$0A) and line ($0216) are put back and error 10005 (program does not exist)\nfollows.","comment":"Current program number"},
        "1949": {"comment":"Current line"},
        "1952": {"comment":"Both kept in the other set"},
        "1953": {"comment":"Program number, or $FF for a name"},
        "1958": {"comment":"A number: switch to it"},
        "1961": {"comment":"A name: start from program 0"},
        "1965": {"synopsis":"Skips program C when no segment is tagged with it.","comment":"Segment tagged C?"},
        "1968": {"comment":"None: next number"},
        "1970": {"synopsis":"Switches to program C and compares its PROGRAM name with the wanted one at $0E34."},
        "1971": {"comment":"Switch to program C"},
        "1975": {"comment":"Starts with PROGRAM \"name\"?"},
        "1981": {"comment":"Push the name"},
        "1984": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "1986": {"comment":"Segment 1's STR_CASE_FLIP"},
        "1989": {"comment":"The wanted name"},
        "1992": {"comment":"Push it"},
        "1995": {"comment":"Compare the two"},
        "1999": {"comment":"Same: make it current"},
        "2002": {"synopsis":"Next program number; past 127 the search fails."},
        "2003": {"comment":"Up to 127"},
        "2006": {"comment":"Original number and line back"},
        "2013": {"comment":"Error 10005, program does not exist"},
        "2016": {"synopsis":"Reads a program's name or number: a string (a string name or a literal) is upper-cased and\nstored\nin the string variable at $0E34 (up to 31 characters) with ($0212) = $FF; otherwise a\nnumeric\nexpression 0-127 goes into ($0212) (error 1000 for others).","comment":"$FF: by name"},
        "2020": {"comment":"A string next?"},
        "2025": {"comment":"Push it"},
        "2028": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "2030": {"comment":"Segment 1's STR_CASE_FLIP"},
        "2033": {"comment":"Into the variable at $0E34"},
        "2036": {"comment":"Up to 31 characters"},
        "2041": {"synopsis":"A program number: an expression 0-127 into ($0212).","comment":"Expression as a byte (error 1000 above 255)"},
        "2044": {"comment":"128-255: error 1000"},
        "2048": {"comment":"Program number"},
        "2052": {"synopsis":"Tests the current program's first line: Z when its first statement is PROGRAM (keyword $39)\nand the token after it is a string literal (class $80), with the token reader on it ($0214);\nNZ\notherwise. ($0216) = the first line.","comment":"Program start"},
        "2055": {"comment":"Current line = the first"},
        "2058": {"comment":"Length 0: no lines"},
        "2062": {"comment":"Keyword number of the first statement"},
        "2067": {"synopsis":"Is it PROGRAM? Then reads the token after it.","comment":"PROGRAM?"},
        "2070": {"comment":"Read the token after it"},
        "2077": {"comment":"Z when a string literal"},
        "2083": {"synopsis":"AUTO statement's action (keyword descriptor at $35BE): segment 1's STMT_AUTO.","comment":"Segment 1's STMT_AUTO"},
        "2087": {"synopsis":"RENUMBER statement's action (keyword descriptor at $3850): segment 1's STMT_RENUMBER.","comment":"Segment 1's STMT_RENUMBER"},
        "2091": {"synopsis":"LLIST, LIST and DELETE statements' actions. LLIST (descriptor at $3928) starts here with\nchannel\n$68; LIST (descriptor at $3779) enters at $082E, inside LD B,$AF, with XOR A: channel 0. An\noptional #channel overrides it (CHANNEL_ARG). Then the lines are re-indented and the mode\nset in\nAF':\ncarry for LIST, enter at $083D (DELETE, descriptor at $3648) inside LD A,$F6 for no carry.\nNo\nrange lists or deletes every line (segment 1's LIST_LINES, 0 to 10000), a range goes through\nsegment 1's LIST_RANGES.","comment":"LLIST: channel $68"},
        "2093": {"comment":"Hides LIST's entry at $082E: XOR A, channel 0"},
        "2095": {"synopsis":"LIST's and LLIST's common part: the output channel, then the line indents.","comment":"Default channel kept"},
        "2096": {"comment":"#channel given? Z: ($0209) set"},
        "2102": {"comment":"No: ($0209) = the default"},
        "2105": {"synopsis":"Re-indents the program's lines, then picks LIST's mode (carry) in AF'.","comment":"Segment 1's LINES_REINDENT"},
        "2108": {"comment":"Hides DELETE's entry at $083D: OR $37, no carry"},
        "2110": {"comment":"LIST: carry"},
        "2111": {"comment":"Mode in AF': carry lists, no carry deletes"},
        "2112": {"comment":"Clear flag bit 2"},
        "2116": {"comment":"Last line + 1: 10000"},
        "2119": {"comment":"Nothing after the word?"},
        "2124": {"comment":"From line 0"},
        "2128": {"comment":"Segment 1's LIST_RANGES"},
        "2132": {"synopsis":"No range: every line from 0 to 10000.","comment":"Segment 1's LIST_LINES"},
        "2136": {"synopsis":"Lists the program line at HL on the current channel ($0209). The line's text is built in\nmemory at $0347 (LINE_TEXT_BUILDW, with the line number and the indentation) and written\nwith\nEXOS 8 (MEM_BLOCK_WRITE). On channel 0 (the editor) the indentation is capped by the window:\nEXOS 11 function 24 (MARG, margins, D = E = $FF) gives the right and left margins, and\n(right -\nleft - 6) / 4 levels are shown; code $18 sets the left margin after the indentation, $19\nends\nthe text, and MARG puts the margins back before the CR LF.","comment":"Current channel"},
        "2140": {"comment":"Z: channel 0"},
        "2141": {"comment":"Other channels: no indentation limit"},
        "2145": {"comment":"MARG (24), margins"},
        "2147": {"comment":"Both $FF"},
        "2150": {"comment":"Channel 0"},
        "2151": {"comment":"EXOS 11: D = right, E = left margin"},
        "2153": {"comment":"EXOS error?"},
        "2154": {"comment":"Window width - 6"},
        "2158": {"comment":"Too narrow: no indentation ($0876 = XOR A)"},
        "2161": {"comment":"Four columns per level"},
        "2165": {"comment":"Hides $0876: XOR A, no levels"},
        "2167": {"synopsis":"Builds the line's text with indent levels up to C, then writes it.","comment":"C = the levels allowed"},
        "2171": {"comment":"Carry: number padded, indents shown"},
        "2173": {"comment":"Build the text at $0347"},
        "2178": {"comment":"Not channel 0: CR LF and write"},
        "2181": {"comment":"$19 after the text"},
        "2188": {"comment":"Write it to channel 0, no CR LF"},
        "2192": {"comment":"MARG (24) with the saved margins"},
        "2195": {"comment":"EXOS 11: margins back"},
        "2197": {"comment":"EXOS error?"},
        "2198": {"comment":"CR LF on channel 0"},
        "2201": {"synopsis":"Adds CR LF to the stored text when NZ, then falls into MEM_BLOCK_WRITE with channel A."},
        "2202": {"comment":"CR LF stored when NZ"},
        "2206": {"synopsis":"Sets ($0209) = A and writes the bytes stored from $0347 up to ($0242) to that channel with\nEXOS 8 (write block); EXOS errors raised. HL kept.","comment":"Channel"},
        "2210": {"comment":"Store pointer"},
        "2213": {"comment":"From the buffer at $0347"},
        "2217": {"comment":"BC = bytes stored"},
        "2221": {"comment":"EXOS 8: write block"},
        "2223": {"comment":"EXOS error?"},
        "2226": {"synopsis":"Lists the program line at HL on channel ($0209) without line number padding or indentation\n(LINE_TEXT_BUILD), CR LF after it, in one EXOS 8 write.","comment":"Channel kept (the build changes ($0209))"},
        "2230": {"comment":"Build the text at $0347"},
        "2233": {"comment":"CR LF"},
        "2237": {"comment":"Channel back"},
        "2240": {"comment":"Write the text"},
        "2242": {"synopsis":"LINE_TEXT_BUILDW with no carry: the line number unpadded, no indentation.","comment":"Any level (none is shown anyway)"},
        "2244": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "2245": {"synopsis":"Builds the text of the program line at HL in memory at $0347 (($0209) = $FF: PRINT_CHAR\nstores at ($0242)): the line number, a space, the indentation, then the statements\n(DETOK_ITEM per\ntoken; text after a keyword without flag bit 6, such as REM, is copied as it is).\nEntry: HL = the line, C = the most indent levels shown, A = the channel, carry = a space and\nthe number padded to the width, indentation shown, and $18 first on channel 0.\nExit: HL past the line's zero.","comment":"Carry and channel kept"},
        "2246": {"comment":"Output into memory"},
        "2250": {"comment":"From $0347"},
        "2257": {"comment":"Leading space when carry"},
        "2260": {"comment":"Line number"},
        "2261": {"comment":"Print it"},
        "2264": {"comment":"Space after it"},
        "2267": {"comment":"Indent byte (+3)"},
        "2271": {"comment":"Indent level when carry, else 0"},
        "2275": {"comment":"Below the cap?"},
        "2280": {"comment":"Cap it"},
        "2281": {"synopsis":"Prints two spaces per indent level, then $18 on channel 0 when carry.","comment":"First item (+4)"},
        "2282": {"comment":"Two spaces per level"},
        "2283": {"comment":"Print them"},
        "2287": {"comment":"No carry: no margin code"},
        "2290": {"comment":"$18: left margin here (channel 0 only)"},
        "2295": {"synopsis":"Items of the line: E bit 0 = tokens (else plain text), bit 1 = the last item ends a word.","comment":"Z: the first pass decodes nothing"},
        "2296": {"comment":"Tokens, no word before"},
        "2299": {"synopsis":"Decodes the token at HL (DETOK_ITEM) unless it is the line's end.","comment":"Back to the item"},
        "2300": {"comment":"Decode a token"},
        "2303": {"synopsis":"Takes the next byte: the line's end returns, a token is decoded, plain text is printed as it\nis.","comment":"Next byte"},
        "2305": {"comment":"Line's end"},
        "2307": {"comment":"Tokens?"},
        "2311": {"comment":"Plain text: print it"},
        "2316": {"synopsis":"Prints one token at HL with the handler of its class from DETOK_TABLE, a space first when\nthe\nlast item ended a word (E bit 1) and this one is not a symbol.\nEntry: HL = the token, E = the flags.\nExit: HL past it, E updated.","comment":"Class bits"},
        "2319": {"comment":"A symbol: no space before"},
        "2324": {"comment":"Last item ended a word?"},
        "2326": {"comment":"Space between them"},
        "2330": {"synopsis":"Runs the class's handler from DETOK_TABLE (the words after the call's return address $0920).","comment":"Class to 0-7"},
        "2333": {"comment":"Handler at $0922 + 2n"},
        "2336": {"comment":"The handlers return here"},
        "2337": {"synopsis":"An unused byte between DETOK_DISPATCH's RET and its table."},
        "2338": {"synopsis":"DETOK_ITEM's handlers, one word per token class, read by CALL_TABLE_A from the call at\n$091D:\nsymbol\nDETOK_SYMBOL, numeric and string name DETOK_NAME, keyword DETOK_KEYWORD, string literal\nDETOK_STRING, line number and numeric constant DETOK_NUMBER."},
        "2352": {"synopsis":"Prints a symbol token: its characters (SYMBOL_PRINT); \"!\" gets a space before it and\nswitches\nto plain text, \"#\" a space after a word, and \")\" ends a word.","comment":"Code"},
        "2355": {"comment":"\"!\" (a comment)?"},
        "2359": {"comment":"Space before it"},
        "2362": {"comment":"The rest is plain text"},
        "2364": {"synopsis":"Tests for \"#\"."},
        "2365": {"comment":"\"#\"?"},
        "2369": {"comment":"After a word: a space"},
        "2374": {"synopsis":"Prints the symbol and says whether it ends a word."},
        "2375": {"comment":"Its characters"},
        "2378": {"comment":"Does not end a word"},
        "2381": {"comment":"\")\" does"},
        "2384": {"synopsis":"Marks that the item ends a word (E bit 1)."},
        "2387": {"synopsis":"Prints a name token: its characters, length from the header's low 5 bits; the name ends a\nword."},
        "2390": {"comment":"Length"},
        "2394": {"comment":"Print the characters (PRINT_COUNTED's loop)"},
        "2397": {"synopsis":"Prints a keyword token ($60, number) as its word from the keyword's descriptor; a keyword\nwith\nflag bit 6 gets a space after it and keeps token mode, others switch to plain text."},
        "2398": {"comment":"Keyword number"},
        "2402": {"comment":"HL = its flags (descriptor +4)"},
        "2406": {"comment":"Plain text after it"},
        "2408": {"comment":"Flag bit 6: operands are tokens"},
        "2414": {"synopsis":"Prints the keyword's word, with a space after it when its operands are tokens."},
        "2415": {"comment":"The word (length first, descriptor +5)"},
        "2420": {"comment":"Space after it"},
        "2423": {"comment":"Ends no word"},
        "2427": {"synopsis":"Prints a string literal token in quotes, a quote inside doubled. The JP Z at $0982 hides the\nloop's start at $0983 (CP (HL): a quote?) and is skipped on the first pass.","comment":"Ends a word"},
        "2430": {"comment":"Length + 1 for the loop"},
        "2432": {"comment":"Opening quote"},
        "2434": {"comment":"Hides $0983: CP (HL), LD A,(HL), the loop's start"},
