        "2588": {"comment":"Yes: evaluate the name string"},
        "2591": {"comment":"DE = the string's length byte"},
        "2596": {"synopsis":"SAVE, creating the file: creates channel ($0209) on the counted name at DE (EXOS 2), raising\nan EXOS error, then writes the program (one, or all with ALL) as modules and an end-of-file\nheader and closes the channel.","comment":"The file's channel"},
        "2601": {"comment":"EXOS error raised"},
        "2602": {"comment":"Reset the run state"},
        "2605": {"comment":"Not SAVE ALL?"},
        "2608": {"comment":"Header type 3: a multi-program file"},
        "2613": {"comment":"Program tags from 127 down"},
        "2615": {"synopsis":"SAVE ALL loop: looks for the segment tagged with program number C; skips the number when\nthere is none.","comment":"Segment tagged C? (segment 1's SEG_TAG_FIND)"},
        "2618": {"comment":"None: try the next number"},
        "2620": {"synopsis":"SAVE ALL: selects program C and writes it as a module."},
        "2621": {"comment":"Select program C"},
        "2624": {"comment":"Write it as a type 4 module"},
        "2628": {"synopsis":"SAVE ALL: the next lower program number; number 0 (program 0, always written) is the last.","comment":"Next program number"},
        "2629": {"comment":"Reached 0: write program 0 too"},
        "2631": {"comment":"Go on down to 1"},
        "2634": {"comment":"Z: nothing more to write"},
        "2635": {"synopsis":"SAVE: writes the current program first when NZ, then a type 10 (end of file) header, and\ncloses channel ($0209); EXOS errors raised.","comment":"Single SAVE: write the current program"},
        "2638": {"comment":"Header type 10: end of file"},
        "2643": {"comment":"Close the file"},
        "2650": {"synopsis":"Writes the current program to channel ($0209) as one module: a type 4 header with the\nprogram's length (its lines and the closing 0 byte), then the lines from ($021A) (EXOS 8).\nEXOS errors are raised.","comment":"Recompute nesting depths (segment 1's LINES_REINDENT)"},
        "2653": {"comment":"HL = the closing 0 byte of the program"},
        "2656": {"comment":"From the program's start"},
        "2661": {"comment":"Length without the closing byte"},
        "2663": {"comment":"With it"},
        "2666": {"comment":"Header type 4: one BASIC program"},
        "2671": {"comment":"DE = the program's start"},
        "2672": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "2673": {"comment":"Write the program"},
        "2680": {"synopsis":"Writes a module header of type A with a zero length (falls into WRITE_HEADER).","comment":"Length 0"},
        "2683": {"synopsis":"Writes a 16-byte module header to channel ($0209) (EXOS 8): built at $0DBB as 0, type A,\nlength HL, the current program number ($020A), then zeros.\nEntry: A = type, HL = length.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"DE = the length"},
        "2684": {"comment":"16 bytes"},
        "2686": {"comment":"Clear $0DBB-$0DCA, going down"},
        "2689": {"synopsis":"Loop: clears the header buffer byte by byte."},
        "2694": {"comment":"Keep the buffer's start, $0DBB"},
        "2696": {"comment":"+1: module type"},
        "2698": {"comment":"+2/+3: length"},
        "2702": {"comment":"+4: the program's number"},
        "2706": {"comment":"The file's channel"},
        "2710": {"comment":"BC = 16 (B is 0 after the loop)"},
        "2712": {"comment":"Write the header"},
        "2716": {"synopsis":"Keyword handler that does nothing but set ($0206) = 2, so that the run loop goes on at the\nnext line without checking the rest of this one. The keyword table gives it to DATA, IMAGE,\nREM, END IF, END SELECT, \"!\" and PROGRAM (and as the second word of many entries); CONTINUE\nand RUN's end come here too.","comment":"After this statement: on at the next line"},
        "2721": {"synopsis":"LOAD, a file that is not in module form (EXOS 29 gave .ASCII, or .ITYPE with type 0): first\nbyte $1A means nothing to load; otherwise the current program is cleared and the file is\nread as typed lines (C3D7) until it ends; a line without a line number is error 20080.","comment":"B = the file's first byte"},
        "2722": {"comment":"Byte $1A: an empty text file?"},
        "2727": {"comment":"Clear the current program"},
        "2731": {"comment":"NC for the line reader"},
        "2732": {"comment":"Enter the file's lines as typed lines"},
        "2735": {"comment":"Read to the end: next module"},
        "2737": {"synopsis":"Raises error 20080, \"Invalid file format\" (run).","comment":"Error 20080, \"Invalid file format\""},
        "2741": {"synopsis":"LOAD [#n:] [\"name\"]: releases the ALLOCATE area, opens the file (default channel $6A), then\nloads module after module with EXOS 29 until .NOMOD: EXOS's own types load themselves, BASIC\ntypes (2 relocatable code, 3 all programs, 4 one program) and text files are read here. When\na header asked for it (byte +5), the loaded program is started (RUN).","comment":"Release the ALLOCATE code area"},
        "2744": {"comment":"Open the file; AF = its channel, kept on the stack"},
        "2747": {"synopsis":"LOAD: clears the auto-start flag and loads the next module (falls through).","comment":"No auto-start yet"},
        "2748": {"synopsis":"LOAD: stores A as the auto-start flag ($0E0B) and loads the next module.","comment":"($0E0B) = run after loading?"},
        "2751": {"synopsis":"LOAD: takes the channel from the stack (carry cleared) and loads the next module.","comment":"The file's channel"},
        "2752": {"comment":"No carry: keep the ALLOCATE area"},
        "2753": {"synopsis":"Loads the next module from channel A with EXOS 29 (header to $0DBB) and handles the status.\nEntry: A = channel, carry set to release the ALLOCATE area first (RUN \"name\" enters here);\nthe channel stays on the stack.","comment":"Keep the channel"},
        "2754": {"comment":"Carry: release the ALLOCATE area"},
        "2757": {"comment":"The 16-byte header buffer"},
        "2762": {"comment":"EXOS 29 loads a module"},
        "2764": {"synopsis":"LOAD: acts on EXOS 29's status: 0 loaded (next module), .ASCII text, .ITYPE a type for\nBASIC, .NOMOD the end; any other error is raised.","comment":"Loaded by EXOS or an extension?"},
        "2765": {"comment":"Yes: the next module"},
        "2767": {"comment":"$EF .ASCII: not a module file?"},
        "2771": {"comment":"$EE .ITYPE: a type EXOS left to us?"},
        "2775": {"comment":"$EC .NOMOD (the end) or an error?"},
        "2777": {"comment":"Other errors raised"},
        "2778": {"synopsis":"LOAD, end of file: when the auto-start flag is set, puts the RUN entry ($0E7E) under the\nreturn address so that returning starts the program; then closes the file.","comment":"Auto-start asked for?"},
        "2784": {"comment":"RUN's entry, inside STMT_START"},
        "2787": {"comment":"Under the channel"},
        "2789": {"synopsis":"LOAD, MERGE, VERIFY: resets the run state, takes the channel from the stack and closes it\n(EXOS 3); EXOS errors raised.","comment":"Reset the run state"},
        "2792": {"comment":"The file's channel"},
        "2793": {"comment":"Close the file"},
        "2797": {"synopsis":"LOAD, .ITYPE: branches on the header's module type in B: 0 a text file, 1 bad, 2 relocatable\ncode, 3 all programs, 4 one program; 5 and up error 20080. For 3 and 4 header byte +5\nbecomes the auto-start flag.","comment":"B = the module type"},
        "2799": {"comment":"Type 0: read as text"},
        "2801": {"comment":"Type 1: bad file"},
        "2805": {"comment":"Type 2: user relocatable module"},
        "2809": {"comment":"Header +5: run after loading"},
        "2815": {"comment":"Type 4: one BASIC program"},
        "2817": {"comment":"Types 5 and up: bad file"},
        "2819": {"comment":"Type 3: all programs; delete every program"},
        "2822": {"synopsis":"LOAD, a multi-program file: loads the next header; a type 4 module is the program numbered\nin header byte +4, which is selected and read; another type is handled as by LOAD_OWN_TYPE,\nother statuses as by LOAD_STATUS.","comment":"The file's channel"},
        "2827": {"comment":"Next module"},
        "2829": {"comment":"Not .ITYPE: the usual handling"},
        "2833": {"comment":"Another program (type 4)?"},
        "2838": {"comment":"($0212) = 0"},
        "2841": {"comment":"Header +4: the program's number"},
        "2845": {"comment":"Select that program"},
        "2848": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "2853": {"synopsis":"LOAD, a type 4 module: reads the program into the current one, then goes on with the next\nmodule.","comment":"Read the program"},
        "2858": {"synopsis":"LOAD, a type 2 module (user relocatable code): opens a gap of the header's size (+2/+3) at\nprogram 0's start, loads the module with EXOS 30 at ($021E), moves ($021E), ($021A), ($0220)\nand ($021C) past it, and calls its initialisation (header +4/+5, an offset from the load\naddress) unless that is $FFFF. Error 5110 \"Insufficient extension space\" when the code would\nreach $4000.","comment":"Keep the current program's number"},
        "2862": {"comment":"Select program 0"},
        "2865": {"comment":"Program 0's start"},
        "2868": {"comment":"Header +2: the module's size"},
        "2873": {"comment":"Past $3FFF?"},
        "2877": {"comment":"Error 5110, \"Insufficient extension space\""},
        "2880": {"comment":"HL = program 0's start; new start kept"},
        "2881": {"comment":"Move program 0 up by BC"},
        "2885": {"comment":"DE = the load address"},
        "2889": {"comment":"Program 0 starts after the module"},
        "2892": {"comment":"The ALLOCATE area is empty there"},
        "2898": {"comment":"Keep the new start"},
        "2902": {"comment":"EXOS 30 loads the module at DE"},
        "2905": {"comment":"Code above it starts here now"},
        "2909": {"comment":"Header +4: initialisation offset"},
        "2912": {"comment":"$FFFF: no initialisation?"},
        "2915": {"comment":"HL = the routine's address"},
        "2916": {"comment":"Call it"},
        "2920": {"comment":"Reselect the program in use before"},
        "2923": {"comment":"The next module"},
        "2926": {"synopsis":"Reads a program module's body into the current program: clears it, ensures header +2/+3\nbytes are free, reads them to ($021A) (EXOS 6) and resets the run state. On a read error\nevery program is deleted and the error raised.","comment":"Clear the current program"},
        "2929": {"comment":"Header +2: the program's length"},
        "2934": {"comment":"Room for it?"},
        "2938": {"comment":"Read to the program's start"},
        "2945": {"comment":"Read the program"},
        "2947": {"comment":"Read: reset the run state, return"},
        "2951": {"comment":"Error: delete every program"},
        "2955": {"comment":"Raise the EXOS error"},
        "2956": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL: a CALL here calls the routine at HL."},
        "2957": {"synopsis":"MERGE [#n:] [\"name\"]: opens the file, reads its header (type 4 only, else error 20080; byte\n+5 kept as auto-start flag), then reads the program line by line and enters each line,\nreplacing a line with the same number.","comment":"Open the file; channel on the stack"},
        "2960": {"comment":"Read the module header"},
        "2963": {"comment":"Read errors raised"},
        "2964": {"comment":"Header +5: run after loading"},
        "2970": {"comment":"One BASIC program (type 4)?"},
        "2976": {"synopsis":"MERGE loop: reads a line's length byte (STOP key checked); length 0 ends the program, else\nreads the line into the buffer at $0248 and moves it into the program, removing an older\nline of that number first.","comment":"The file's channel"},
        "2978": {"comment":"B = the line's length byte"},
        "2981": {"comment":"STOP key pressed?"},
        "2985": {"comment":"Yes: error $E5 (9229, \"STOP key pressed\")"},
        "2988": {"comment":"Into the line buffer"},
        "2994": {"comment":"BC = the line's length"},
        "2997": {"comment":"Length 0: the program's end"},
        "3004": {"comment":"The rest of the line"},
        "3005": {"comment":"Read it to $0249"},
        "3008": {"comment":"The line's number"},
        "3011": {"comment":"Is there such a line?"},
        "3015": {"comment":"Found: remove it"},
        "3020": {"comment":"Open a gap of the line's size"},
        "3023": {"comment":"DE = the gap"},
        "3024": {"comment":"Copy the line in"},
        "3029": {"comment":"Next line"},
        "3031": {"synopsis":"VERIFY [#n:] [\"name\"]: opens the file and compares it with the programs in memory: a type 4\nmodule with the current program, a type 3 file program by program (each must exist). Any\ndifference is error 20081, \"Programs do not VERIFY\".","comment":"Open the file; channel on the stack"},
        "3034": {"comment":"Read the module header"},
        "3037": {"comment":"Read: check its type"},
        "3039": {"comment":"$E4 .EOF: an empty file"},
        "3041": {"comment":"Other read errors raised"},
        "3042": {"synopsis":"Raises error 20081, \"Programs do not VERIFY\" (run).","comment":"Error 20081, \"Programs do not VERIFY\""},
        "3045": {"synopsis":"VERIFY: type 4 compares the current program; type 3 goes on header by header; another type\nis error 20080.","comment":"Header +1: module type"},
        "3046": {"comment":"One program?"},
        "3050": {"comment":"All programs?"},
        "3052": {"synopsis":"VERIFY: error 20080 when NZ (a type it cannot compare).","comment":"Error 20080, \"Invalid file format\""},
        "3055": {"synopsis":"VERIFY, a multi-program file: reads the next header; end of file (.EOF or a type 10 header)\ncloses, a type 4 module is compared with the program numbered in header +4.","comment":"Next module header"},
        "3058": {"comment":"$E4 .EOF: done"},
        "3062": {"comment":"Other read errors raised"},
        "3064": {"comment":"Type 10: end of file?"},
        "3069": {"comment":"A program (type 4)?"},
        "3073": {"comment":"Header +4: the program's number"},
        "3077": {"comment":"Program 0 always exists"},
        "3080": {"comment":"Its segment (segment 1's SEG_TAG_FIND)"},
        "3083": {"comment":"No such program: they differ"},
        "3085": {"synopsis":"VERIFY: selects program C and compares it, then reads the next header.","comment":"Select program C"},
        "3088": {"comment":"Compare it"},
        "3093": {"synopsis":"VERIFY, a type 4 module: compares the current program, then closes the file.","comment":"Compare the current program"},
        "3096": {"synopsis":"VERIFY: closes the file through LOAD_CLOSE."},
        "3099": {"synopsis":"Compares the current program byte by byte with the next header +2/+3 bytes of channel\n($0209); error 20081 on a difference or when the module does not end where the program does.","comment":"Recompute nesting depths, as SAVE did"},
        "3102": {"comment":"From the program's start"},
        "3105": {"comment":"Header +2: the length to compare"},
        "3109": {"synopsis":"VERIFY loop: reads one byte and compares it with the next program byte."},
        "3110": {"comment":"Read a byte to B"},
        "3115": {"comment":"EXOS error raised"},
        "3118": {"comment":"Same as the program byte? (HL+1, BC-1)"},
        "3120": {"comment":"No: they differ"},
        "3122": {"comment":"More bytes?"},
        "3125": {"comment":"Keep where the comparison ended"},
        "3126": {"comment":"HL = the program's end"},
        "3131": {"comment":"Ended at the same place?"},
        "3133": {"comment":"No: they differ"},
        "3136": {"synopsis":"Reads a module header from channel ($0209): one byte (EXOS 5, not checked), then the 15\nbytes to $0DBC (EXOS 6, errors raised).\nExit: Z with DE = $0DBC (the type byte); NZ with A = the status when the first read failed."},
        "3139": {"comment":"Keep the channel"},
        "3140": {"comment":"The header's first byte"},
        "3142": {"comment":"Error (.EOF at the end): return it"},
        "3143": {"comment":"Type byte onwards"},
        "3147": {"comment":"The other 15 bytes"},
        "3151": {"comment":"Read them"},
        "3156": {"synopsis":"Opens the file a LOAD-type statement names: [#n:] and an optional name string (default\nchannel $6A, the empty name if none), with EXOS 1 (errors raised).\nExit: the channel's AF is left on the stack under the return address, for the caller to pop.","comment":"Default channel $6A"},
        "3158": {"comment":"#n and file name"},
        "3161": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "3162": {"comment":"Leave the channel on the stack"},
        "3164": {"comment":"Open channel A on name DE"},
        "3168": {"synopsis":"Reads an optional \"#n\" (symbol $03), followed by \":\" or the line's end.\nExit: Z with ($0209) = n and B = the channel in use before; NZ (no \"#\") with A = B =\n($0209). Error 7001 \"Invalid channel number\" for n over 255.","comment":"Current symbol \"#\" ($03)?"},
        "3173": {"comment":"Return the channel in use"},
        "3178": {"comment":"Next token, then HL = the channel number"},
        "3182": {"comment":"Over 255?"},
        "3183": {"comment":"Error 7001, \"Invalid channel number\""},
        "3186": {"comment":"Followed by \":\" ($10)?"},
        "3191": {"comment":"No: must be the line's end"},
        "3194": {"comment":"Past the \":\""},
        "3197": {"comment":"B = the channel in use before"},
        "3200": {"comment":"The new output channel"},
        "3204": {"comment":"Z: a channel was given"},
        "3206": {"synopsis":"Reads \"[#n:] [name]\": the channel (default A) into ($0209), then, when the token starts a\nstring, evaluates it as the file name.\nEntry: A = default channel.\nExit: A = the channel, B = the channel in use before, DE = the counted name (the empty one\nat EMPTY_STRING when none); Z when a name was given (it is on the value stack).","comment":"C = the default channel"},
        "3207": {"comment":"\"#n\" given?"},
        "3212": {"comment":"No: the default channel"},
        "3216": {"synopsis":"Branch: evaluates the file name when the token starts a string.","comment":"Keep the old channel (B)"},
        "3217": {"comment":"Keep the channel (A)"},
        "3218": {"comment":"A string name or literal next?"},
        "3221": {"comment":"No: the empty name"},
        "3226": {"comment":"Evaluate the name string"},
        "3229": {"comment":"DE = its length byte"},
        "3234": {"comment":"Z: a name was given"},
        "3235": {"synopsis":"Branch: returns A = the channel and B = the old channel; flags kept.","comment":"B = the channel pushed as A"},
        "3239": {"synopsis":"NEW [ALL]: without ALL deletes the current program and releases the ALLOCATE area; NEW ALL\ndeletes every program (error 20000 when something else follows).","comment":"Nothing after NEW?"},
        "3244": {"comment":"Yes: clear the current program"},
        "3246": {"comment":"The word ALL"},
        "3249": {"comment":"Error 20000 if it is not ALL"},
        "3252": {"comment":"Must end the line"},
        "3255": {"synopsis":"Deletes every program: each program 127 down to 1 that has a segment is selected and\ncleared, then program 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Program numbers from 127 down"},
        "3257": {"synopsis":"Loop: clears program C when its segment exists."},
        "3258": {"comment":"Segment tagged C? (segment 1's SEG_TAG_FIND)"},
        "3261": {"comment":"Yes: select and clear it"},
        "3265": {"comment":"Down to 1"},
        "3268": {"synopsis":"Selects program C and clears it (falls into PROG_CLEAR).","comment":"Select program C"},
        "3271": {"synopsis":"Clears the current program (a 0 at its start), then does CODE_AREA_FREE.","comment":"The program's start"},
        "3274": {"comment":"End mark: no lines"},
        "3276": {"synopsis":"Releases the ALLOCATE area: moves program 0 down to ($021E) and sets ($021C) = ($0220) =\n($021E); then reselects the program that was current.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Keep the current program's number"},
        "3280": {"comment":"Select program 0"},
        "3283": {"comment":"Base of the ALLOCATE area"},
        "3286": {"comment":"Next CODE byte goes there"},
        "3289": {"comment":"ALLOCATE area ends there too"},
        "3293": {"comment":"Program 0's start"},
        "3297": {"comment":"Size of the area"},
        "3302": {"comment":"Nothing allocated?"},
        "3304": {"comment":"DE = the program's end"},
        "3307": {"comment":"Move program 0 down"},
        "3310": {"synopsis":"Branch: program 0 now starts at HL; reselects the program kept on the stack.","comment":"Program 0's new start"},
        "3313": {"comment":"Its first line is the current one"},
        "3317": {"comment":"Reselect the program kept"},
        "3320": {"synopsis":"ALLOCATE n: makes the ALLOCATE area n bytes longer by moving program 0 up (error 5120\n\"Insufficient ALLOCATE space\" past $3FFF), adjusting ($0216)/($0214) when program 0 is the\none running, then rescans the programs' definitions (LINES_SCAN_DEFS) with the token state\nkept.","comment":"Keep the current program's number"},
        "3324": {"comment":"HL = the byte count"},
        "3328": {"comment":"Select program 0"},
        "3331": {"comment":"BC = the byte count"},
        "3332": {"comment":"End of the ALLOCATE area"},
        "3336": {"comment":"Past 64K?"},
        "3337": {"comment":"Error 5120, \"Insufficient ALLOCATE space\""},
        "3340": {"comment":"Past $3FFF?"},
        "3347": {"comment":"Move program 0 up by BC"},
        "3350": {"comment":"E = the program in use"},
        "3352": {"comment":"Program 0 in use?"},
        "3354": {"comment":"The area's new end"},
        "3355": {"comment":"Program 0's new start"},
        "3361": {"comment":"The current line"},
        "3364": {"comment":"The read pointer"},
        "3368": {"comment":"Not program 0: no change"},
        "3370": {"comment":"Not running: no change"},
        "3376": {"comment":"The running line moved by BC"},
        "3378": {"comment":"The read pointer too"},
        "3380": {"synopsis":"ALLOCATE: reselects the program in use and rescans its definitions, keeping ($0204), ($0214)\nand ($0216).","comment":"C = the program in use"},
        "3383": {"comment":"Reselect it"},
        "3386": {"comment":"Keep the current symbol"},
        "3390": {"comment":"Rescan the definitions (LINES_SCAN_DEFS)"},
        "3406": {"synopsis":"CONTINUE: clears the STOP request; in a running program (a handler) goes on at SCOPE_POP\nwith\ncarry clear; at the prompt it needs bit 3 of ($0200) (a program was stopped), else error\n20020 \"CONTINUE not possible\", and clears bit 5 before ending as STMT_NEXT_LINE.","comment":"Clear the STOP request"},
        "3410": {"comment":"Carry clear for SCOPE_POP"},
        "3411": {"comment":"Program running?"},
        "3418": {"comment":"Can the stopped program go on?"},
        "3422": {"comment":"No: error 20020, \"CONTINUE not possible\""},
        "3425": {"comment":"Clear bit 5 (tested at $03C6)"},
        "3432": {"synopsis":"Runs the program from line ($0216): sets bit 1 of ($0200) (running), keeps ($023A) and\nstores SP there, then runs line after line; returns at the program's end (a 0 length) or\nwhen a statement leaves ($0206) = 4 or more, with ($023A) restored.\n1. Each line: STOP key request (error 9229), the TRACE output \"<n>\" when bit 4 of ($0200) is\n   set.\n2. The line's keyword (+5) is run through EFE7 with ($0206) = 0.\n3. ($0206) then says what follows: 0 the next statement after \":\" or the line's end, 1 the\n   line's end, 2 the next line, 3 the line now in ($0216).","comment":"Running a program"},
        "3436": {"comment":"The outer run's SP"},
        "3440": {"comment":"SP to come back to"},
        "3444": {"synopsis":"Run loop: resumes with SP from ($023A); the error code at $F429 jumps here.","comment":"Back to the saved SP"},
        "3448": {"synopsis":"Run loop: the line at ($0216): its length byte; 0 is the program's end.","comment":"The line to run"},
        "3451": {"comment":"Its length byte"},
        "3453": {"comment":"End of the program?"},
        "3456": {"synopsis":"Run loop: back to the saved SP, restores the outer ($023A) and returns.","comment":"Back to the saved SP"},
        "3460": {"comment":"The outer run's SP"},
        "3465": {"synopsis":"Run loop, a line: checks the STOP request, prints the TRACE mark when on, then runs the\nline's keyword.","comment":"STOP key pressed?"},
        "3472": {"comment":"Keep line+1"},
        "3473": {"comment":"TRACE on?"},
        "3479": {"comment":"The TRACE channel"},
        "3485": {"comment":"A 0 byte: does the channel exist?"},
        "3489": {"comment":"$FB .ICHAN: not open?"},
        "3491": {"comment":"Error 7401, \"TRACE channel not open\""},
        "3494": {"comment":"\"<\""},
        "3499": {"comment":"No padding"},
        "3500": {"comment":"Print the line number"},
        "3503": {"comment":"\">\""},
        "3508": {"synopsis":"Run loop: C = the line's keyword (byte +5); the read pointer goes after it.","comment":"Line+1"},
        "3512": {"comment":"Line+5: the keyword's number"},
        "3515": {"comment":"Read from line+6 on"},
        "3518": {"synopsis":"Run loop: reads the statement's first token, clears ($0206) and runs keyword C; then acts on\n($0206).","comment":"First token after the keyword"},
        "3521": {"comment":"Default: the next statement"},
        "3525": {"comment":"Run keyword C's handler"},
        "3528": {"comment":"What next?"},
        "3531": {"comment":"0: another statement or the line's end"},
        "3535": {"comment":"1: check the line's end"},
        "3538": {"comment":"2: the next line"},
        "3541": {"comment":"3: the line now in ($0216)"},
        "3543": {"comment":"4 and up: stop running"},
        "3549": {"synopsis":"Run loop: a \":\" ($10) brings another statement on the same line (C = its keyword number from\n($0203)); anything else must be the line's end.","comment":"\":\" next?"},
        "3556": {"comment":"The keyword after it"},
        "3559": {"comment":"C = its number"},
        "3564": {"synopsis":"Run loop: error 20000 unless the line's end follows.","comment":"Must be the line's end"},
        "3567": {"synopsis":"Run loop: ($0216) moves to the next line.","comment":"The current line"},
        "3570": {"comment":"Past it by its length"},
        "3577": {"synopsis":"Run loop: runs the line in ($0216)."},
        "3580": {"synopsis":"Raises error 9229, \"STOP key pressed\" (run).","comment":"Error 9229, \"STOP key pressed\""},
        "3584": {"synopsis":"Prints the counted text that follows the CALL to this routine (with PRINT_COUNTED) and\nreturns after it.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"HL = the text after the CALL"},
        "3585": {"comment":"Print it (PRINT_COUNTED)"},
        "3588": {"comment":"Return past the text"},
        "3590": {"synopsis":"ASK option var / ASK n var: reads an EXOS variable (EXOS 16, B = 0) into a numeric variable.\nThe option word comes from the option table (segment 1's SETOPT_LOOKUP), and must name an\nEXOS variable; a number must be 1-255. Errors: 20060 \"Invalid machine option use\", 20030\n\"Identifier expected\", 1000 for a number over 255.","comment":"An option word? (segment 1's SETOPT_LOOKUP)"},
        "3593": {"comment":"Bit 7: an EXOS variable option?"},
        "3595": {"comment":"C = the variable's number"},
        "3597": {"comment":"Found the word"},
        "3599": {"comment":"No word: A = the number (0-255)"},
        "3603": {"comment":"Z when 0"},
        "3604": {"synopsis":"ASK: error 20060 when Z (variable 0, or an option that is not an EXOS variable); then\nexpects a numeric variable.","comment":"Error 20060, \"Invalid machine option use\""},
        "3607": {"comment":"Word given: past it"},
        "3610": {"comment":"A numeric name next?"},
        "3613": {"comment":"No: error 20030, \"Identifier expected\""},
        "3616": {"comment":"B = 0: read the variable"},
        "3618": {"comment":"EXOS 16; D = its value"},
        "3620": {"comment":"EXOS error raised"},
        "3621": {"comment":"Keep the value"},
        "3622": {"comment":"HL = the variable's value field"},
        "3625": {"comment":"Value to HL"},
        "3626": {"comment":"HL = the value, 0-255"},
        "3629": {"comment":"Push it (NUM_PUSH_INT)"},
        "3633": {"comment":"Store it in the variable (NUM_POP_VAR)"},
        "3636": {"synopsis":"CALL name[(args)]: evaluates the call as an expression (B = 3, through EXPR_OR_LEVEL) and\nputs the\nvalue stack back to the depth it had, dropping any result. Error 20034 \"Type mismatch\" when\na string comes first.","comment":"A string?"},
        "3639": {"comment":"Error 20034, \"Type mismatch\""},
        "3642": {"comment":"The stack's bottom"},
        "3649": {"comment":"Depth below the bottom"},
        "3653": {"comment":"Compute; bit 1 kept"},
        "3655": {"comment":"Run the call as an expression"},
        "3659": {"comment":"Back to the depth kept"},
        "3667": {"synopsis":"CAPTURE: reads its two channel numbers (through PARSE_FROM_TO) and asks EXOS 17 (capture\nchannel) to\ntake the first's input from the second; EXOS errors raised.","comment":"B, C = the channels from the arguments"},
        "3670": {"comment":"A = the channel to capture"},
        "3671": {"comment":"C = the channel it reads from"},
        "3672": {"comment":"EXOS 17 captures the channel"},
        "3676": {"synopsis":"CAUSE [EXCEPTION] n: raises error n.","comment":"The word EXCEPTION"},
        "3679": {"comment":"Given?"},
        "3682": {"comment":"Yes: past it"},
        "3685": {"comment":"HL = n"},
        "3688": {"comment":"Raise error n"},
        "3689": {"synopsis":"Expects symbol $03 (\"#\"), then evaluates an expression to A = 0-255; error 20000 without the\n\"#\", 7001 \"Invalid channel number\" when the value is larger.\nExit: A = L = the value.","comment":"Symbol \"#\" must come"},
        "3694": {"comment":"HL = the value"},
        "3697": {"comment":"Over 255?"},
        "3699": {"comment":"Error 7001, \"Invalid channel number\""},
        "3704": {"synopsis":"START, RUN [line | \"name\"] [(args)] and, from $0EAC, CHAIN: starts a program.\n1. START enters here (carry clear when no program is in memory, then the file is loaded from\n   channel $6A first); RUN enters at $0E7E, inside the OR, with carry set.\n2. RUN line starts at that line (error 20004 when it does not exist); RUN \"name\" loads the\n   file and runs it.\n3. Arguments in brackets are evaluated (ARGS_EVAL_REV) and kept at $0595 while the program\n   is reset; they are then assigned to the parameters of a first line PROGRAM \"name\"(p1,\n   ...) (error 4301 \"Error in CHAIN parameters\" for a wrong type).\n4. Run state is reset (OPTION ANGLE, channel 0, the random generator) and RUN_LOOP runs the\n   program; when it returns, the prompt loop at BASIC_READY takes over.","comment":"Carry: no program in memory"},
        "3707": {"comment":"Some program: carry"},
        "3709": {"comment":"None: NC (RUN enters at +1: SCF)"},
        "3711": {"comment":"Keep the carry"},
        "3712": {"comment":"Clear the STOP request"},
        "3716": {"comment":"Release the ALLOCATE area at the start"},
        "3720": {"comment":"Run the program in use"},
        "3727": {"comment":"Start line: the first"},
        "3730": {"comment":"START with nothing in memory: load"},
        "3732": {"comment":"RUN with a line number?"},
        "3739": {"comment":"RUN \"name\"?"},
        "3744": {"comment":"Class $03 cannot occur: always on"},
        "3748": {"synopsis":"START/RUN \"name\": opens the file (channel $6A) and has it loaded before running.","comment":"Start line 0"},
        "3749": {"comment":"Open the file; channel on the stack"},
        "3752": {"comment":"A = the channel"},
        "3753": {"comment":"Carry: load the file"},
        "3756": {"synopsis":"CHAIN n / CHAIN \"name\": PROG_ARG_READ reads which program to run into ($0212) (or its name\nto\n$0E34); the ALLOCATE area is kept; then on as RUN from the start.","comment":"The program to run"},
        "3759": {"comment":"Keep the ALLOCATE area"},
        "3763": {"synopsis":"RUN: from the program's first line.","comment":"Start line 0; no file to load"},
        "3768": {"synopsis":"RUN n: finds line n (error 20004 \"Line number does not exist\").","comment":"Find the line"},
        "3771": {"comment":"Error 20004, \"Line number does not exist\""},
        "3774": {"comment":"Past the number"},
        "3777": {"synopsis":"RUN: keeps the start line (HL) and the load flag (carry), empties the value stack and reads\nthe bracketed arguments.","comment":"The start line"},
        "3778": {"synopsis":"RUN: keeps AF (carry: load a file, channel A), empties the value stack and reads the\narguments.","comment":"Load flag and channel"},
        "3779": {"comment":"Empty the value stack"},
        "3785": {"comment":"\"(\" next: arguments?"},
        "3792": {"comment":"Evaluate them, last first"},
        "3795": {"comment":"Z: no end check"},
        "3796": {"synopsis":"RUN: checks the line's end, copies the arguments on the value stack to below $0595, loads\nthe file when asked, resets the program areas and copies the arguments back.","comment":"Must be the line's end"},
        "3799": {"comment":"The arguments' size"},
        "3809": {"comment":"256 bytes or more?"},
        "3811": {"comment":"Error 5000, \"Insufficient memory\""},
        "3816": {"comment":"BC = the size + 1"},
        "3817": {"comment":"HL = the stack's bottom byte"},
        "3818": {"comment":"Copied to end at $0595"},
        "3821": {"comment":"Load flag and channel"},
        "3824": {"comment":"Keep the arguments"},
        "3826": {"comment":"The file's channel"},
        "3829": {"comment":"Load it (LOAD_MODULE_A)"},
        "3832": {"comment":"RUN or START?"},
        "3836": {"comment":"Yes: release the ALLOCATE area"},
        "3839": {"comment":"Select the program to run"},
        "3842": {"comment":"Rescan the definitions (LINES_SCAN_DEFS)"},
        "3845": {"comment":"DE = the size + 1"},
        "3847": {"comment":"Room for the arguments?"},
        "3851": {"comment":"Back to the stack's bottom"},
        "3855": {"comment":"From the copy at $0595"},
        "3858": {"comment":"The top item"},
        "3863": {"comment":"First line PROGRAM \"name\"?"},
        "3866": {"comment":"No: no parameters"},
        "3868": {"comment":"Token after the name"},
        "3871": {"comment":"\"(\": parameters?"},
        "3878": {"synopsis":"RUN, parameters: reads the next parameter name (\")\" ends the list), makes its variable and\ngives it the next argument.","comment":"Next token"},
        "3881": {"comment":"\")\": the list ends"},
        "3888": {"comment":"Make the variable; HL = its name"},
        "3891": {"comment":"HL = its value field"},
        "3893": {"comment":"Z: a string parameter"},
        "3894": {"comment":"Numeric: set to 0"},
        "3896": {"comment":"String: past the maximum length"},
        "3897": {"comment":"Length 0: empty"},
        "3900": {"synopsis":"RUN, a numeric parameter: set to 0 before its argument is taken."},
        "3901": {"comment":"Push something (NUM_PUSH_INT)"},
        "3904": {"comment":"Make it 0"},
        "3908": {"comment":"Store it (NUM_POP_VAR)"},
        "3911": {"synopsis":"RUN: looks at the top argument's type; none left (type 0) leaves the parameter as it is.","comment":"String or numeric parameter"},
        "3912": {"comment":"Top argument's type"},
        "3916": {"comment":"HL = the value field"},
        "3917": {"comment":"Numeric parameter?"},
        "3919": {"comment":"No argument left?"},
        "3922": {"comment":"A string argument?"},
        "3926": {"comment":"Store it (STR_POP_VAR)"},
        "3929": {"comment":"Done"},
        "3930": {"synopsis":"RUN, a numeric parameter: no argument left leaves it at 0.","comment":"No argument left?"},
        "3933": {"comment":"A number?"},
        "3935": {"synopsis":"RUN: error 4301 \"Error in CHAIN parameters\" when NZ (the argument's type does not fit), else\nstores the number.","comment":"Error 4301, \"Error in CHAIN parameters\""},
        "3938": {"comment":"Store it (NUM_POP_VAR)"},
        "3941": {"synopsis":"RUN: \",\" brings the next parameter; else \")\" must end the list.","comment":"Next token"},
        "3944": {"comment":"\",\": another parameter?"},
        "3951": {"comment":"Must be \")\""},
        "3956": {"synopsis":"RUN: recomputes the nesting depths, resets the run state (radians, channel 0, ($0205), the\nrandom generator), sets bit 3 of ($0200) (CONTINUE allowed), sets the start line, empties\nthe value stack and runs RUN_LOOP from SP = $0DBB; afterwards ends as STMT_END does.","comment":"Recompute nesting depths (segment 1's LINES_REINDENT)"},
        "3959": {"comment":"The program's first line"},
        "3965": {"comment":"OPTION ANGLE RADIANS"},
        "3969": {"comment":"Output to channel 0"},
        "3973": {"comment":"No key read"},
        "3976": {"comment":"Reset the random generator's state"},
        "3983": {"comment":"CONTINUE allowed"},
        "3987": {"comment":"The start line"},
        "3990": {"comment":"0: the first line"},
        "3995": {"synopsis":"RUN: ($0216) = the start line, empty value stack, then runs the program.","comment":"The line to start at"},
        "3998": {"comment":"Empty the value stack"},
        "4004": {"comment":"Fresh machine stack"},
        "4007": {"comment":"Run the program"},
        "4010": {"comment":"Ended: ($0206) = 2"},
        "4013": {"synopsis":"END (and the end of RUN): clears bit 3 of ($0200) (no CONTINUE) and goes back to the prompt\nloop at BASIC_READY.","comment":"No CONTINUE"},
        "4017": {"comment":"Back to the prompt loop"},
        "4020": {"synopsis":"Skips one argument (string or numeric, B = 0: parsed only), then: the line's end is error\n20000, \")\" ends the list (next token, then the line's end must follow), else (\",\") the rest\nis evaluated through ARGS_EVAL_REV.","comment":"Parse only"},
        "4022": {"comment":"A string?"},
        "4027": {"comment":"Skip a string expression"},
        "4030": {"comment":"Z: done"},
        "4031": {"synopsis":"Branch: skips a numeric expression when NZ, then checks what follows the argument.","comment":"Skip a numeric expression"},
        "4034": {"comment":"Line's end too soon?"},
        "4039": {"comment":"Error 20000, \"Not understood\""},
        "4042": {"comment":"\")\": the last argument?"},
        "4044": {"comment":"Past it; then the line's end"},
        "4047": {"synopsis":"Evaluates a bracketed argument list from its last argument to its first: each argument is\nskipped, the rest is done by recursion (ARGS_SKIP_ONE), then the read pointer goes back and\nthe argument is evaluated; the first argument ends on top of the value stack.","comment":"Where this argument starts"},
        "4051": {"comment":"Its first token"},
        "4054": {"comment":"Skip it; do the rest first"},
        "4057": {"comment":"Back to this argument"},
        "4061": {"comment":"Its first token again"},
        "4064": {"comment":"A string?"},
        "4067": {"comment":"Evaluate it (string or numeric)"},
        "4070": {"synopsis":"CLOSE #n: closes channel n (EXOS 3); error 7004 \"Channel not open\" when EXOS reports an\nerror.","comment":"A = the channel"},
        "4073": {"comment":"Close it"},
        "4075": {"comment":"Closed: done"},
        "4076": {"comment":"Error 7004, \"Channel not open\""},
        "4080": {"synopsis":"CODE [var] = string: when a numeric variable comes first it is set to the current CODE\naddress ($021C); then the string's bytes are copied there and ($021C) moves past them. The\nspace is not checked.","comment":"A numeric name first?"},
        "4083": {"comment":"No: straight to \"=\""},
        "4085": {"comment":"The next CODE address"},
        "4088": {"comment":"Push it (NUM_PUSH_INT)"},
        "4091": {"comment":"HL = the variable's value field"},
        "4094": {"comment":"Store it (NUM_POP_VAR)"},
        "4097": {"synopsis":"CODE statement, the bytes (CODE's routine at $0FF0 falls in here, or jumps here when no\nnumeric name leads): \"=\" and a string expression must follow; the string's bytes are copied\nto the code pointer ($021C), which moves past them, and the string is dropped.\nErrors: 20000 without \"=\".","comment":"Symbol $13 \"=\" must follow (error 20000)"},
        "4102": {"comment":"EVAL_STRING: the bytes to store"},
        "4105": {"comment":"HL = the string's length byte"},
        "4109": {"comment":"DE = the code pointer ($021C)"},
        "4113": {"comment":"Length 0?"},
        "4118": {"comment":"Past the length byte"},
        "4119": {"comment":"Copy the string's bytes to the code area"},
        "4123": {"comment":"Code pointer past them"},
        "4127": {"synopsis":"An empty string: nothing copied, the string is dropped (ITEM_DROP).","comment":"ITEM_DROP: the string"},
        "4130": {"synopsis":"COPY statement (keyword table entry): copies characters from one channel to another until\nthe source ends.\n1. Sets FLG_EDIT (EXOS variable 32) to $C0, SEND NOW and SEND ALL, so the editor channel\n   gives its whole text and then .EOF.\n2. Reads FROM #n and TO #m (PARSE_FROM_TO): B = the source (0 by default), C = the\n   destination (104\n   by default).\n3. Copies character by character with EXOS 5 and 7 until .EOF ($E4).\nErrors: 9229 when STOP is pressed; other EXOS errors as 9000 + code.","comment":"FLG_EDIT = $C0: SEND NOW and SEND ALL"},
        "4132": {"comment":"B = 1 write, C = 32 FLG_EDIT"},
        "4137": {"comment":"B = FROM channel (0), C = TO channel (104)"},
        "4140": {"comment":"H = source, L = destination"},
        "4142": {"synopsis":"COPY's loop: one character from channel H to channel L per pass.","comment":"Read a character from the source"},
        "4145": {"comment":"Got one?"},
        "4147": {"comment":".EOF: the text has ended"},
        "4150": {"comment":"Other EXOS errors: error 9000 + A"},
        "4151": {"synopsis":"A character was read: stops on a STOP request (bit 2 of ($0200)), else writes it.","comment":"STOP pressed?"},
        "4155": {"comment":"Error 9229: STOP key pressed"},
        "4158": {"comment":"Write it to the destination"},
        "4161": {"comment":"EXOS error: 9000 + A"},
        "4164": {"synopsis":"Syntax check (keyword table, second word) of CLEAR, DISPLAY, ENVELOPE, PLOT, SET, SOUND,\nTRACE and GET: a leading \"#\" channel expression is skipped and must be followed by \":\" or by\none more token ending the line; the rest of the statement is skipped.\nErrors: 20000.","comment":"The token after the keyword"},
        "4167": {"comment":"A \"#\" channel?"},
        "4171": {"comment":"Skip the channel expression (not computed)"},
        "4174": {"comment":"\":\" after it?"},
        "4181": {"comment":"Else one more token, which must end the line"},
        "4186": {"synopsis":"Syntax check (keyword table, second word) of GOTO and GOSUB: reads the token after the\nkeyword and, when it is a line number, retypes it $A2 (a line reference); no line number is\nerror 20000 \"Not understood\".","comment":"Mark the line number token as a line reference"},
        "4189": {"comment":"Done when there was a line number"},
        "4190": {"comment":"Error 20000: Not understood"},
        "4193": {"synopsis":"Syntax check (keyword table, second word) of most statements: reads the next token and skips\nthe rest of the statement (it falls into STMT_SKIP).","comment":"Next token"},
        "4196": {"comment":"Carry: no bracket skip on this pass"},
        "4197": {"synopsis":"STMT_SKIP's branch: skips a bracketed group with ARGS_SKIP_PARENS.","comment":"ARGS_SKIP_PARENS: past a bracketed group"},
        "4200": {"synopsis":"Call byte $3D: skips tokens, and bracketed groups as a whole, up to the statement's end:\nsymbol $10 \":\" or the line's end (0 or 1).\nEntry: the current token read.\nExit: ($0204) = $10, 0 or 1.","comment":"The current symbol"},
        "4203": {"comment":"\":\"? The statement ends here"},
        "4206": {"comment":"Line end (0 or 1)?"},
        "4209": {"comment":"\"(\"?"},
        "4215": {"synopsis":"TIME statement (keyword table entry): runs segment 1's STMT_TIME through a call list.","comment":"Segment 1's STMT_TIME (call byte $C2)"},
        "4219": {"synopsis":"DATE statement (keyword table entry): runs segment 1's STMT_DATE through a call list.","comment":"Segment 1's STMT_DATE (call byte $C3)"},
        "4223": {"synopsis":"Syntax check (keyword table, second word) of DEF: the name, an optional parameter list \"(\n... )\", then either the line's end, which turns the line's keyword byte ($024D) into $0E,\nthe DEF of a block, or \"=\" (a one-line function; the expression is left to the caller).\nErrors: 20000.","comment":"The routine's name"},
        "4226": {"comment":"The token after it"},
        "4229": {"comment":"\"(\": a parameter list?"},
        "4233": {"synopsis":"CHK_DEF's loop: tokens up to \")\" or the line's end.","comment":"Next token"},
        "4236": {"comment":"\")\"?"},
        "4238": {"comment":"Line end?"},
        "4244": {"synopsis":"The parameter list must close with \")\" (error 20000).","comment":"\")\" must close it (error 20000)"},
        "4249": {"synopsis":"After the name (and parameters): the line's end makes a block DEF, anything else must be\n\"=\".","comment":"Line end after the name?"},
        "4251": {"comment":"Else \"=\" must follow (error 20000)"},
        "4256": {"comment":"Keyword $0E: the block form of DEF"},
        "4258": {"comment":"Into the stored line's keyword byte"},
        "4262": {"synopsis":"Syntax check (keyword table, second word) of END: plain END needs nothing more. END followed\nby a word looks it up in END_WORDS: the line's keyword byte ($024D) becomes the two-word\nkeyword (END IF, END SELECT, END DEF, END WHEN or END HANDLER), the second word's token is\nremoved from the line buffer (LINEBUF_RESIZE), and the line must end there.\nErrors: 20000 for any other word or anything after it.","comment":"The word after END"},
        "4265": {"comment":"Plain END: nothing more to check"},
        "4266": {"comment":"The table of second words"},
        "4269": {"synopsis":"CHK_END's search: one row of END_WORDS per pass.","comment":"DE = the word's counted text"},
        "4273": {"comment":"The table's end?"},
        "4275": {"comment":"Error 20000: Not understood"},
        "4280": {"comment":"Z when the current word is that text"},
        "4284": {"comment":"A = the two-word keyword's number"},
        "4286": {"comment":"Not this one: try the next row"},
        "4288": {"comment":"Into the stored line's keyword byte"},
        "4291": {"comment":"HL = the second word's token start"},
        "4295": {"comment":"LINEBUF_RESIZE: removes the second word's token"},
        "4298": {"comment":"The token after it"},
        "4301": {"comment":"Must end the line (error 20000)"},
        "4304": {"synopsis":"The second words of END, 3 bytes a row, read by CHK_END: the address of the word's text\n(length first, inside the keyword table) and the number of the two-word keyword it makes: IF\n$1A, SELECT $1B, DEF $18, WHEN $1C, HANDLER $19. A zero word ends it."},
        "4321": {"synopsis":"EXIT statement (keyword table entry): leaves a block.\n1. Sets mode 2 ($0206): execution goes on with the line after the current line ($0216).\n2. EXIT DO and EXIT FOR: the top stack item must be the DO item (type 5) or the FOR item\n   (type 4); the line address at its +3 becomes the current line and the item is dropped.\n3. EXIT DEF and EXIT HANDLER (($0207) = 2 for HANDLER): values are dropped and the call\n   frame (a type 7 item) is unwound at SCOPE_POP.\nErrors: 20000 for another word, 20051 when the item is not there.","comment":"Mode 2: continue with the next line"},
        "4324": {"comment":"EXIT DO?"},
        "4330": {"comment":"DO block item: type 5"},
        "4334": {"comment":"EXIT FOR?"},
        "4340": {"comment":"FOR block item: type 4"},
        "4344": {"comment":"EXIT DEF?"},
        "4352": {"comment":"EXIT HANDLER?"},
        "4358": {"comment":"Else error 20000: Not understood"},
        "4361": {"comment":"($0207) = 2 for EXIT HANDLER"},
        "4365": {"synopsis":"EXIT DEF / EXIT HANDLER: drops values and unwinds the type 7 item; with none on top, A = the\ntype - 7 fails the test below (error 20051).","comment":"Drop values: A = the top item's type"},
        "4368": {"comment":"A type 7 item (a call frame)?"},
        "4370": {"comment":"Unwind to it"},
        "4373": {"synopsis":"EXIT DO / EXIT FOR: the top item must have type A (error 20051); its +3 word becomes the\ncurrent line and the item is dropped.","comment":"Does the top item have the type wanted?"},
        "4377": {"comment":"Error 20051"},
        "4380": {"comment":"To the item's word +3"},
        "4383": {"comment":"The line address it holds"},
        "4387": {"comment":"Becomes the current line"},
        "4390": {"comment":"Drop the block item"},
        "4393": {"synopsis":"FLUSH statement (keyword table entry): FLUSH #n sends a channel's buffered data with EXOS\n11, special function 16 (@@FLSH, the network device's).\nErrors: 20000 without \"#n\"; EXOS errors as 9000 + code.","comment":"\"#n:\" must lead (Z)"},
        "4396": {"comment":"Error 20000 without it"},
        "4399": {"comment":"B: the channel to restore"},
        "4400": {"comment":"@@FLSH: send the buffered data"},
        "4404": {"comment":"EXOS error: 9000 + A"},
        "4405": {"comment":"($0209) back to B"},
        "4408": {"synopsis":"GET statement (keyword table entry): GET [#n:] name$ reads one character, if one is waiting,\nfrom channel n (105, the keyboard channel, by default) into the string variable (an empty\nstring when none is). It asks EXOS 9 first, so it never waits.\nErrors: 20031 \"String identifier expected\"; EXOS errors as 9000 + code.","comment":"Optional \"#n:\" (Z when given)"},
        "4411": {"comment":"B: the channel to restore"},
        "4412": {"comment":"Channel given: A = it"},
        "4414": {"comment":"Else channel 105 ($69)"},
        "4416": {"synopsis":"A = the channel to read: tests that a string name follows, then asks the channel's status."},
        "4417": {"comment":"A string name must follow"},
        "4422": {"comment":"Error 20031: String identifier expected"},
        "4427": {"comment":"Is a character waiting?"},
        "4429": {"comment":"EXOS error: 9000 + A"},
        "4431": {"comment":"B = 0: an empty string"},
        "4433": {"comment":"HL = the stack's top"},
        "4436": {"comment":"C = 0: a character is ready?"},
        "4440": {"comment":"B = the character"},
        "4442": {"comment":"EXOS error: 9000 + A"},
        "4443": {"comment":"It is the string's text"},
        "4445": {"comment":"Length 1"},
        "4447": {"synopsis":"Pushes the string item (type 3, length B, the character when B = 1) and stores it in the\nvariable.","comment":"The length byte"},
        "4449": {"comment":"Type 3: a string item"},
        "4452": {"comment":"The new top"},
        "4455": {"comment":"HL = the variable (array element)"},
        "4458": {"comment":"STR_POP_VAR: store it"},
        "4461": {"comment":"($0209) back to B"},
        "4464": {"synopsis":"Moves to the B-th line number of an ON list. Entered here with the token before the list\n(GOTO) current, or at LIST_PICK with the first number current.\nEntry: B = the item wanted (1 = the first).\nExit: NC with that number the current token; carry when the list ends first (B = 0 never\nmatches).","comment":"Next list item"},
        "4467": {"synopsis":"LIST_NEXT_ITEM's count: returns when B reaches 0, else steps over the \",\" (carry at the\nline's end).","comment":"Is this the item wanted?"},
        "4469": {"comment":"The token after it"},
        "4472": {"comment":"Line end: carry, no such item"},
        "4474": {"comment":"On to the next item"},
        "4476": {"synopsis":"Syntax check (keyword table, second word) of ON: skips the selector expression, then each\nline number of the list after GOTO or GOSUB is retyped $A2 (a line reference); the list ends\nthe line.\nErrors: 20000 for a missing number or anything after the list.","comment":"The token after ON"},
        "4479": {"comment":"SKIP_NUM_EXPR: the selector"},
        "4482": {"synopsis":"CHK_ON's loop: one line number per pass, separated by \",\".","comment":"The line number token"},
        "4485": {"comment":"Its value"},
        "4488": {"comment":"None (0)?"},
        "4490": {"comment":"Error 20000: Not understood"},
        "4493": {"comment":"IY = the read pointer"},
        "4497": {"comment":"Retype the number token $A2: a line reference"},
        "4501": {"comment":"The token after it"},
        "4504": {"comment":"\",\"? Another number follows"},
        "4508": {"comment":"Else the line must end (error 20000)"},
        "4511": {"synopsis":"ON statement (keyword table entry): ON n GOTO list or ON n GOSUB list. n (0-255, error 1000)\npicks the line number; when the list has no n-th item the statement does nothing. The GOSUB\nform goes on into KW_GOSUB, the GOTO form to ON_GOTO.\nErrors: 20000 when neither GOTO nor GOSUB follows.","comment":"A = the selector, 0-255 (error 1000)"},
        "4514": {"comment":"B counts the list items"},
        "4515": {"comment":"ON ... GOTO?"},
        "4523": {"comment":"Else GOSUB must follow (error 20000)"},
        "4529": {"comment":"Move to the B-th line number"},
        "4532": {"comment":"No such item: carry on with the next statement"},
        "4533": {"synopsis":"GOSUB statement (keyword table entry; ON ... GOSUB comes here too): finds line ($0218),\npushes a type 6 item (3 bytes) holding the address of the line after the current one, makes\nthe target the current line ($0216) and sets mode 3.\nErrors: 5000 for no memory, 20004 \"Line number does not exist\".","comment":"4 bytes for the return item"},
        "4536": {"comment":"MEM_ENSURE_DE"},
        "4539": {"comment":"Find line ($0218)"},
        "4542": {"comment":"Error 20004: Line number does not exist"},
        "4545": {"comment":"Keep the target line"},
        "4546": {"comment":"The current line"},
        "4549": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "4553": {"comment":"DE = the line after it: the return point"},
        "4554": {"comment":"HL = the stack's top"},
        "4557": {"comment":"Push the return line's address"},
        "4560": {"comment":"Type 6: a GOSUB return item"},
        "4563": {"comment":"The target becomes the current line"},
        "4566": {"synopsis":"Sets mode 3 ($0206): the statement loop goes on at the start of line ($0216).","comment":"Mode 3: continue at line ($0216)"},
        "4571": {"synopsis":"ON ... GOTO: moves to the n-th line number (none: return), then KW_GOTO.","comment":"Move to the B-th line number"},
        "4574": {"comment":"No such item: carry on"},
        "4575": {"synopsis":"GOTO statement (keyword table entry; IF ... THEN n and ON ... GOTO come here too): finds\nline ($0218) (error 20004 \"Line number does not exist\"), makes it the current line with mode\n3, then drops every FOR or DO block item (types 1-5) on top of the stack whose line span,\nthe words at +1 and +3, does not hold the target. A type 6 or higher item, or the stack's\nbottom, stops the walk.","comment":"Mode 3: continue at line ($0216)"},
        "4578": {"comment":"Find line ($0218)"},
        "4581": {"comment":"Error 20004: Line number does not exist"},
        "4584": {"comment":"The target becomes the current line"},
        "4588": {"synopsis":"KW_GOTO's loop: one stack item per pass, HL = the target line.","comment":"The top stack item"},
        "4591": {"comment":"A = its type"},
        "4593": {"comment":"BC = word +1: the block's first line"},
        "4597": {"comment":"DE = word +3: the block's last line"},
        "4601": {"comment":"The stack's bottom?"},
        "4603": {"comment":"A DO item (type 5)?"},
        "4607": {"comment":"Types 6 and above stop the unwinding"},
        "4608": {"comment":"Types 1-4: BC unchanged"},
        "4609": {"synopsis":"Is the target line in [BC, DE]? Yes: return; no: drop the item.","comment":"Type 5: BC + 1 (its first line excluded)"},
        "4611": {"comment":"Target before the block?"},
        "4616": {"comment":"DE + 1: the block's last line included"},
        "4617": {"comment":"Target inside the block?"},
        "4620": {"comment":"Yes: keep the item and stop"},
        "4621": {"synopsis":"The target is outside the block: its item is dropped (LEDF3) and the next one tested."},
        "4622": {"comment":"Drop the block item"},
        "4625": {"comment":"And look at the next one"},
        "4627": {"synopsis":"Syntax check (keyword table, second word) of IF: skips the condition, which THEN must\nfollow.\n1. Nothing after THEN: the IF keyword byte becomes $26, the IF of a block.\n2. A line number: it is retyped $A2 (a line reference).\n3. A statement: its keyword is tokenised and checked (STMT_TOKENISE), and must have bit 4 of\n   its\n   keyword flags (error 20073).\nErrors: 20000 without THEN.","comment":"The condition's start"},
        "4631": {"comment":"Skip the condition (not computed)"},
        "4634": {"comment":"THEN must follow"},
        "4640": {"comment":"Error 20000 without it"},
        "4643": {"comment":"HL = the text after THEN"},
        "4646": {"comment":"The token after THEN"},
        "4649": {"comment":"DE = the condition's start"},
        "4650": {"comment":"Something after THEN?"},
        "4652": {"comment":"Keyword $26: the block form of IF"},
        "4654": {"comment":"The IF keyword's number byte"},
        "4657": {"synopsis":"Something follows THEN: a line number or a statement.","comment":"DE = the text after THEN"},
        "4658": {"comment":"A line number after THEN?"},
        "4663": {"comment":"Yes: mark it as a line reference"},
        "4667": {"comment":"NC: tokenise the statement after THEN"},
        "4669": {"comment":"Tokenise its keyword and run its check"},
        "4673": {"comment":"Past the $60 byte"},
        "4674": {"comment":"C = the keyword's number"},
        "4675": {"comment":"KEYWORD_FLAGS: HL = its flags byte"},
        "4678": {"comment":"Bit 4: allowed after THEN?"},
        "4681": {"comment":"Error 20073"},
        "4685": {"synopsis":"IF statement, one-line form (keyword table entry): evaluates the condition; false skips the\nrest of the line (mode 2). True: a line number after THEN goes to KW_GOTO, a statement after\nit is run through its keyword's routine (KW_CALL_ACTION).","comment":"Evaluate the condition and drop it (Z = false)"},
        "4688": {"comment":"False: mode 2 skips the rest of the line"},
        "4691": {"comment":"The token after THEN"},
        "4694": {"comment":"Its class"},
        "4697": {"comment":"A line number ($A0)?"},
        "4699": {"comment":"Yes: as GOTO"},
        "4702": {"comment":"C = the statement's keyword number"},
        "4705": {"comment":"The token after it"},
        "4708": {"comment":"Run keyword C's routine"},
        "4711": {"synopsis":"Syntax check (keyword table, second word) of LET: one or more targets, each a name with\noptional subscripts, separated by \",\", then \"=\"; the value is skipped (STMT_SKIP).\nErrors: 20000.","comment":"Next token"},
        "4714": {"comment":"The token after the name"},
        "4717": {"synopsis":"CHK_LET: the symbol after a target: \",\", \"=\" or subscripts.","comment":"\",\"? Another target"},
        "4721": {"comment":"\"=\": the value follows"},
        "4723": {"comment":"Skip the value"},
        "4726": {"comment":"\"(\": subscripts?"},
        "4728": {"comment":"Error 20000: Not understood"},
        "4731": {"comment":"ARGS_SKIP_PARENS: past them"},
        "4736": {"synopsis":"LET statement (keyword table entry): LET a, b, ... = value. Every target must have the first\none's type (numeric or string). Their addresses are kept on the CPU stack above a 0 marker;\nthe value is evaluated once and stored in each, then dropped.\nErrors: 20000 for a mixed or missing target or a missing \"=\".","comment":"0: marks the targets' end on the stack"},
        "4740": {"comment":"D = $FF first time: the name is current"},
        "4741": {"synopsis":"KW_LET's loop: reads the next target's name and checks its type against D.","comment":"After \",\": the next name"},
        "4744": {"comment":"The name's class"},
        "4747": {"comment":"Same type as the first target?"},
        "4750": {"comment":"$FF (first target)? Else error 20000"},
        "4754": {"comment":"D = the first target's class"},
        "4755": {"comment":"$20: a numeric name?"},
        "4759": {"comment":"$40: a string name? Else error 20000"},
        "4764": {"synopsis":"Finds the target variable (or array element) and keeps its address.","comment":"Find the variable: HL = its address"},
        "4769": {"comment":"Keep it on the CPU stack"},
        "4770": {"comment":"The symbol after the target"},
        "4773": {"comment":"\",\"? Another target"},
        "4777": {"comment":"\"=\" must follow (error 20000)"},
        "4782": {"comment":"Numeric targets?"},
        "4787": {"comment":"EVAL_NUMERIC: the value"},
        "4790": {"synopsis":"Stores the number in each target, last first, up to the 0 marker; then drops it.","comment":"The next target"},
        "4791": {"comment":"The 0 marker?"},
        "4793": {"comment":"Yes: drop the value"},
        "4796": {"comment":"Store it, kept on the stack"},
        "4801": {"synopsis":"String targets: evaluates the string value.","comment":"EVAL_STRING: the value"},
        "4804": {"synopsis":"Stores the string in each target (STR_POP_VAR's store, kept on the stack) up to the 0\nmarker; then drops it.","comment":"The next target"},
        "4805": {"comment":"The 0 marker?"},
        "4807": {"comment":"Yes: drop the value"},
        "4810": {"comment":"Store it, kept on the stack"},
        "4815": {"synopsis":"LOOK statement (keyword table entry): LOOK [#n,] [AT x,y,] ... : var reads the character\ncode at the channel's current position (EXOS 5 on channel 101 by default, or #n) into a\nnumeric variable. AT x,y sends ESC \"s\" and ESC \"A\" x y to the channel first.\nErrors: 20000; EXOS errors as 9000 + code.","comment":"The current channel"},
        "4819": {"comment":"Kept to restore at the end"},
        "4820": {"comment":"Default channel 101 ($65)"},
        "4822": {"comment":"Carry: the first item is current"},
        "4823": {"synopsis":"KW_LOOK's loop: one \"#n\" or AT item per pass.","comment":"After \",\": the next item"},
        "4826": {"comment":"The item's symbol"},
        "4829": {"comment":"A \"#\" channel?"},
        "4833": {"comment":"EVAL_BYTE_ARG: the channel number"},
        "4836": {"comment":"Read from it"},
        "4841": {"synopsis":"Not a channel: AT x,y, or the end of the items.","comment":"AT x,y?"},
        "4847": {"comment":"Neither: the variable follows"},
        "4849": {"comment":"The token after AT"},
        "4852": {"comment":"ESC \"s\""},
        "4857": {"comment":"DE = x, HL = y"},
        "4860": {"comment":"ESC \"A\" x y: moves the position"},
        "4865": {"synopsis":"After an item: \",\" for another, else \":\" and the variable.","comment":"The symbol after the item"},
        "4868": {"comment":"\",\"? Another item"},
        "4872": {"comment":"\":\" must follow (error 20000)"},
        "4877": {"synopsis":"Reads the character and stores its code in the variable.","comment":"The channel"},
        "4880": {"comment":"Read the character there"},
        "4882": {"comment":"EXOS error: 9000 + A"},
        "4883": {"comment":"HL = its code"},
        "4885": {"comment":"NUM_PUSH_INT"},
        "4888": {"comment":"HL = the variable (array element)"},
        "4891": {"comment":"NUM_POP_VAR: store the code"},
        "4894": {"comment":"($0209) back"},
        "4897": {"synopsis":"OPEN statement (keyword table entry): OPEN #n: [NAME] file$ [ACCESS INPUT | ACCESS OUTPUT].\n1. Reads the channel and the name, and the access: INPUT (or none) opens the file (EXOS 1),\n   OUTPUT creates it (EXOS 2).\n2. Moves the stack first (STACK_RELOCATE).\n3. A channel 1-99 sets bit 6 of ($0200): user channels are open.\n4. On an EXOS error the channel is closed again.\nErrors: 20000 for bad syntax; 7003 when EXOS answers .CHANX (the channel exists); other EXOS\nerrors as 9000 + code.","comment":"\"#n:\" must lead (Z)"},
        "4900": {"comment":"Error 20000 without it"},
        "4903": {"comment":"B: the channel to restore"},
        "4904": {"comment":"A: the channel to open"},
        "4905": {"comment":"A plain word?"},
        "4908": {"comment":"Then it must be NAME (error 20000)"},
        "4914": {"comment":"EVAL_STRING: the file name"},
        "4917": {"comment":"C = 0: open for reading"},
        "4919": {"comment":"The symbol after the name"},
        "4922": {"comment":"Line end?"},
        "4926": {"comment":"\":\"?"},
        "4930": {"comment":"Else ACCESS must follow (error 20000)"},
        "4936": {"comment":"ACCESS INPUT?"},
        "4939": {"comment":"C = 0"},
        "4946": {"comment":"C = 1"},
        "4947": {"comment":"ACCESS OUTPUT?"},
        "4953": {"comment":"Neither: error 20000"},
        "4956": {"synopsis":"Past the access word.","comment":"The token after it"},
        "4959": {"synopsis":"Opens or creates the channel, C = 0 for EXOS 1, 1 for EXOS 2.","comment":"Keep the mode"},
        "4960": {"comment":"STACK_RELOCATE before EXOS takes RAM"},
        "4964": {"comment":"A = the channel"},
        "4966": {"comment":"Channel 0?"},
        "4968": {"comment":"100 or above?"},
        "4972": {"comment":"Bit 6 of ($0200): user channels are open"},
        "4976": {"synopsis":"The EXOS call, DE = the file name.","comment":"DE = the name (length first)"},
        "4981": {"comment":"C = 1 (OUTPUT)?"},
        "4984": {"comment":"EXOS 1: open the channel"},
        "4986": {"comment":"Hides +1 RST 30h / EXOS 2: create the channel"},
        "4989": {"comment":".CHANX: the channel exists?"},
        "4991": {"comment":"Error 7003"},
        "4994": {"comment":"Opened?"},
        "4997": {"comment":"Keep the EXOS error"},
        "4998": {"comment":"The channel number"},
        "5001": {"comment":"Close it again"},
        "5004": {"comment":"Error 9000 + A"},
        "5005": {"synopsis":"Drops the name and puts the old channel back into ($0209).","comment":"ITEM_DROP: the name"},
        "5008": {"comment":"($0209) back to B"},
        "5011": {"synopsis":"OPTION statement (keyword table entry): OPTION ANGLE RADIANS clears, OPTION ANGLE DEGREES\nsets bit 0 of ($0201), the flag the trigonometric functions test.\nErrors: 20000.","comment":"ANGLE must follow (error 20000)"},
        "5017": {"comment":"RADIANS?"},
        "5025": {"comment":"Else DEGREES must follow (error 20000)"},
        "5031": {"comment":"Bit 0 of ($0201): DEGREES on"},
        "5036": {"synopsis":"RADIANS: clears the DEGREES flag and reads past the word.","comment":"DEGREES off: radians"},
        "5040": {"comment":"Past RADIANS"},
        "5043": {"synopsis":"OUT statement (keyword table entry): OUT port, byte writes the byte to the Z80 port (0-255).\nErrors: 1000 \"Unexpected value given\" for a port or byte above 255.","comment":"HL = the port, A = the byte"},
        "5046": {"comment":"Port above 255?"},
        "5048": {"comment":"Error 1000: Unexpected value given"},
        "5051": {"comment":"C = the port"},
        "5055": {"synopsis":"PING statement (keyword table entry): writes BEL (7) to channel 103; an EXOS error is\nignored.","comment":"Channel 103 ($67)"},
        "5057": {"comment":"BEL (7)"},
        "5059": {"comment":"Write it; no error check"},
        "5062": {"synopsis":"POKE statement (keyword table entry): POKE address, byte writes the byte at the address as\nthe Z80 sees it now.","comment":"HL = the address, A = the byte"},
        "5067": {"synopsis":"Reads \"address, byte\" for POKE, SPOKE and OUT: the address may be 0-65535 (or negative: it\nis taken modulo 65536 through x - 32768), the byte 0-255.\nExit: HL = the address, A = the byte.\nErrors: 1000 for a value that does not fit, 20000 without \",\".","comment":"EVAL_NUMERIC: the address"},
        "5070": {"comment":"32768"},
        "5074": {"comment":"NUM_PUSH_INT"},
        "5077": {"comment":"NUM_SUB: x - 32768 fits a signed word"},
        "5080": {"comment":"NUM_POP_INT"},
        "5084": {"comment":"+ 32768: HL = x as an unsigned word"},
        "5085": {"comment":"\",\" must follow (error 20000)"},
        "5090": {"comment":"A = the byte (0-255, error 1000)"},
        "5093": {"synopsis":"SPOKE statement (keyword table entry): SPOKE segment, address, byte writes the byte into a\nsegment: the address is moved into page 1 ($4000-$7FFF), page 1 is set to the segment (port\n$B1) for the write and restored.","comment":"A = the segment (0-255, error 1000)"},
        "5097": {"comment":"\",\" must follow (error 20000)"},
        "5102": {"comment":"HL = the address, A = the byte"},
        "5105": {"comment":"The address moved into page 1"},
        "5109": {"comment":"E = the byte"},
        "5110": {"comment":"Page 1's segment"},
        "5112": {"comment":"Kept in A'"},
        "5113": {"comment":"A = the segment wanted"},
        "5114": {"comment":"Page 1 = that segment"},
        "5116": {"comment":"Write the byte"},
        "5117": {"comment":"The old segment"},
        "5118": {"comment":"Page 1 restored"},
        "5121": {"synopsis":"Syntax check (keyword table, second word) of PRINT and LPRINT: runs segment 1's PRINT_CHECK.","comment":"Segment 1's PRINT_CHECK (call byte $BD)"},
        "5125": {"synopsis":"LPRINT statement (keyword table entry): prints on channel 104. PRINT's entry is $1408,\ninside the next instruction: C = 0. Both set ($0209) to C, run segment 1's PRINT_EXEC and\nrestore ($0209).","comment":"LPRINT: channel 104 ($68)"},
        "5127": {"comment":"Hides +1 LD C,0: PRINT's entry, channel 0"},
        "5130": {"comment":"The current channel"},
        "5134": {"comment":"Kept to restore at the end"},
        "5135": {"comment":"The channel to print on"},
        "5136": {"comment":"Segment 1's PRINT_EXEC (call byte $BE)"},
        "5139": {"comment":"($0209) back"},
        "5142": {"synopsis":"Writes ESC \"=\", E + 32 and D + 32 to channel ($0209): moves the text cursor (INPUT AT row,\ncolumn: E = the row, D = the column).","comment":"ESC \"=\""},
        "5147": {"comment":"E + 32 first"},
        "5150": {"comment":"Then D + 32"},
        "5151": {"synopsis":"Writes E + 32 to channel ($0209) with PRINT_CHAR.","comment":"Code + 32"},
        "5154": {"comment":"PRINT_CHAR"},
        "5157": {"synopsis":"CLEAR statement (keyword table entry).\n1. CLEAR #n NET clears a network channel's buffers (EXOS 11, @@CLR); CLEAR #n writes code\n   $1A to the channel.\n2. Otherwise a list of options separated by \",\" or \";\": FKEYS (segment 1's FKEYS_DEFAULT),\n   FONT (EXOS 11, @@FONT on channel 102), or an entry of CLEAR_OPTIONS, which writes a code\n   to its channel.\nErrors: 20000 for an unknown option; EXOS errors as 9000 + code.","comment":"Optional \"#n:\" (Z when given)"},
        "5160": {"comment":"B: the channel to restore"},
        "5161": {"comment":"No channel: the word options"},
        "5163": {"comment":"CLEAR #n NET?"},
        "5169": {"comment":"No: just clear the channel's screen"},
        "5171": {"comment":"Past NET"},
        "5174": {"comment":"The channel"},
        "5177": {"comment":"@@CLR: clear the network buffers"},
        "5181": {"comment":"EXOS error: 9000 + A"},
        "5182": {"synopsis":"CLEAR #n: writes code $1A to the channel unless NET was done; then ($0209) is restored.","comment":"Code $1A, written when NET was not given"},
        "5184": {"comment":"PRINT_CHAR"},
        "5189": {"synopsis":"KW_CLEAR's loop: one option per pass.","comment":"FKEYS?"},
        "5197": {"comment":"Segment 1's FKEYS_DEFAULT (call byte $C5)"},
        "5200": {"comment":"EXOS error: 9000 + A"},
        "5203": {"synopsis":"Not FKEYS: FONT?","comment":"FONT?"},
        "5211": {"comment":"Channel 102 ($66)"},
        "5213": {"comment":"@@FONT: the default character set"},
        "5217": {"comment":"EXOS error: 9000 + A"},
        "5220": {"synopsis":"Not FONT: looks the word up in CLEAR_OPTIONS.","comment":"Z never holds here (FONT's test gave NZ)"},
        "5223": {"comment":"The option table"},
        "5226": {"synopsis":"One row of CLEAR_OPTIONS per pass: B = the action, C = the channel, DE = the name.","comment":"B = the action byte"},
        "5227": {"comment":"The table's end?"},
        "5228": {"comment":"Error 20000: Not understood"},
        "5232": {"comment":"C = the channel"},
        "5235": {"comment":"DE = the option's counted name"},
        "5241": {"comment":"Z when the current word is that name"},
        "5245": {"comment":"Not this one: the next row"},
        "5247": {"comment":"($0209) = the option's channel"},
        "5250": {"comment":"Carry = bit 0; B = the code"},
        "5252": {"comment":"A = the code"},
        "5253": {"comment":"Bit 0 clear: write the code"},
        "5255": {"comment":"Code 0: QUEUE"},
        "5257": {"comment":"Write it to the channel"},
        "5260": {"comment":"And to channel 101 ($65)"},
        "5266": {"synopsis":"Action 1 (QUEUE): evaluates a value (0-255) and writes ESC \"Z\" and it to the channel.","comment":"The value after QUEUE (0-255)"},
        "5270": {"comment":"ESC \"Z\""},
        "5275": {"comment":"The value"},
        "5276": {"synopsis":"Writes code A to channel ($0209).","comment":"PRINT_CHAR"},
        "5279": {"synopsis":"After an option: \",\" or \";\" for another, else the end.","comment":"The token after the option"},
        "5282": {"comment":"\",\"? Another option"},
        "5286": {"comment":"\";\"? Another option"},
        "5290": {"synopsis":"Restores ($0209) and returns.","comment":"($0209) back"},
        "5293": {"synopsis":"CLEAR's word options, 4 bytes a row, read by CLEAR_TBL_LOOP: action B, channel C, the word's\ntext address (length first). B bit 0 clear: B / 2 is a code written to the channel; set: B /\n2 = 0 is QUEUE, else the code also goes to channel 101. SCREEN $35 ch 0, TEXT $34 ch 0,\nGRAPHICS $34 ch 101, SOUND $34 ch 103, QUEUE $01 ch 103, ENVELOPE $30 ch 103. A zero byte\nends it."},
        "5318": {"synopsis":"RANDOMIZE statement (keyword table entry): seeds the generator from the refresh register\n(top byte, ($0211)) and EXOS variable 39 RANDOM_IRQ (low byte, ($0246)), then falls into\nRND_STEP.","comment":"A = the refresh register"},
        "5320": {"comment":"The generator's top byte"},
        "5323": {"comment":"B = 0 read, C = 39 RANDOM_IRQ"},
        "5326": {"comment":"D = RANDOM_IRQ"},
        "5328": {"comment":"Into the generator's low byte"},
        "5332": {"synopsis":"Call byte $2D: steps the 24-bit random generator, ($0211) top and ($0246) low word, 16\ntimes; each step shifts it left and feeds in bit 3 XOR bit 0 of the top byte.\nExit: A = the new ($0211).\nChanges: AF, B, HL.","comment":"16 steps"},
        "5334": {"comment":"The top byte"},
        "5337": {"synopsis":"RND_STEP's loop: one shift per pass.","comment":"H = it"},
        "5338": {"comment":"Bit 3 XOR bit 0 of it"},
        "5342": {"comment":"Into carry"},
        "5344": {"comment":"A = the top byte again"},
        "5345": {"comment":"The low 16 bits"},
        "5348": {"comment":"Shifted left, the new bit in at bit 0"},
        "5353": {"comment":"And on into the top byte"},
        "5356": {"comment":"The new top byte"},
        "5360": {"synopsis":"Syntax check (keyword table, second word) of READ: the options of IO_OPTS (only IF MISSING\napplies to READ).","comment":"The token after READ"},
        "5363": {"comment":"A = 0: READ"},
        "5366": {"synopsis":"Syntax check (keyword table, second word) of INPUT: the options of IO_OPTS.","comment":"The token after INPUT"},
        "5369": {"comment":"A = 1: INPUT"},
        "5373": {"synopsis":"Syntax check (keyword table, second word) of LINE: INPUT must follow, then the options of\nIO_OPTS.","comment":"The token after LINE"},
        "5376": {"comment":"INPUT must follow (error 20000)"},
        "5382": {"comment":"A = $FF: LINE INPUT"},
        "5384": {"synopsis":"Check only (B bit 0 cleared), then IO_OPTS.","comment":"Check only: nothing computed"},
        "5386": {"synopsis":"Parses the options of READ, INPUT and LINE INPUT up to the \":\" that ends them: #channel, IF\nMISSING (a line number or EXIT DEF / DO / FOR), PROMPT string, AT row, column; separated by\n\",\" or \";\". With B bit 0 set (INPUT's and READ's routines, $1638) they are computed: the\nchannel goes into ($0209), the prompt into $0496, AT moves the cursor on channel 0;\notherwise only checked, and an IF MISSING line number is retyped $A2.\nEntry: A = 0 READ, 1 INPUT, $FF LINE INPUT; B bit 0 = compute.\nExit: E bit 0 a line for IF MISSING, bit 1 any option, bit 2 AT; Z with no option. Errors:\n20000.","comment":"AF' = the kind (Z for READ)"},
        "5388": {"comment":"E: bit 1 an option seen, 0 a line, 2 AT"},
        "5390": {"synopsis":"IO_OPTS's loop: one option per pass.","comment":"A \"#\" channel?"},
        "5397": {"comment":"READ?"},
        "5400": {"comment":"INPUT: an option seen"},
        "5404": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "5408": {"comment":"No: skip the channel expression"},
        "5413": {"synopsis":"Computing: the channel number goes into ($0209).","comment":"EVAL_BYTE_ARG: the channel"},
        "5416": {"comment":"Read from it"},
        "5421": {"synopsis":"READ with \"#\": not an option here; the tests below go on.","comment":"AF' back"},
        "5422": {"synopsis":"IF MISSING? Not this option: PROMPT is tested next.","comment":"IF MISSING?"},
        "5432": {"comment":"An option seen"},
        "5435": {"comment":"The token after IF"},
        "5438": {"comment":"HL' = the read pointer here"},
        "5443": {"comment":"MISSING"},
        "5446": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "5450": {"comment":"Check: MISSING?"},
        "5453": {"comment":"No: go on with the next separator"},
        "5455": {"comment":"Past MISSING"},
        "5458": {"comment":"Z: no second check"},
        "5459": {"synopsis":"After MISSING: a line number, or EXIT DEF / DO / FOR.","comment":"Computing: MISSING must follow (error 20000)"},
        "5462": {"comment":"A line number given?"},
        "5469": {"comment":"Check only: mark it as a line reference"},
        "5475": {"comment":"Bit 0: IF MISSING goes to a line"},
        "5480": {"synopsis":"IF MISSING EXIT DEF, DO or FOR.","comment":"HL' = the read pointer here"},
        "5485": {"comment":"Else EXIT must follow (error 20000)"},
        "5491": {"comment":"EXIT DEF?"},
        "5499": {"comment":"EXIT DO?"},
        "5507": {"comment":"EXIT FOR? Else error 20000"},
        "5518": {"synopsis":"Past the option's last word.","comment":"The token after it"},
        "5521": {"synopsis":"After an option: \",\" or \";\" for another, else \":\" must end the list.","comment":"The flags"},
        "5522": {"comment":"The separator"},
        "5525": {"comment":"\",\"? Another option"},
        "5529": {"comment":"\";\"? Another option"},
        "5531": {"comment":"Else \":\" must follow (error 20000)"},
        "5536": {"synopsis":"Reads past the separator and parses the next option.","comment":"The token after the separator"},
        "5539": {"comment":"The next option"},
        "5542": {"synopsis":"PROMPT string (not for READ).","comment":"PROMPT?"},
        "5550": {"comment":"READ?"},
        "5554": {"comment":"An option seen"},
        "5558": {"comment":"The token after PROMPT"},
        "5561": {"comment":"The prompt string (evaluated when B bit 0)"},
        "5564": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "5569": {"comment":"The string's length byte"},
        "5576": {"comment":"The prompt buffer at $0496"},
        "5579": {"comment":"Length byte included"},
        "5580": {"comment":"Copy the prompt"},
        "5582": {"comment":"The string dropped"},
        "5588": {"synopsis":"AT row, column (not for READ); none of the options: the end.","comment":"AT?"},
        "5596": {"comment":"READ?"},
        "5601": {"comment":"Bit 2: AT given"},
        "5604": {"comment":"The row"},
        "5607": {"comment":"\",\" must follow (error 20000)"},
        "5612": {"comment":"The column"},
        "5615": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "5620": {"comment":"Pop the column (0-255)"},
        "5624": {"comment":"Pop the row (0-255)"},
        "5627": {"comment":"D = the column"},
        "5628": {"comment":"E = the row"},
        "5629": {"comment":"Channel 0?"},
        "5632": {"comment":"On the screen channel (0)?"},
        "5633": {"comment":"Then moves the cursor to the two values (CURSOR_AT_DE)"},
        "5636": {"comment":"Compute flag back"},
        "5637": {"comment":"Look for the next option"},
        "5639": {"synopsis":"READ meets AT or PROMPT: they are no options there; puts the mode flags back and falls into\nINPOPT_END, so the word is read as a variable name.","comment":"Mode flags back to AF'"},
        "5640": {"synopsis":"End of the option list of READ / INPUT / LINE INPUT (the parser at IO_OPTS), at a token that\nis no option: returns when no option was read; after an option and a comma it is error 20000\n(Not understood).","comment":"E: bit 1 = an option was read"},
        "5641": {"comment":"None: the variables start here"},
        "5644": {"comment":"Error 20000: an option must follow the comma"},
        "5647": {"synopsis":"READ statement (keyword 59's action): reads DATA items into the listed variables. Mode A = 0\nfor RDIN_EXEC.","comment":"Mode 0: READ"},
        "5650": {"synopsis":"INPUT statement (keyword 39's action): mode A = 1 for RDIN_EXEC.","comment":"Mode 1: INPUT"},
        "5654": {"synopsis":"LINE INPUT statement (keyword 41 LINE's action): the word INPUT must follow (error 20000\notherwise); mode A = $FF for RDIN_EXEC.","comment":"The word INPUT must follow"},
        "5660": {"comment":"Mode $FF: LINE INPUT"},
        "5662": {"synopsis":"The action shared by READ, INPUT and LINE INPUT.\nEntry: A = mode (0 READ, 1 INPUT, $FF LINE INPUT); the current token follows the keyword.\n1. Keeps the output channel ($0209) on the stack, sets HL' = 0 (no IF MISSING clause), makes\n   \"? \" the prompt at $0496 and reads the options (#channel, AT, PROMPT, IF MISSING) with\n   the parser at IO_OPTS, computing.\n2. READ starts at the DATA pointer ($022C)/($022E); INPUT and LINE INPUT start with an empty\n   buffer at $0248, read pointer ($0230).\n3. For each variable (RDIN_NEXT_VAR) one item is taken from that text and stored; the\n   program's ($0214) is saved and put back around it.\n4. Out of items: the IF MISSING action, else error 8001 (Out of data in READ/INPUT). The end\n   (RDIN_DONE) puts ($0209) back.","comment":"Mode to AF'"},
        "5663": {"comment":"The output channel, put back at the end"},
        "5667": {"comment":"HL' = 0: no IF MISSING clause yet"},
        "5671": {"comment":"Same channel for now"},
        "5674": {"comment":"The prompt at $0496: counted text \"? \""},
        "5677": {"comment":"Length 2"},
        "5680": {"comment":"\"?\""},
        "5683": {"comment":"Space"},
        "5685": {"comment":"Compute"},
        "5687": {"comment":"Mode back in A for the option parser"},
        "5688": {"comment":"Reads #channel, AT, PROMPT, IF MISSING"},
        "5692": {"comment":"BC' = the current token's first byte"},
        "5698": {"comment":"Mode flags"},
        "5699": {"comment":"READ?"},
        "5702": {"comment":"INPUT: read pointer at the empty buffer"},
        "5708": {"comment":"Buffer length 0"},
        "5711": {"comment":"And an end byte"},
        "5712": {"synopsis":"Next variable of READ / INPUT / LINE INPUT: INPUT and LINE INPUT go to INPUT_FIND_ITEM, READ\nfalls into READ_FIND_DATA.","comment":"Mode flags"},
        "5713": {"comment":"INPUT or LINE INPUT?"},
        "5715": {"synopsis":"READ: steps over a comma at the DATA pointer ($022E), then finds the next item from the DATA\nline ($022C) on.","comment":"Mode flags back to AF'"},
        "5716": {"comment":"The DATA text pointer"},
        "5720": {"comment":"Past a comma?"},
        "5728": {"synopsis":"Loop of READ over the program lines from ($022C): stops on a DATA line with text left at\n($022E) (an item), steps over lines that are not DATA or are used up, and ends at the\nprogram's end (RDIN_MISSING).","comment":"The DATA line"},
        "5731": {"comment":"Program's end?"},
        "5735": {"comment":"Line +5: its keyword"},
        "5739": {"comment":"Keyword 12, DATA?"},
        "5744": {"comment":"Its text pointer"},
        "5748": {"comment":"\"!\": a remark ends the items"},
        "5752": {"comment":"Line's end?"},
        "5753": {"comment":"No: an item is there"},
        "5755": {"synopsis":"READ: moves ($022C) to the next program line and ($022E) to its text (line + 6), and looks\nagain.","comment":"Past this line: + its length"},
        "5763": {"comment":"Its text: line + 6"},
        "5771": {"synopsis":"INPUT got an empty item: drops the variable's address, the program pointer and the flags\nkept for it, and goes on as RDIN_MISSING.","comment":"Drops the variable's address"},
        "5772": {"comment":"And the program pointer"},
        "5773": {"comment":"Flags back in E"},
        "5774": {"synopsis":"No item left: runs the IF MISSING clause when there is one (then ends the statement),\notherwise raises error 8001, Out of data in READ/INPUT.","comment":"An IF MISSING clause?"},
        "5777": {"comment":"Yes: it ran; end the statement"},
        "5780": {"comment":"Error 8001: Out of data in READ/INPUT"},
        "5784": {"synopsis":"INPUT / LINE INPUT: LINE INPUT goes straight to INPUT_ITEM; INPUT first steps over a comma\nat ($0230).","comment":"LINE INPUT?"},
        "5787": {"comment":"Mode flags back to AF'"},
        "5788": {"comment":"The input text pointer"},
        "5792": {"comment":"Past a comma?"},
        "5800": {"synopsis":"INPUT: takes the mode flags out again and goes on into INPUT_ITEM.","comment":"Mode flags"},
        "5801": {"synopsis":"INPUT / LINE INPUT: when the text at ($0230) is used up, reads a new line from the channel\n(INPUT_NEW_LINE); a stopped read counts as a missing item.","comment":"Mode flags back to AF'"},
        "5802": {"comment":"The input text pointer"},
        "5805": {"comment":"Text used up?"},
        "5809": {"comment":"Prompt, then read a new line"},
        "5812": {"comment":"Read stopped: treat as missing"},
        "5814": {"synopsis":"Reads one item into the current variable.\n1. The token must be a name (error 20000); VAR_FIND_VISIBLE (segment 1) and ARRAY_ELEMENT\n   find its address; E bit 2 records whether a comma follows (another variable), otherwise\n   the statement must end there.\n2. The program pointer ($0214) is kept and ($0214) is pointed at the DATA text ($022E) or\n   the input text ($0230).\n3. A string variable takes the whole input line (LINE INPUT) or one item (TEXT_PUSH_ITEM), a\n   numeric one a number (TEXT_TO_NUMBER); the value is popped into the variable."},
        "5815": {"comment":"Is the token a name?"},
        "5818": {"comment":"No: error 20000"},
        "5821": {"comment":"HL = the variable (element), C = flags"},
        "5825": {"comment":"No comma yet"},
        "5827": {"comment":"Another variable follows (\",\")?"},
        "5834": {"comment":"Yes: remember it"},
        "5836": {"synopsis":"Keeps the flags; without a comma after the variable the statement must end there (error\n20000)."},
        "5837": {"comment":"No comma: the line must end here"},
        "5840": {"comment":"DE = the variable's address"},
        "5841": {"comment":"The program pointer, kept"},
        "5845": {"comment":"And the variable"},
        "5846": {"comment":"Mode flags"},
        "5847": {"comment":"READ: the DATA text"},
        "5850": {"comment":"READ?"},
        "5852": {"comment":"INPUT: the input text"},
        "5855": {"synopsis":"Points the token reader ($0214) at the item text, then branches on the variable's type.","comment":"The token reader reads the item text"},
        "5858": {"comment":"Mode flags back to AF'"},
        "5859": {"comment":"A numeric variable?"},
        "5863": {"comment":"Mode flags"},
        "5864": {"comment":"READ or INPUT: one string item"},
        "5867": {"comment":"LINE INPUT: the whole buffer"},
        "5870": {"comment":"Length - 1"},
        "5871": {"comment":"BC = that count"},
        "5874": {"comment":"The length byte is now 2 less"},
        "5875": {"comment":"HL = the buffer's last copied byte + 1"},
        "5876": {"comment":"The reader stops at the text's end"},
        "5879": {"comment":"Copy below the stack's top"},
        "5885": {"comment":"Moves length byte and text as a string"},
        "5888": {"comment":"Type 3: a string item"},
        "5890": {"comment":"It is the new top"},
        "5893": {"comment":"Mode $FF (LINE INPUT) again, M"},
        "5895": {"synopsis":"READ / INPUT into a string variable: pushes the next item of the text as a string\n(TEXT_PUSH_ITEM), then pops it into the variable (STR_POP_VAR).","comment":"READ or INPUT: push one text item"},
        "5898": {"comment":"Mode flags back to AF'"},
        "5899": {"comment":"The variable"},
        "5900": {"comment":"STR_POP_VAR: store the string"},
        "5905": {"synopsis":"Numeric variable: LINE INPUT is error 20031 (String identifier expected); INPUT with nothing\nleft is an empty item (RDIN_EMPTY).","comment":"Mode flags"},
        "5906": {"comment":"LINE INPUT: error 20031"},
        "5909": {"comment":"Mode flags back to AF'"},
        "5910": {"comment":"TEXT_SKIP_BLANKS: HL at the item"},
        "5913": {"comment":"Mode flags"},
        "5914": {"comment":"READ?"},
        "5916": {"comment":"Mode flags back to AF'"},
        "5917": {"comment":"INPUT: nothing typed for it?"},
        "5923": {"synopsis":"Reads a decimal number from the item text (TEXT_TO_NUMBER), pushes it and pops it into the\nvariable (NUM_POP_VAR).","comment":"Mode flags back to AF'"},
        "5924": {"comment":"TEXT_TO_NUMBER: number to $0595"},
        "5927": {"comment":"NUM_PUSH_WORK: push it"},
        "5930": {"comment":"The variable"},
        "5931": {"comment":"NUM_POP_VAR: store the number"},
        "5934": {"synopsis":"After an item: it must end in a comma, \"!\" or the text's end (error 20034, Type mismatch,\notherwise); the new position goes back to ($0230) or ($022E), the program pointer back to\n($0214).","comment":"TEXT_SKIP_BLANKS: HL after the item"},
        "5937": {"comment":"The program pointer"},
        "5938": {"comment":"Comma?"},
        "5943": {"comment":"\"!\"?"},
        "5947": {"comment":"Text's end?"},
        "5948": {"comment":"Something else: error 20034"},
        "5951": {"synopsis":"Stores the item text's new position: READ in ($022E), INPUT in ($0230).","comment":"Mode flags"},
        "5952": {"comment":"READ?"},
        "5954": {"comment":"INPUT: the new input text pointer"},
        "5959": {"synopsis":"READ: the new DATA text pointer.","comment":"The new DATA text pointer"},
        "5962": {"synopsis":"Puts the program's reader back to the statement, reads the token after the variable and\nloops while a comma followed it.","comment":"Mode flags back to AF'"},
        "5963": {"comment":"Back to the statement's text"},
        "5967": {"comment":"Past the variable's comma"},
        "5971": {"comment":"Another variable?"},
        "5976": {"synopsis":"End of READ / INPUT / LINE INPUT: CHAN_RESTORE pops the kept output channel back into\n($0209) and\nreturns.","comment":"Channel back into ($0209), return"},
        "5979": {"synopsis":"Pushes the next item of the text at ($0214) as a string: a quoted one (\"\" inside stands for\none quote; no closing quote is error 20043, Missing closing quotes) or an unquoted one up to\na comma, \"!\" or the text's end. ($0214) moves past it.\nEntry: ($0214) at the item.\nExit: the string pushed (type 3); AF kept.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"AF kept (the mode flags)"},
        "5980": {"comment":"TEXT_SKIP_BLANKS: HL at the item"},
        "5983": {"comment":"Length counter, -1"},
        "5985": {"comment":"C = 0: unquoted"},
        "5988": {"comment":"Opening quote?"},
        "5992": {"comment":"C = 1: quoted"},
        "5993": {"synopsis":"Loop over the item's characters: steps past one and counts it.","comment":"Next character"},
        "5994": {"synopsis":"Counts a character and tests it: quoted items end at a single quote, unquoted ones at\nTXTITEM_UNQ's ends.","comment":"Count it"},
        "5996": {"comment":"Quoted?"},
        "6000": {"comment":"Text's end inside quotes?"},
        "6001": {"comment":"Yes: error 20043, Missing closing quotes"},
        "6004": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "6008": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6010": {"comment":"Doubled quote: one quote character"},
        "6014": {"comment":"Closing quote: the item ends"},
        "6016": {"synopsis":"Unquoted item: ends at a comma, \"!\" or the text's end.","comment":"Comma?"},
        "6020": {"comment":"\"!\"?"},
        "6024": {"comment":"Text's end?"},
        "6027": {"synopsis":"Item found: E = its length. Moves ($0214) past it, then copies its characters backwards\nbelow the stack's top (a quote of a pair once, the closing quote dropped).","comment":"Length kept"},
        "6028": {"comment":"The reader continues after the item"},
        "6031": {"comment":"B = characters to copy"},
        "6032": {"comment":"Destination: below the stack's top"},
        "6036": {"comment":"All copied?"},
        "6037": {"synopsis":"Copy loop, from the item's end backwards: a quote in a quoted item is replaced by the\ncharacter before it."},
        "6041": {"comment":"Previous source character"},
        "6043": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "6047": {"comment":"In a quoted item?"},
        "6051": {"comment":"Takes the character before it"},
        "6053": {"synopsis":"Stores one character of the item below the stack's top.","comment":"Stores it"},
        "6056": {"synopsis":"Puts the length byte and the type byte 3 in front of the copied text and makes it the\nstack's top."},
        "6057": {"comment":"E = the length"},
        "6058": {"comment":"Length byte"},
        "6060": {"comment":"Type 3: a string"},
        "6062": {"comment":"New top of the stack"},
        "6065": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "6067": {"synopsis":"Runs the IF MISSING clause, kept in HL' by the option parser: reads its text and does a GOTO\nto its line number (E bit 0 set) or its EXIT (DEF, DO or FOR).\nExit: NC when there is no clause; C when it ran.","comment":"HL' = the clause's text, 0 for none"},
        "6071": {"comment":"None: NC"},
        "6073": {"comment":"The reader goes to the clause"},
        "6077": {"comment":"Its first token"},
        "6080": {"comment":"E bit 0: a line number?"},
        "6085": {"comment":"EXIT ...: the EXIT statement's action"},
        "6088": {"comment":"Z: skips the GOTO"},
        "6089": {"synopsis":"IF MISSING with a line number: the GOTO statement's action (KW_GOTO).","comment":"Line number: the GOTO action"},
        "6093": {"comment":"C: the clause ran"},
        "6095": {"synopsis":"Reads a new input line for INPUT / LINE INPUT: prints the prompt at $0496 when the channel\nis 0, writes $18 to EXOS variable 32 (FLG_EDIT), reads the line into the buffer at $0248\n(INPUT_LINE) and points ($0230) at its text ($0249).\nExit: C when the read was stopped; A = $FF."},
        "6096": {"comment":"On the screen channel (0)?"},
        "6100": {"comment":"Then the prompt text"},
        "6103": {"comment":"PRINT_COUNTED"},
        "6106": {"comment":"Write (B = 1) EXOS variable 32"},
        "6109": {"comment":"Value $18"},
        "6113": {"comment":"INPUT_LINE: reads into $0248"},
        "6116": {"comment":"The input text starts at $0249"},
        "6123": {"comment":"A = $FF"},
        "6126": {"synopsis":"REDIRECT statement (keyword 60's action): PARSE_FROM_TO reads the FROM and TO channels (B,\ndefault\n0; C, default $68), then EXOS 18 redirects channel A = B to C; an EXOS error is raised (RST\n18h).","comment":"B = FROM channel, C = TO channel"},
        "6129": {"comment":"A = the channel redirected"},
        "6132": {"comment":"EXOS error: BASIC error 9000 + A"},
        "6134": {"synopsis":"Syntax check of RESTORE and RUN (their descriptors' second address): reads the next token\nand, when it is a line number, marks it as one (LINEREF_MARK).","comment":"The token after the keyword"},
        "6137": {"comment":"The number read, 0 if none"},
        "6142": {"comment":"None: return"},
        "6143": {"synopsis":"Marks the current number token as a line number: its type byte (before the text at ($0347))\nbecomes $A2. Also used by $1237 and $155F.","comment":"The token's type byte"},
        "6147": {"comment":"$A2: a line number reference"},
        "6150": {"synopsis":"RESTORE statement (keyword 63's action): sets the DATA pointer to the given line (error\n20004, Line number does not exist, when there is none) or to the program's start.","comment":"A line number given?"},
        "6155": {"comment":"No: the program's start"},
        "6160": {"comment":"LINE_FIND for line ($0218)"},
        "6163": {"comment":"Not found: error 20004"},
        "6166": {"comment":"Past the number"},
        "6169": {"synopsis":"Sets the DATA pointer: ($022C) = the line at HL, ($022E) = its text (line + 6).","comment":"The DATA line"},
        "6172": {"comment":"Its text: line + 6"},
        "6180": {"synopsis":"RETRY statement (keyword 64's action): ($0207) = 0, then leaves the handler's scope through\nSCOPE_POP with NC (no value kept).","comment":"NC; ($0207) = 0"},
        "6184": {"comment":"Leave the scope"},
        "6187": {"synopsis":"RETURN statement (keyword 65's action): the line must end here; drops the items above the\nnearest GOSUB record (type 6), error 10002 (RETURN without GOSUB) when there is none;\nBLOCK_LEAVE\nmakes the record's line current and drops the record (returning through STACK_TOP_DE), then\n($0206) = 3 (SET_MODE_LINE).","comment":"Nothing may follow (error 20000)"},
        "6190": {"synopsis":"Drops stack items of types below 6 until a record of type 6 or more, or the stack's bottom.","comment":"Drop the top if its type is below 6"},
        "6195": {"comment":"A GOSUB record (type 6)?"},
        "6197": {"comment":"No: error 10002, RETURN without GOSUB"},
        "6200": {"comment":"Its line becomes current; record dropped"},
        "6203": {"comment":"($0206) = 3"},
        "6206": {"synopsis":"EXT statement (keyword 84's action): hands a command string (the string expression, or an\nempty one) to the extension ROMs with EXOS 26 at $FA78, which raises an EXOS error and drops\nthe string.","comment":"Line's end?"},
        "6211": {"comment":"Then an empty counted text"},
        "6216": {"comment":"EVAL_STRING: the command string"},
        "6219": {"comment":"DE = its length byte"},
        "6224": {"synopsis":"Goes on to EXT_PASS_CMD: EXOS 26 with the string at DE.","comment":"EXOS 26, error check, ITEM_DROP"},
        "6227": {"comment":"Not reached from code in this ROM"},
        "6228": {"synopsis":"SET statement (keyword 69's action): CHANNEL_ARG reads an optional \"#channel\", then segment\n1's\nSTMT_SET (call byte $B7) does the rest.","comment":"Optional \"#channel\""},
        "6231": {"comment":"STMT_SET (segment 1)"},
        "6235": {"synopsis":"INFO statement (keyword 73's action; also called by $02CA).\n1. Resets the run state (RUN_STATE_RESET) and reads the system status (EXOS 20, $ED63).\n2. Prints the working and non-working RAM segments' total as \"n bytes in system\", then the\n   non-working ones as \"n bytes not working\" when there are any (PRINT_SEG_BYTES prints n x\n16384 and\n   \"bytes \").\n3. Prints \"n bytes unused\": free segments x 16384 + the EXOS boundary (EXOS 22) + $3FFF\n   minus the low 14 bits of ($0226).\n4. When any program exists (PROGS_ANY), lists program 0, the current one and every program\n   1-127 that has a segment: its number, \"*\" for the current one, its size and its first\n   line; then switches back to the current program.","comment":"RUN_STATE_RESET"},
        "6238": {"comment":"($0226), kept for the unused count"},
        "6242": {"comment":"EXOS 20 to $0E2C; HL = working segments"},
        "6245": {"comment":"DE = them, HL = $0E2C"},
        "6246": {"comment":"Byte 6: non-working segments"},
        "6251": {"comment":"Kept for the second line"},
        "6252": {"comment":"HL = all segments"},
        "6254": {"comment":"Prints HL x 16384 and \"bytes \""},
        "6257": {"comment":"PRINT_COUNTED of the text after it"},
        "6260": {"synopsis":"Text \"in system\" CR LF, length first, printed by INFO_STMT after the bytes in system count."},
        "6272": {"comment":"Non-working segments"},
        "6273": {"comment":"None?"},
        "6277": {"comment":"Prints HL x 16384 and \"bytes \""},
        "6280": {"comment":"PRINT_COUNTED of the text after it"},
        "6283": {"synopsis":"Text \"not working\" CR LF, length first, printed by INFO_STMT after the non-working bytes\ncount."},
        "6297": {"synopsis":"INFO, step 3: adds up the unused memory and prints \"n bytes unused\", then lists the\nprograms.","comment":"($0226)"},
        "6298": {"comment":"$3FFF minus its low 14 bits"},
        "6307": {"comment":"NUM_PUSH_INT"},
        "6310": {"comment":"EXOS 22: DE = EXOS boundary"},
        "6313": {"comment":"NUM_PUSH_INT"},
        "6316": {"comment":"EXOS 20 byte 1: free segments"},
        "6322": {"comment":"NUM_PUSH_INT"},
        "6325": {"comment":"x 16384, + boundary, + the first"},
        "6329": {"comment":"NUM_PUSH_INT: 16384"},
        "6330": {"comment":"NUM_MUL: free segments x 16384"},
        "6331": {"comment":"NUM_ADD: + the EXOS boundary"},
        "6332": {"comment":"NUM_ADD: + the first count"},
        "6333": {"comment":"End of the call list"},
        "6334": {"comment":"Prints the top number"},
        "6340": {"comment":"PRINT_COUNTED of the text after it"},
        "6343": {"synopsis":"Text \"bytes unused\" CR LF CR LF, length first, printed by INFO_UNUSED."},
        "6360": {"comment":"ITEM_DROP: the total"},
        "6363": {"comment":"Any program at all?"},
        "6366": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "6367": {"comment":"B = the current program's number"},
        "6371": {"comment":"C = 0: the first program"},
        "6373": {"synopsis":"INFO, step 4: for each program number C (0-127): program 0 and the current one are shown;\nanother only when a segment is tagged with its number (SEG_TAG_FIND).","comment":"B = current, C = this one"},
        "6375": {"comment":"The current program?"},
        "6378": {"comment":"Program 0?"},
        "6381": {"comment":"SEG_TAG_FIND (segment 1): a segment for C?"},
        "6382": {"comment":"SEG_TAG_FIND"},
        "6383": {"comment":"End of the call list"},
        "6384": {"comment":"None: next number"},
        "6386": {"synopsis":"INFO: switches to program C (PROG_SWITCH) and prints its number in five places, then \"*\"\nwhen it\nis the current one or a space.","comment":"Switch to program C"},
        "6389": {"comment":"L = its number"},
        "6393": {"comment":"Prints it in 5 places, spaces in front"},
        "6396": {"comment":"B = current, C = this one"},
        "6399": {"comment":"The current one?"},
        "6400": {"comment":"\"*\" marks it"},
        "6404": {"comment":"Others: a space"},
        "6406": {"synopsis":"INFO: prints the mark, then the program's size (its end - its start) in five places and\nthree spaces.","comment":"PRINT_CHAR"},
        "6409": {"comment":"HL = the program's end"},
        "6412": {"comment":"Its start"},
        "6418": {"comment":"Size in bytes"},
        "6420": {"comment":"Prints it in 5 places"},
        "6423": {"comment":"PRINT_COUNTED: 3 spaces"},
        "6426": {"synopsis":"Text of three spaces, length first, printed by INFO_MARK_OUT after a program's size."},
        "6430": {"comment":"The program's start"},
        "6431": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "6435": {"comment":"Empty: only CR LF"},
        "6438": {"comment":"Z: no line to list"},
        "6439": {"synopsis":"INFO: lists the program's first line (LINE_LIST_CH) when it has one.","comment":"Lists its first line"},
        "6442": {"synopsis":"INFO: the next program number, up to 127; then switches back to the current program\n(PROG_SWITCH).","comment":"B = current, C = this one"},
        "6443": {"comment":"Next number"},
        "6444": {"comment":"Up to 127"},
        "6447": {"comment":"Switch back to the current program"},
        "6451": {"synopsis":"Finds whether any program exists: a segment tagged with a program number 1-127 in segment\n1's segment table (SEG_TAG_FIND), or a current program that is not empty. Also called by\nSTART ($0E78).\nExit: NC when there is one; C when there is none.\nChanges: A, C, HL.","comment":"Program numbers 127 down to 1"},
        "6453": {"synopsis":"Loop over program numbers C = 127 down to 1: returns NC at the first one with a segment.","comment":"SEG_TAG_FIND (segment 1)"},
        "6454": {"comment":"SEG_TAG_FIND"},
        "6455": {"comment":"End of the call list"},
        "6456": {"comment":"Found: NC"},
        "6457": {"comment":"Next number"},
        "6460": {"comment":"The current program's start"},
        "6463": {"comment":"Not empty?"},
        "6465": {"comment":"NC: a program"},
        "6466": {"comment":"C: no program at all"},
        "6468": {"synopsis":"STOP statement (keyword 72's action): prints the STOP message (PRINT_STOP_MSG, which returns\nHL = the current line), calls CMD_LEVEL_CALL, makes that line current again and sets ($0206)\n= 2\n(STMT_NEXT_LINE).","comment":"PRINT_STOP_MSG; HL = ($0216)"},
        "6472": {"comment":"Sets bit 5 of ($0200), then BASIC_STATUS"},
        "6476": {"comment":"The line is current again"},
        "6479": {"comment":"($0206) = 2"},
        "6482": {"synopsis":"TOGGLE statement (keyword 76's action): the option word (SETOPT_LOOKUP, segment 1) or a\nnumber 1-255 gives an EXOS variable, which EXOS 16 toggles (B = 2). An option that is no\nEXOS variable, or 0, is error 20060 (Invalid machine option use); an EXOS error is raised\n(RST 18h).","comment":"SETOPT_LOOKUP (segment 1): an option?"},
        "6483": {"comment":"SETOPT_LOOKUP"},
        "6484": {"comment":"End of the call list"},
        "6485": {"comment":"Bit 7: an EXOS variable option?"},
        "6487": {"comment":"C = its variable number"},
        "6489": {"comment":"Found by name?"},
        "6491": {"comment":"No: A = a number from the expression"},
        "6494": {"comment":"It is the variable number"},
        "6495": {"comment":"0?"},
        "6496": {"synopsis":"TOGGLE: error 20060 for variable 0 or an option that is no EXOS variable; otherwise toggles\nEXOS variable C.","comment":"Error 20060: Invalid machine option use"},
        "6499": {"comment":"By name: past the word"},
        "6502": {"comment":"Toggle (B = 2) EXOS variable C"},
        "6506": {"comment":"EXOS error: BASIC error 9000 + A"},
        "6508": {"synopsis":"TRACE statement (keyword 77's action): TRACE OFF clears bit 4 of ($0200); TRACE ON sets it,\nand with TO #n stores the channel n in ($0208). Any other word is error 20000.","comment":"The word ON?"},
        "6516": {"comment":"The word OFF?"},
        "6522": {"comment":"Neither: error 20000"},
        "6525": {"comment":"OFF: tracing off"},
        "6529": {"comment":"Past OFF"},
        "6532": {"synopsis":"TRACE ON: sets bit 4 of ($0200); \"TO\" and symbol $03 (the \"#\" of a channel) then give the\ntrace channel, kept in ($0208).","comment":"Tracing on"},
        "6536": {"comment":"Past ON"},
        "6539": {"comment":"The word TO?"},
        "6546": {"comment":"Past TO"},
        "6549": {"comment":"A channel (\"#\", symbol $03)?"},
        "6552": {"comment":"EVAL_BYTE_ARG: A = the channel"},
        "6555": {"comment":"The trace channel"},
        "6559": {"synopsis":"WAIT statement (keyword 91's action): segment 1's STMT_WAIT_DELAY (call byte $C0) does it.","comment":"STMT_WAIT_DELAY (segment 1)"},
        "6560": {"comment":"STMT_WAIT_DELAY"},
        "6561": {"comment":"End of the call list"},
        "6563": {"synopsis":"Syntax check of ELSE (keyword 21) when a line is stored: when the word IF follows, the\nline's keyword byte ($024D in the buffer) becomes 22 (ELSE IF) and the word IF is removed\n(LINEBUF_RESIZE closes the gap).","comment":"The token after ELSE"},
        "6566": {"comment":"The word IF?"},
        "6572": {"comment":"No: plain ELSE"},
        "6573": {"comment":"The buffered line's keyword byte"},
        "6576": {"comment":"Keyword 22: ELSE IF"},
        "6578": {"comment":"The text goes on right after it"},
        "6579": {"comment":"LINEBUF_RESIZE: removes the IF"},
        "6582": {"synopsis":"Block IF statement (keyword 38's action), also an ELSE IF reached by skipping: evaluates the\ncondition; true: the word THEN must follow and the block's lines run. False: skips to the\nnext ELSE IF (whose condition is tried), ELSE or END IF (IF_SKIP_BRANCH).","comment":"Condition: Z when it is 0"},
        "6585": {"comment":"The word THEN"},
        "6588": {"comment":"True: THEN must follow (error 20000)"},
        "6591": {"comment":"False: to the next branch"},
        "6594": {"comment":"ELSE or END IF: run on from there"},
        "6595": {"comment":"ELSE IF: its text after the keyword"},
        "6600": {"comment":"Its first token"},
        "6603": {"comment":"Try its condition"},
        "6605": {"synopsis":"ELSE and ELSE IF statements (keywords 21 and 22's action), reached after a branch ran: skips\nevery further branch up to END IF.","comment":"To the next branch"},
        "6608": {"comment":"END IF: done"},
        "6611": {"synopsis":"Skips the lines of an IF branch: makes the next line of the same nesting depth current\n(($0206) = 2, LINE_GOTO_LEVEL) and tests its keyword.\nExit: C (and Z) for ELSE IF (22); NC and Z for ELSE (21); NC and NZ for END IF (26); DE =\nthe line's keyword byte. Any other keyword is error 20051, Invalid end of block.","comment":"($0206) = 2"},
        "6614": {"comment":"Next line at this depth; A = keyword"},
        "6617": {"comment":"Keyword 22, ELSE IF?"},
        "6619": {"comment":"C"},
        "6621": {"comment":"Keyword 21, ELSE?"},
        "6624": {"comment":"Keyword 26, END IF?"},
        "6626": {"comment":"Other: error 20051, Invalid end of block"},
        "6629": {"comment":"NZ, NC"},
        "6631": {"synopsis":"Action of a multi-line DEF (keyword 14) and of HANDLER (keyword 35) met in the normal run:\nskips the block to its END DEF (24) or END HANDLER (25) line, which becomes current; any\nother line at that depth is error 20051, Invalid end of block.","comment":"($0206) = 2"},
        "6634": {"comment":"Next line at this depth; A = keyword"},
        "6637": {"comment":"Keyword 24, END DEF?"},
        "6640": {"comment":"Keyword 25, END HANDLER?"},
        "6643": {"comment":"Other: error 20051"},
        "6646": {"synopsis":"Calls a function defined with DEF (from the evaluator, $21A2 and $22B2).\nEntry: HL = the function name's value field (its value, then the DEF line's address); C =\nits flags (bit 0 string); A and the carry are kept in the scope record.\n1. Opens a scope (SCOPE_PUSH) and keeps the caller's text position in HL'/DE' (TEXT_POS_SWAP\n   switches between the two texts).\n2. Reads the DEF line: declares the function's name in the new scope (VAR_DECLARE, segment\n   1) as its result variable.\n3. Binds the parameters to the arguments one by one: REF parameters are declared as\n   references to the caller's variables (VAR_DECLARE_REF), the others get the argument's\n   value. New names stay hidden (bit 6 of their first letter cleared) until all arguments\n   are read, then SCOPE_NAMES shows them. A count or bracket mismatch is error 4000, Error\n   in DEF parameter.\n4. A multi-line DEF runs its body with the run loop RUN_LOOP until END DEF, which pops the\n   scope with the result; a one-line DEF evaluates the expression after \"=\" and pops the\n   scope keeping it.\nExit: the result pushed; the caller's text position back; the token after the call read.","comment":"The function's value field"},
        "6647": {"comment":"Opens the function's scope"},
        "6651": {"comment":"Flags kept"},
        "6652": {"comment":"HL' = the caller's line"},
        "6656": {"comment":"DE' = the caller's read pointer"},
        "6661": {"comment":"A string function?"},
        "6663": {"comment":"A number is 6 bytes"},
        "6668": {"comment":"String: its maximum length"},
        "6669": {"comment":"Past the maximum and length bytes"},
        "6671": {"synopsis":"Takes the DEF line's address stored after the function's value, makes that line current and\nreads it from line + 6; the function's name is declared as the result variable of the new\nscope.","comment":"Past the value"},
        "6672": {"comment":"The DEF line's address"},
        "6676": {"comment":"It is the current line"},
        "6679": {"comment":"Its text: line + 6"},
        "6686": {"comment":"The function's name"},
        "6689": {"comment":"VAR_DECLARE (segment 1): result variable"},
        "6690": {"comment":"VAR_DECLARE"},
        "6691": {"comment":"End of the call list"},
        "6692": {"comment":"Next token of the DEF"},
        "6695": {"comment":"\"(\": parameters?"},
        "6700": {"comment":"To the caller's text"},
        "6703": {"comment":"Its next token"},
        "6706": {"comment":"\"(\" there too?"},
        "6708": {"comment":"No: error 4000, Error in DEF parameter"},
        "6711": {"comment":"Back to the DEF"},
        "6714": {"synopsis":"Loop over the DEF's parameters: REF before the name binds by reference, otherwise by value\n(FNCALL_VAL_PARAM).","comment":"The parameter's first token"},
        "6717": {"comment":"The word REF?"},
        "6723": {"comment":"No: a value parameter"},
        "6725": {"comment":"To the caller's text"},
        "6728": {"comment":"The argument"},
        "6731": {"comment":"Must be a name: Z string, NZ numeric"},
        "6734": {"comment":"VAR_FIND_ANY (segment 1): the caller's variable"},
        "6735": {"comment":"VAR_FIND_ANY"},
        "6736": {"comment":"End of the call list"},
        "6737": {"comment":"The token after it"},
        "6740": {"comment":"An array element (\"(\")?"},
        "6747": {"comment":"Compute"},
        "6749": {"comment":"ARRAY_ELEMENT: HL = the element"},
        "6752": {"comment":"A plain variable now"},
        "6754": {"synopsis":"REF parameter: declares the DEF's parameter name in the new scope as a reference to the\ncaller's variable at HL (VAR_DECLARE_REF), its name hidden for now.","comment":"The caller's variable"},
        "6755": {"comment":"Its flags"},
        "6756": {"comment":"E = the argument's separator"},
        "6759": {"comment":"Back to the DEF"},
        "6762": {"comment":"The parameter's name"},
        "6766": {"comment":"The new entry goes at ($0234)"},
        "6769": {"comment":"Kept; HL = the caller's variable"},
        "6771": {"comment":"A = flags for the reference"},
        "6772": {"comment":"VAR_DECLARE_REF (segment 1)"},
        "6773": {"comment":"VAR_DECLARE_REF"},
        "6774": {"comment":"End of the call list"},
        "6776": {"comment":"The new entry"},
        "6777": {"comment":"+4: its name's first byte"},
        "6781": {"comment":"Hidden until all arguments are read"},
        "6785": {"synopsis":"Value parameter: creates the parameter's variable (PARAM_CREATE, name hidden), evaluates the\ncaller's argument of the same type and pops it into the variable.","comment":"Creates it: HL = name, BC = length"},
        "6788": {"comment":"Hidden until all arguments are read"},
        "6790": {"comment":"HL = its value field"},
        "6792": {"comment":"Z: a string"},
        "6793": {"comment":"To the caller's text"},
        "6796": {"comment":"The argument's first token"},
        "6801": {"comment":"Evaluates a string (Z) or a number"},
        "6806": {"comment":"A number?"},
        "6808": {"comment":"STR_POP_VAR into the parameter"},
        "6811": {"comment":"Z: skips the number store"},
        "6812": {"synopsis":"Stores a numeric argument (NUM_POP_VAR), then reads the argument's separator and goes back\nto the DEF's text.","comment":"NUM_POP_VAR into the parameter"},
        "6815": {"comment":"E = the argument's separator"},
        "6818": {"comment":"Back to the DEF"},
        "6821": {"synopsis":"After a parameter: a comma in both texts takes the next one; otherwise both must have \")\"\n(error 4000 otherwise).","comment":"The token after the parameter"},
        "6824": {"comment":"Comma?"},
        "6828": {"comment":"The caller had a comma too?"},
        "6833": {"synopsis":"The parameter list must end with \")\" in the DEF and in the call (E bit 1); then the new\nnames are shown (SCOPE_NAMES with C).","comment":"\")\"?"},
        "6835": {"synopsis":"Error 4000, Error in DEF parameter, when NZ.","comment":"No: error 4000, Error in DEF parameter"},
        "6838": {"comment":"The caller ended with \")\"?"},
        "6840": {"comment":"No: error 4000"},
        "6843": {"comment":"Past \")\" in the DEF"},
        "6846": {"comment":"C: show the scope's names"},
        "6847": {"comment":"SCOPE_NAMES"},
        "6850": {"synopsis":"Runs the function: $EFBF with B = 14 finds whether the DEF line is a multi-line DEF (Z, and\nthe line after the DEF becomes the current one: BLOCK_ENTER with B = 14, block DEF); then\nthe run loop RUN_LOOP runs it to END DEF. Otherwise FNCALL_EXPR.","comment":"The DEF line"},
        "6853": {"comment":"Keyword 14: a multi-line DEF?"},
        "6858": {"comment":"No: a one-line DEF"},
        "6860": {"comment":"The caller's position kept"},
        "6863": {"comment":"Runs the body up to END DEF"},
        "6869": {"comment":"Drops the flags"},
        "6872": {"synopsis":"One-line DEF: symbol $13 (\"=\") must follow; the expression after it is evaluated as a number or a string (the function's type) and SCOPE_POP keeps it as the result (C).","comment":"Symbol $13 must follow (error 20000)"},
        "6877": {"comment":"The function's flags"},
        "6878": {"comment":"A string function?"},
        "6882": {"comment":"EVAL_NUMERIC"},
        "6885": {"comment":"Z: skips the string"},
        "6886": {"synopsis":"String function: EVAL_STRING; then closes the scope keeping the value.","comment":"EVAL_STRING"},
        "6889": {"comment":"C: the value on top is the result"},
        "6890": {"comment":"SCOPE_POP"},
        "6893": {"synopsis":"Back to the caller's text (TEXT_POS_SWAP) and the token after the call.","comment":"Back to the caller's text"},
        "6896": {"comment":"TOKEN_NEXT"},
        "6899": {"synopsis":"Checks that the current token is a name, for a DEF parameter.\nExit: Z for a string name, NZ for a numeric one; error 4000 (Error in DEF parameter) for\nanything else.","comment":"A string name: Z, NC"},
        "6902": {"comment":"Then return"},
        "6903": {"comment":"A numeric name?"},
        "6905": {"comment":"No: error 4000"},
        "6907": {"comment":"NZ, NC"},
        "6909": {"synopsis":"Creates a variable for the current name in the current scope (VAR_CREATE, segment 1), with\nits initial value (also used by $0F30).\nExit: HL = the entry's name (+4); BC = the name's length; Z for a string name, NZ for a\nnumeric one (PARAM_NAME_TYPE).","comment":"Must be a name: Z string"},
        "6912": {"comment":"Type kept"},
        "6913": {"comment":"The new entry goes at ($0234)"},
        "6917": {"comment":"VAR_CREATE (segment 1)"},
        "6918": {"comment":"VAR_CREATE"},
        "6919": {"comment":"End of the call list"},
        "6920": {"comment":"The new entry"},
        "6921": {"comment":"+3: its name's length"},
        "6927": {"comment":"+4: the name"},
        "6928": {"comment":"Type back"},
        "6930": {"synopsis":"Swaps the token reader's position (($0214) read pointer, ($0216) current line) with the one\nkept in DE' and HL': switches between a DEF's text and its caller's.\nChanges: BC', DE', HL'."},
        "6931": {"comment":"The read pointers swap"},
        "6941": {"comment":"The current lines swap"},
        "6952": {"synopsis":"E = the kind of the current symbol after an argument: 1 for \",\" ($0C), 2 for \")\" ($09), 0\nfor anything else (Z for the first two).","comment":"The current symbol"},
        "6955": {"comment":"1: comma"},
        "6960": {"comment":"2: closing bracket"},
        "6965": {"comment":"0: anything else"},
        "6968": {"synopsis":"Opens a scope for a function call or a handler: pushes a 6-byte record of type 7 on the\nBASIC stack: +1/+2 the old scope start ($0236), +3 A x 2 + carry (bit 0: no result to keep),\n+4/+5 the allocation pointer ($0234); the new scope starts at ($0234).\nEntry: A, carry.\nExit: ($0236) = ($0234) = DE.\nChanges: A, DE, HL.","comment":"Below the stack's top"},
        "6971": {"comment":"The allocation pointer"},
        "6976": {"comment":"+4/+5: ($0234)"},
        "6981": {"comment":"+3: A x 2 + carry"},
        "6984": {"comment":"+1/+2: the old scope start"},
        "6992": {"comment":"Type 7: a scope record"},
        "6994": {"comment":"New top of the stack"},
        "6998": {"comment":"The scope starts at ($0234)"},
        "7003": {"synopsis":"END HANDLER statement (keyword 25's action): ($0207) = 3, then falls into END_DEF_STMT.","comment":"($0207) = 3"},
        "7007": {"synopsis":"END DEF statement (keyword 24's action): SCOPE_POP with NC, which pushes the function's\nresult variable.","comment":"NC: push the result variable"},
        "7008": {"synopsis":"Closes the newest scope (the type 7 record of SCOPE_PUSH).\nEntry: C = keep the value item on top of the stack as the result; NC = push the value of the\nscope's first variable (the function's name) as the result.\n1. Steps over the kept value, then over records of type 4 (25 bytes), below 4 (5 bytes) and\n   6 (3 bytes) to the type 7 record; another type is error 20051, Invalid end of block.\n2. Forgets the scope's names (SCOPE_NAMES with NC) and restores ($0236) and ($0234) from the\n   record; ($0206) = 0 (C) or 4 (NC).\n3. A record pushed with carry drops everything down to it and returns. Otherwise the kept\n   value is moved down over the dropped records (C), or the result variable's value is\n   pushed (SCOPEPOP_RESULT).","comment":"Carry kept"},
        "7009": {"comment":"The stack's top"},
        "7012": {"comment":"No value to keep?"},
        "7014": {"comment":"The value's type"},
        "7015": {"comment":"A number is 9 bytes"},
        "7022": {"comment":"String: + 2 + its length"},
        "7025": {"synopsis":"Steps HL past the kept value item.","comment":"Past the value"},
        "7026": {"synopsis":"Keeps the address after the value, then looks for the type 7 record over the records above\nit."},
        "7027": {"comment":"End of the kept value"},
        "7029": {"comment":"$19 is ADD HL,DE: the loop steps at $1B76"},
        "7031": {"comment":"Record type"},
        "7032": {"comment":"Type 4: 25 bytes"},
        "7039": {"comment":"Below 4: 5 bytes"},
        "7043": {"comment":"Type 6: 3 bytes"},
        "7049": {"comment":"Type 7, the scope?"},
        "7051": {"comment":"No: error 20051, Invalid end of block"},
        "7054": {"comment":"Its +1"},
        "7056": {"comment":"NC: forgets the scope's names"},
        "7060": {"comment":"+1/+2: the old scope start"},
        "7068": {"comment":"+3: flags"},
        "7070": {"comment":"+4/+5: the allocation pointer"},
        "7078": {"comment":"The entry carry"},
        "7079": {"comment":"C: 0"},
        "7085": {"synopsis":"Stores ($0206) (0 when a value was kept, 4 otherwise); a record whose bit 0 is set (no\nresult) just drops the stack down to it.","comment":"($0206): 0 or 4"},
        "7088": {"comment":"Record pushed with carry?"},
        "7090": {"comment":"DE = end of the kept value"},
        "7093": {"comment":"Drop down to the record"},
        "7097": {"synopsis":"C: moves the kept value down so that it ends where the record ended, and makes it the\nstack's top.","comment":"NC: push the result variable"},
        "7100": {"comment":"The value's start"},
        "7105": {"comment":"BC = its size"},
        "7109": {"comment":"HL = its end"},
        "7110": {"comment":"DE = the record's end"},
        "7113": {"comment":"Moves the value down"},
        "7116": {"synopsis":"Sets the BASIC stack's top ($0228) = DE. Also the return address that BLOCK_LEAVE pushes,\nwhich\ndrops RETURN's GOSUB record this way.","comment":"New top of the stack"},
        "7121": {"synopsis":"NC: drops the stack down to the record and pushes the value of the scope's first variable\n(BC, the function's name): NUM_PUSH_VAR or STR_PUSH_AT for a string.","comment":"Drop down to the record"},
        "7124": {"comment":"The scope's first entry"},
        "7126": {"comment":"+2: its flags"},
        "7129": {"comment":"+3: the name's length"},
        "7133": {"comment":"+4: the name"},
        "7134": {"comment":"HL = its value field"},
        "7135": {"comment":"A string?"},
        "7137": {"comment":"NUM_PUSH_VAR"},
        "7140": {"comment":"Pushes the string variable"},
        "7143": {"synopsis":"Goes over the 32 hash chains of names at $0DCB; the names made in the current scope (entries\nat or above ($0236)) are at their fronts.\nEntry: C = show them (bit 6 of each one's first letter set, the state that a lookup\nmatches); NC = forget them (each chain's head moved past them).\nChanges: AF', BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Carry kept in F'"},
        "7144": {"comment":"The 32 hash chain heads"},
        "7147": {"comment":"Count"},
        "7149": {"synopsis":"Next hash chain: keeps the head's address.","comment":"The head's address"},
        "7151": {"synopsis":"Follows a link: BC = DE = the next entry (the candidate head).","comment":"The counter in A"},
        "7152": {"comment":"DE = the next entry"},
        "7155": {"comment":"BC = it, the head if it stays"},
        "7157": {"synopsis":"An entry below ($0236) (or 0) ends the chain's scope part and becomes its head; one inside\nis skipped (NC) or shown (C).","comment":"The scope's start"},
        "7161": {"comment":"Entry below it?"},
        "7165": {"comment":"Yes: the head is BC"},
        "7167": {"comment":"The carry"},
        "7168": {"comment":"NC: skip it"},
        "7170": {"comment":"Carry: keep the entry, follow its link"},
        "7171": {"comment":"DE = the next entry"},
        "7177": {"comment":"Bit 6 of the entry's byte +4 set"},
        "7179": {"comment":"Test the next entry"},
        "7181": {"synopsis":"Stores BC, the first entry kept, as this bucket's head and moves on to the next of the 32\nbuckets.","comment":"This bucket's head"},
        "7182": {"comment":"Head = BC (unchanged when marking)"},
        "7186": {"comment":"All 32 buckets done?"},
        "7190": {"synopsis":"SELECT statement (keyword $44, from the keyword table at $3895). Evaluates the selector\nafter an optional word CASE (a string when it starts with a string name or literal), then\nlooks at the lines at the block's level one by one (LINE_GOTO_LEVEL, which makes each the\ncurrent line\n($0216)):\n1. CASE: its items, separated by commas, are tried in turn: IS <relation> value (REL_NUMERIC\n   /\n   REL_STRING), value TO value, or a single value (compared with ITEM_COMPARE), each against\na\n   copy of the selector; CASE ELSE matches anything.\n2. A match drops the selector; the run goes on after that CASE line (($0206) = 2).\n3. END SELECT reached without a match is error 10004 \"No CASE selected\"; another line at the\n   block's level is error 20051 \"Invalid end of block\".\nRun: FOR J=1 TO 7 over CASE 1 / CASE 2 TO 3,6 / CASE IS >6 / CASE ELSE printed ONE TWO3 TWO3\nELSE ELSE TWO3 BIG; SELECT \"AB\" matched CASE \"AA\" TO \"AC\"; SELECT 9 with only CASE 1 stopped\nwith \"No CASE selected\".","comment":"Optional word CASE after SELECT"},
        "7196": {"comment":"Skip it"},
        "7199": {"comment":"Z when the selector is a string"},
        "7202": {"comment":"Keep the selector's type"},
        "7203": {"comment":"The selector, pushed"},
        "7206": {"comment":"($0206) = 2: run on after ($0216)"},
        "7209": {"synopsis":"Loop: the next line at the block's level must be CASE or END SELECT.","comment":"Next line at this level; A = its keyword"},
        "7212": {"comment":"CASE?"},
        "7216": {"comment":"END SELECT?"},
        "7218": {"comment":"Anything else: error 20051"},
        "7221": {"comment":"No CASE matched: error 10004"},
        "7225": {"synopsis":"A CASE line: its list is read from the byte after the keyword.","comment":"Past the CASE keyword"},
        "7226": {"comment":"Read the CASE line from there"},
        "7230": {"synopsis":"Loop over the items of a CASE line: an IS relation, ELSE, a range or a single value.","comment":"The item's first token"},
        "7233": {"comment":"CASE IS?"},
        "7239": {"comment":"No: ELSE, a range or a value"},
        "7241": {"comment":"A copy of the selector"},
        "7244": {"comment":"Past IS: the operator"},
        "7247": {"comment":"Selector's type back (Z string)"},
        "7249": {"comment":"Compute this time"},
        "7251": {"comment":"A numeric selector?"},
        "7253": {"comment":"String relation, C = its truth"},
        "7256": {"comment":"Z: no numeric relation"},
        "7257": {"synopsis":"CASE IS with a numeric selector: the relation with a numeric value (C = its truth).","comment":"Numeric relation, C = its truth"},
        "7260": {"comment":"Z when the relation holds"},
        "7263": {"synopsis":"An item without IS: ELSE matches; otherwise a value, perhaps the low end of a range.","comment":"CASE ELSE?"},
        "7269": {"comment":"Yes: it matches"},
        "7271": {"comment":"A copy of the selector"},
        "7274": {"comment":"Selector's type back"},
        "7276": {"comment":"The item's value, of that type"},
        "7279": {"comment":"A range (TO follows)?"},
        "7287": {"comment":"Single value"},
        "7289": {"comment":"Compare with the selector copy"},
        "7292": {"comment":"Z when equal"},
        "7294": {"synopsis":"CASE a TO b: matches when a <= selector <= b.","comment":"Range: the selector copy"},
        "7296": {"comment":"...against the low end"},
        "7299": {"comment":"Below it: no match"},
        "7302": {"comment":"Another copy for the high end"},
        "7305": {"comment":"Past TO"},
        "7310": {"comment":"The high end"},
        "7315": {"comment":"Compare the selector with it"},
        "7318": {"comment":"Below the high end: a match"},
        "7321": {"synopsis":"Z: the item matched; otherwise the next item.","comment":"Equal: a match"},
        "7323": {"synopsis":"The item did not match: a comma leads to the next item, otherwise the next CASE line.","comment":"More items after a comma?"},
        "7328": {"comment":"Next item"},
        "7331": {"comment":"Next CASE line"},
        "7334": {"synopsis":"A match: drops the selector; the run goes on after this CASE line.","comment":"Selector's type off the stack"},
        "7335": {"comment":"Drop the selector"},
        "7338": {"synopsis":"CASE statement (keyword $05, from the keyword table at $35DF), reached when the lines after\nthe CASE that matched have run: skips the following CASE lines of the block and goes on\nafter END SELECT (($0206) = 2). Another line at the block's level is error 20051 \"Invalid\nend of block\".","comment":"Next line at this level; A = its keyword"},
        "7341": {"comment":"Another CASE?"},
        "7343": {"comment":"Skip it"},
        "7345": {"comment":"END SELECT?"},
        "7347": {"comment":"Anything else: error 20051"},
        "7350": {"comment":"Run on after END SELECT"},
        "7353": {"synopsis":"DO statement (keyword $12, from the keyword table at $366A).\n1. A first run pushes a type 5 item, 5 bytes: +0 5, +1/+2 the DO line, +3/+4 the LOOP line\n   (the next line at the block's level; error 20051 \"Invalid end of block\" when it is not\n   LOOP). When LOOP sends the run back here, the top item is already the type 5 item of this\n   line and is kept.\n2. Tests the DO's own condition (LOOP_CONDITION): kept (or none), the statement ends and the\n   body\n   runs; failed, the item is popped and the run goes on after the LOOP line (BLOCK_LEAVE).\nRun: DO WHILE I<5 ... LOOP.","comment":"Room for 4 bytes (+2)"},
        "7359": {"comment":"Top item"},
        "7362": {"comment":"Its type"},
        "7363": {"comment":"DE = its first word"},
        "7367": {"comment":"The DO line"},
        "7370": {"comment":"A DO/LOOP item?"},
        "7374": {"comment":"For this DO line?"},
        "7376": {"comment":"Yes: only test the condition"},
        "7378": {"synopsis":"A first run: checks that the block ends in LOOP and pushes the type 5 item.","comment":"Keyword of the next line at this level"},
        "7381": {"comment":"LOOP?"},
        "7383": {"comment":"No: error 20051"},
        "7386": {"comment":"Push the LOOP line, then the DO line"},
        "7393": {"comment":"Type 5: a DO/LOOP item"},
        "7395": {"synopsis":"Tests the DO's condition: kept, returns into the body; failed, leaves the loop.","comment":"C = 1 to run the body"},
        "7398": {"comment":"Run the body?"},
        "7400": {"comment":"Leave: HL = item +2"},
        "7405": {"synopsis":"Leaves a control block: HL + 1 points at a line word of the item on top. Makes that line\n($0216), sets ($0206) = 2 (the run goes on after it) and returns through STACK_TOP_DE, which\nsets\n($0228) = DE, popping the stack up to just past the word. DO uses it with HL = item +2 (the\nLOOP line at +3/+4); RETURN calls it at $1838 for the GOSUB item.\nEntry: HL = the byte before the line word.","comment":"Return through STACK_TOP_DE: ($0228) = DE"},
        "7409": {"synopsis":"Takes the line word at HL + 1 as the current line ($0216) and sets ($0206) = 2: the run goes\non after that line.\nExit: DE = HL + 3, past the word. NEXT calls it ($1DFC) with HL = the FOR item, to run on\nafter the FOR line.","comment":"At the line word"},
        "7414": {"comment":"HL = the line, DE = past the word"},
        "7415": {"comment":"It becomes the current line"},
        "7418": {"comment":"($0206) = 2: run on after it"},
        "7421": {"synopsis":"Pushes the start of a control item: below DE (the top) the word HL (an end line), then the\ncurrent line ($0216), then one byte for the type.\nEntry: DE = ($0228), HL = the end line.\nExit: HL = ($0228) = the new top, where the caller writes the item's type. Used by DO and\nFOR.","comment":"HL = the top, DE = the end line"},
        "7422": {"comment":"End line below the top"},
        "7426": {"comment":"Then the current line"},
        "7430": {"synopsis":"Entry for one word: pushes DE below HL (the top) and leaves a byte for the type; HL =\n($0228) = the new top. GOSUB calls it at $11CD (the type 6 item, the line after the GOSUB)."},
        "7434": {"comment":"Byte for the type"},
        "7435": {"comment":"The new top"},
        "7439": {"synopsis":"LOOP statement (keyword $2C, from the keyword table at $378D): the top item must be a\nDO/LOOP item (type 5; error 20051 \"Invalid end of block\" otherwise). Tests LOOP's own\ncondition (LOOP_CONDITION): kept (or none), the DO line becomes the current line and runs\nagain\n(($0206) = 3), where DO tests its own condition; failed, the item is popped and the run goes\non after LOOP.","comment":"Top item"},
        "7442": {"comment":"Its type"},
        "7443": {"comment":"A DO/LOOP item?"},
        "7445": {"comment":"No: error 20051"},
        "7448": {"comment":"C = 1 to go round again"},
        "7452": {"comment":"Top item again"},
        "7455": {"comment":"Leave the loop?"},
        "7457": {"comment":"($0206) = 3: run line ($0216)"},
        "7460": {"comment":"DE = the DO line from +1/+2"},
        "7465": {"comment":"It becomes the current line"},
        "7468": {"synopsis":"Leaves the loop: pops the 5-byte item; the run goes on after LOOP.","comment":"Past the 5-byte item"},
        "7472": {"comment":"Pop it"},
        "7476": {"synopsis":"Reads the optional condition of DO or LOOP: none (the line's end), WHILE e or UNTIL e.\nExit: C = 1 when the loop goes on (no condition, WHILE true, UNTIL false), C = 0 to leave;\nerror 20000 \"Not understood\" for another word.","comment":"Line's end: no condition"},
        "7481": {"comment":"C = 1: go on"},
        "7484": {"comment":"UNTIL?"},
        "7490": {"comment":"A = 1: invert the truth"},
        "7492": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "7494": {"comment":"WHILE?"},
        "7500": {"comment":"Neither: error 20000"},
        "7503": {"comment":"A = 0: the truth as it is"},
        "7504": {"synopsis":"Reads the condition after UNTIL (A = 1) or WHILE (A = 0) and gives C = its truth XOR A.","comment":"Keep the UNTIL flag"},
        "7505": {"comment":"Past the word"},
        "7508": {"comment":"Evaluate and pop, Z when false"},
        "7511": {"comment":"C = 0 when false"},
        "7515": {"comment":"C = 1 when true"},
        "7516": {"synopsis":"C = the truth (0 or 1) XOR the UNTIL flag in A."},
        "7517": {"comment":"UNTIL turns it round"},
        "7520": {"synopsis":"FOR statement (keyword $1F, from the keyword table at $3707): FOR v = a TO b [STEP s].\n1. v must be a plain numeric variable (error 20000 \"Not understood\" otherwise); a is stored\n   in it.\n2. Pushes a type 4 item, 25 bytes: +0 4, +1/+2 the FOR line, +3/+4 the NEXT line (the next\n   line at the block's level; error 20051 \"Invalid end of block\" when it is not NEXT), +5/+6\n   the variable's address, +7 the step (9 bytes, 1 without STEP), +16 the limit (9 bytes).\n3. Tests the variable against the limit (FOR_TEST_LIMIT): within it, the body runs; past it,\n   the item\n   is popped and the run goes on after the NEXT line.\nRun: FOR I=1 TO 3 ... NEXT printed 1 2 3.","comment":"Room for 24 bytes (+2)"},
        "7526": {"comment":"A numeric name?"},
        "7529": {"comment":"No: error 20000"},
        "7532": {"comment":"Find the variable"},
        "7535": {"comment":"A plain variable (flags 0)?"},
        "7537": {"comment":"No: error 20000"},
        "7540": {"comment":"Keep its value field"},
        "7541": {"comment":"Past the name"},
        "7544": {"comment":"Expect \"=\""},
        "7549": {"comment":"The start value"},
        "7553": {"comment":"HL = the variable"},
        "7554": {"comment":"Store the start value"},
        "7557": {"comment":"Expect TO"},
        "7563": {"comment":"The limit, pushed"},
        "7566": {"comment":"STEP?"},
        "7574": {"comment":"The step after STEP"},
        "7579": {"synopsis":"No STEP: the step is 1.","comment":"No STEP: 1"},
        "7585": {"synopsis":"Completes the FOR item below the step: the variable's address, then the two lines and the\ntype.","comment":"The variable's address"},
        "7587": {"comment":"Below the step"},
        "7590": {"comment":"...the variable's address"},
        "7594": {"comment":"Where it sits"},
        "7595": {"comment":"Keyword of the next line at this level"},
        "7598": {"comment":"NEXT?"},
        "7600": {"comment":"No: error 20051"},
        "7604": {"comment":"Push the NEXT line and the FOR line"},
        "7607": {"comment":"Type 4: a FOR item"},
        "7609": {"comment":"HL = the variable"},
        "7610": {"comment":"Test it against the limit"},
        "7612": {"synopsis":"NEXT statement (keyword $2F, from the keyword table at $37AB): the top item must be the FOR\nitem whose NEXT line is this line (error 20051 \"Invalid end of block\" otherwise). Adds the\nstep to the variable, sets the run to go on after the FOR line (ITEM_LINE_RESUME), then\ntests the\nvariable against the limit (FOR_TEST_LIMIT): past it, the item is popped and the run goes on\nafter\nthis line instead.","comment":"Top item"},
        "7616": {"comment":"Its type"},
        "7617": {"comment":"DE = the NEXT line at +3/+4"},
        "7624": {"comment":"BC = the variable at +5/+6"},
        "7627": {"comment":"This line?"},
        "7635": {"comment":"A FOR item?"},
        "7637": {"synopsis":"Error 20051 unless the top item is the FOR item of this NEXT line.","comment":"No: error 20051"},
        "7640": {"comment":"The item's address"},
        "7641": {"comment":"Keep the variable's address"},
        "7642": {"comment":"Room for a number below the top"},
        "7649": {"comment":"IY = the new top"},
        "7652": {"comment":"Item +7 (the step)"},
        "7657": {"comment":"...copied to the top"},
        "7660": {"comment":"The variable's value"},
        "7665": {"comment":"Value + step"},
        "7668": {"comment":"HL = the variable"},
        "7670": {"comment":"Back into it"},
        "7673": {"comment":"Run on after the FOR line"},
        "7679": {"comment":"HL = the variable"},
        "7680": {"synopsis":"Pushes the variable at HL and a copy of the limit (the FOR item is then 18 bytes up) and\ncompares them (both popped) by the step's sign: a step not negative goes on while value <=\nlimit, a negative one while value >= limit. Within it, returns: the body runs, or after NEXT\nthe run goes on after the FOR line. Past it: FOR_FINISHED.\nEntry: HL = the control variable, the FOR item on top.","comment":"The variable's value"},
        "7683": {"comment":"Room for the limit copy"},
        "7695": {"comment":"Item +16 (the limit)"},
        "7700": {"comment":"Copy it to the top"},
        "7703": {"comment":"IY = item +7 (the step)"},
        "7708": {"comment":"Z when the step is not negative"},
        "7711": {"comment":"IY = the top"},
        "7715": {"comment":"Counting up?"},
        "7717": {"comment":"Down: value - limit"},
        "7720": {"comment":"Not below: the body runs"},
        "7723": {"synopsis":"Step not negative: goes on while value <= limit.","comment":"Up: value - limit"},
        "7726": {"comment":"Equal: the body runs"},
        "7727": {"comment":"Below: the body runs"},
        "7728": {"synopsis":"The loop is over: pops the FOR item and goes on after its NEXT line.","comment":"The FOR item"},
        "7734": {"comment":"DE = its NEXT line"},
        "7738": {"comment":"Past the 25-byte item"},
        "7742": {"comment":"Pop it"},
        "7745": {"comment":"($0206) = 2: run on after"},
        "7749": {"comment":"...the NEXT line"},
        "7752": {"synopsis":"WHEN EXCEPTION USE name statement (keyword $50, from the keyword table at $3917). The name,\nfound by segment 1's VAR_FIND_ANY, must be an entry with flags 4 (error 20040 \"Variable not\ninitialised\" otherwise; a handler by the statement's form), and the next line at the block's\nlevel END WHEN (error 20051 \"Invalid end of block\").\nPushes a type 8 item, 12 bytes: +0 8, +1 the old ($0240), +2/+3 the word at the name's value\nfield +6, +4..+7 not written, +8/+9 the old ($023A) (the stack pointer the run loop keeps,\n$CD70), +10/+11 the END WHEN line. Counts ($0240), the WHEN depth, up and runs on from the\nnext line (RUN_FROM_NEXT). Run: WHEN EXCEPTION USE H.","comment":"Expect EXCEPTION"},
        "7758": {"comment":"Expect USE"},
        "7764": {"comment":"Room for 12 bytes (+2)"},
        "7770": {"comment":"A name?"},
        "7773": {"comment":"No: error 20000"},
        "7776": {"comment":"Keyword of the next line at this level"},
        "7779": {"comment":"END WHEN?"},
        "7781": {"comment":"No: error 20051"},
        "7784": {"comment":"Keep the END WHEN line"},
        "7785": {"comment":"Find the handler's name"},
        "7788": {"comment":"Not found?"},
        "7790": {"comment":"Error 20040"},
        "7793": {"comment":"Flags 4?"},
        "7796": {"comment":"No: error 20040"},
        "7799": {"comment":"Past the name"},
        "7802": {"comment":"BC = the word at its value +6"},
        "7808": {"comment":"Build the item below the top"},
        "7812": {"comment":"+10/+11: the END WHEN line"},
        "7816": {"comment":"+8/+9: the run loop's saved SP"},
        "7824": {"comment":"Skip +4..+7"},
        "7828": {"comment":"+2/+3: the handler's word"},
        "7831": {"comment":"+1: the WHEN depth"},
        "7836": {"comment":"+0: type 8"},
        "7839": {"comment":"One WHEN deeper"},
        "7843": {"comment":"Run on from the next line"},
        "7845": {"synopsis":"END WHEN statement (keyword $1C, from the keyword table at $36E1): the top item must be a\nWHEN item (type 8; error 20051 \"Invalid end of block\" otherwise). Restores ($0240) and\n($023A) from it, pops it and runs on from the next line (RUN_FROM_NEXT).","comment":"Top item"},
        "7849": {"comment":"A WHEN item?"},
        "7851": {"comment":"No: error 20051"},
        "7854": {"comment":"+1: the old WHEN depth"},
        "7859": {"comment":"DE = the saved SP at +8/+9"},
        "7866": {"comment":"HL = past the 12-byte item"},
        "7869": {"comment":"Restore it"},
        "7873": {"comment":"A = 0: back into the run loop"},
        "7874": {"synopsis":"Sets ($0228) = HL and goes back into the run loop at the line after ($0216): RESUME_AFTER\nwith A =\n0 jumps to RUN_RESUME.","comment":"The current line"},
        "7878": {"comment":"Run on after it"},
        "7881": {"synopsis":"Evaluates a numeric expression and pops it.\nExit: Z when it was 0 (a false condition), NZ otherwise. Called by the DO/LOOP condition\n($1D54) and at $124E and $19B7.","comment":"The condition, pushed"},
        "7884": {"comment":"Z when it is 0"},
        "7887": {"synopsis":"Pops the 9-byte number at IY (the top, as the number routines leave IY); flags kept. Falls\ninto STACK_TOP_IY.","comment":"Past the number"},
        "7892": {"synopsis":"Sets ($0228) = IY, the new top.","comment":"The new top"},
        "7897": {"synopsis":"Parses a numeric expression from the current token without computing it (B bit 0 cleared);\nonly ($0214) moves. OR $37 clears carry, so no token is read first. Its second byte ($1EDA,\nSCF) is an entry that reads the next token first (called at $104B, $1217, $1520).","comment":"NC: start at the current token"},
        "7899": {"comment":"Parse only"},
        "7901": {"comment":"Into the evaluator"},
        "7903": {"synopsis":"Evaluates a string expression when Z, a numeric one otherwise (falls into EVAL_NUMERIC).","comment":"A string?"},
        "7906": {"synopsis":"Evaluates a numeric expression from the current token and pushes the number (B bit 0 set:\ncomputed). The levels, the loosest first: OR and BOR (EXPR_OR_LEVEL), AND and BAND\n(EXPR_AND_LEVEL), NOT and\nBNOT (EXPR_NOT_LEVEL), one relation (EXPR_RELATION, also between strings), + and -\n(EXPR_ADD_LEVEL), then the\nmultiplicative levels from EVAL_TERM. With B bit 0 clear everything is only parsed\n(SKIP_NUM_EXPR). IY\nis kept.\nEntries inside the instructions: $1EE3 (SCF) computes after reading the next token; $1EE7\n(SCF in LD A,$37) reads the next token and keeps B bit 0 as the caller set it; EXPR_NUM_IFC\nreads\nit when carry; EXPR_NUM starts at the current token with B as set.","comment":"NC: no token read first"},
        "7908": {"comment":"Compute"},
        "7910": {"comment":"Hides SCF: entry $1EE7"},
        "7912": {"synopsis":"Entry: reads the next token first when carry, then evaluates with B bit 0 as set (EXPR_NUM).","comment":"Carry: read the next token first"},
        "7915": {"synopsis":"Numeric expression from the current token, computed when B bit 0 is set: clears B bit 1,\nkeeps IY and runs the OR level."},
        "7917": {"synopsis":"OR level: a left operand from the AND level (EXPR_AND_LEVEL), then any OR or BOR operators;\nrestores\nB and IY at the end. Entry here keeps B bit 1 (called at $0E47).","comment":"Keep IY"},
        "7919": {"comment":"Left operand: AND level"},
        "7923": {"synopsis":"Loop: OR (OR_LOGICAL), BOR, or the end of the level.","comment":"OR?"},
        "7929": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "7931": {"comment":"BOR?"},
        "7937": {"comment":"Neither: B and IY back"},
        "7940": {"comment":"Done"},
        "7941": {"comment":"BOR: keep IY"},
        "7943": {"comment":"Past BOR"},
        "7946": {"comment":"Right operand"},
        "7950": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "7954": {"comment":"BC = right word, HL = left's high byte"},
        "7957": {"comment":"OR the 16-bit words"},
        "7964": {"comment":"Next operator"},
        "7966": {"synopsis":"OR, computed: a left operand that is not 0 is the result and the right side is only parsed\n(OR_SKIP_RIGHT); a left 0 is dropped and the rest of the expression is the result\n(OR_TAKE_RIGHT). Run: 3 OR\n0 = 3, 0 OR 5 = 5.","comment":"Past OR"},
        "7970": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "7974": {"comment":"Keep B"},
        "7975": {"comment":"Left operand 0?"},
        "7979": {"comment":"Yes: the right side is the result"},
        "7981": {"synopsis":"Parses the right operand without computing it; the left stays the result."},
        "7982": {"comment":"Parse only"},
        "7984": {"comment":"The right operand"},
        "7989": {"synopsis":"Drops the left 0 and evaluates the rest of the expression as the result.","comment":"Drop the left operand"},
        "7994": {"comment":"The rest is the result"},
        "7996": {"synopsis":"Drops the left operand (not 0); the rest of the AND level is the result (falls into\nEXPR_AND_LEVEL).","comment":"Drop the left operand"},
        "7999": {"synopsis":"AND level: a left operand from the NOT level (EXPR_NOT_LEVEL), then any AND or BAND\noperators. BAND\nANDs the two 16-bit words; AND, computed, keeps a left 0 and only parses the right side, or\ndrops a left operand that is not 0 for the right side. Run: 2 AND 0 = 0, 2 AND 7 = 7, 12\nBAND 10 = 8.","comment":"Left operand: NOT level"},
        "8003": {"synopsis":"Loop: AND (AND_LOGICAL), BAND, or the end of the level.","comment":"AND?"},
        "8009": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "8011": {"comment":"BAND?"},
        "8018": {"comment":"Neither: done"},
        "8019": {"comment":"Past BAND"},
        "8022": {"comment":"Right operand"},
        "8026": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "8030": {"comment":"BC = right word, HL = left's high byte"},
        "8033": {"comment":"AND the 16-bit words"},
        "8040": {"comment":"Next operator"},
        "8042": {"synopsis":"AND, computed: a left operand not 0 is dropped for the right side (AND_TAKE_RIGHT); a left 0\nstays\nand the right side is only parsed (AND_SKIP_RIGHT).","comment":"Past AND"},
        "8046": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "8051": {"comment":"Left operand 0?"},
        "8055": {"comment":"No: the right side is the result"},
        "8057": {"synopsis":"Parses the right operand without computing it; the left 0 stays the result."},
        "8058": {"comment":"Parse only"},
        "8060": {"comment":"The right operand"},
        "8065": {"synopsis":"NOT level: NOT x gives -1 for 0 and 0 otherwise; BNOT x complements the 16-bit word; without\neither, the relation level (EXPR_RELATION). The NOT path has no B bit 0 test. Run: NOT 0 =\n-1, NOT 3\n= 0, BNOT 0 = -1, 12 BOR 3 = 15.","comment":"NOT?"},
        "8071": {"comment":"C: NOT"},
        "8074": {"comment":"BNOT?"},
        "8080": {"comment":"Neither: a relation"},
        "8082": {"synopsis":"NOT (carry) or BNOT (no carry): reads the operand at the relation level and applies the\noperator.","comment":"Keep which one"},
        "8083": {"comment":"Past the word"},
        "8086": {"comment":"The operand"},
        "8090": {"comment":"BNOT?"},
        "8092": {"comment":"NOT: Z when the operand is 0"},
        "8095": {"comment":"Pop it, flags kept"},
        "8098": {"comment":"0 gives -1"},
        "8103": {"comment":"Else 0"},
        "8104": {"synopsis":"Writes HL as an integer into the slot just popped and makes it the top again.","comment":"Integer HL at IY - 9"},
        "8107": {"comment":"($0228) = IY"},
        "8110": {"synopsis":"BNOT: complements the 16-bit word at +2/+3 of the top number.","comment":"Top number"},
        "8113": {"comment":"Its word at +2/+3"},
        "8116": {"comment":"Low byte complemented"},
        "8120": {"comment":"High byte complemented"},
        "8123": {"synopsis":"Relation level. A string on the left (a string name or literal) needs a relational operator\nand a string on the right (REL_STRING). A numeric operand from the + and - level\n(EXPR_ADD_LEVEL) may be\nfollowed by one operator, symbols $12-$17 (< = > <> <= >=), and a second operand\n(REL_NUMERIC).\nComputed, a relation leaves -1 (true) or 0 (false) on the stack (REL_PUSH_RESULT).","comment":"The token's class"},
        "8126": {"comment":"A string literal?"},
        "8130": {"comment":"A string name?"},
        "8134": {"synopsis":"A string on the left: reads it, then the operator and the right string.","comment":"Left string"},
        "8137": {"comment":"Operator and right string, C = truth"},
        "8142": {"synopsis":"A numeric left operand, then an optional relation.","comment":"Left operand: + and - level"},
        "8145": {"comment":"A relational operator next?"},
        "8150": {"comment":"Below \"<\": no"},
        "8153": {"comment":"Above \">=\": no"},
        "8154": {"comment":"Right operand and comparison"},
        "8157": {"synopsis":"Computed: pushes -1 for C = 1 (true), 0 for C = 0.","comment":"Computing?"},
        "8161": {"comment":"True: -1"},
        "8164": {"comment":"C = 0?"},
        "8168": {"comment":"False: 0"},
        "8169": {"synopsis":"Pushes the result HL as an integer.","comment":"Push the result"},
        "8174": {"synopsis":"Reads a relational operator ($12-$17, else error 20000 \"Not understood\") and the right\nnumeric operand; computed, compares the two (both popped by NUM_COMPARE) and gives C = 1\nwhen the relation holds (REL_TRUTH). Called by SELECT for CASE IS.","comment":"Operator symbol"},
        "8179": {"comment":"Below \"<\": error 20000"},
        "8184": {"comment":"Above \">=\": error 20000"},
        "8187": {"comment":"E = the operator"},
        "8188": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8193": {"comment":"Right operand: + and - level"},
        "8198": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "8203": {"comment":"Compare: H gives the sign"},
        "8206": {"comment":"C from the operator"},
        "8208": {"synopsis":"As REL_NUMERIC for strings: a relational operator, then the right string (EXPR_STR);\ncomputed,\ncompares the two strings (STR_COMPARE, both popped) and gives C = 1 when the relation holds.","comment":"Operator symbol"},
        "8213": {"comment":"Below \"<\": error 20000"},
        "8218": {"comment":"Above \">=\": error 20000"},
        "8221": {"comment":"E = the operator"},
        "8224": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8227": {"comment":"Right string"},
        "8232": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "8237": {"comment":"Compare: H gives the sign"},
        "8240": {"synopsis":"Truth of a relation.\nEntry: E = the operator's symbol ($12-$17), H = the comparison's sign (0 equal, positive\ngreater, negative less). REL_OP_MASKS says which outcomes make the operator true.\nExit: C = 1 true, C = 0 false."},
        "8242": {"comment":"Assume true"},
        "8244": {"comment":"Index = operator - $12"},
        "8250": {"comment":"A = the sign"},
        "8251": {"comment":"The operator's mask"},
        "8255": {"comment":"True when equal?"},
        "8259": {"comment":"Equal?"},
        "8260": {"comment":"Yes: true"},
        "8261": {"synopsis":"Tests the operator's greater bit.","comment":"True when greater?"},
        "8265": {"comment":"Equal?"},
        "8268": {"comment":"Greater: true"},
        "8269": {"synopsis":"Tests the operator's less bit.","comment":"True when less?"},
        "8274": {"comment":"Less: true"},
        "8275": {"synopsis":"No outcome matched: C = 0.","comment":"False"},
        "8278": {"synopsis":"Truth masks of the relational operators, one byte per symbol $12-$17: bit 0 true when less,\nbit 1 when equal, bit 2 when greater. Read by $203B.","comment":"\"<\": less"},
        "8279": {"comment":"\"=\": equal"},
        "8280": {"comment":"\">\": greater"},
        "8281": {"comment":"\"<>\": less or greater"},
        "8282": {"comment":"\"<=\": less or equal"},
        "8283": {"comment":"\">=\": equal or greater"},
        "8284": {"synopsis":"Compares the top two items and pops both: numbers when NZ (COMPARE_IY: flags and H give the\nsign\nof next - top), strings when Z (falls into STR_COMPARE). Used by SELECT for CASE values and\nranges.","comment":"IY = the top"},
        "8288": {"comment":"Numbers: compare them"},
        "8291": {"synopsis":"Compares the top two strings (next with top) and pops both. A shorter string is smaller;\nstrings of the same length compare character by character (the length bytes are compared\nfirst).\nExit: H = 0 and Z when equal, H negative and M when next is smaller, H = 1 when next is\ngreater.\nRun: \"B\" < \"AA\" true, \"ABC\" < \"B\" false, \"AB\" < \"AC\" true, \"A\" < \"AB\" true, \"BA\" > \"AB\"\ntrue.","comment":"Top string"},
        "8294": {"comment":"At its length"},
        "8296": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "8299": {"comment":"Next string's length byte"},
        "8303": {"comment":"Next's length"},
        "8304": {"comment":"Shorter than top's?"},
        "8307": {"comment":"No: top's length"},
        "8308": {"synopsis":"A = the shorter length: pops both strings and sets up the byte compare.","comment":"C = next's length"},
        "8309": {"comment":"Past the next string"},
        "8311": {"comment":"Pop both"},
        "8314": {"comment":"Bytes to compare: the lengths, then A"},
        "8316": {"comment":"DE = next, HL = top, at the lengths"},
        "8318": {"synopsis":"Compares byte by byte while the bytes are equal.","comment":"Byte of next"},
        "8320": {"comment":"Against top's byte"},
        "8322": {"comment":"All compared?"},
        "8325": {"comment":"Same: go on"},
        "8327": {"synopsis":"H = the sign of the last pair's difference, next - top.","comment":"Top's last byte"},
        "8329": {"comment":"HL = next's byte"},
        "8332": {"comment":"Minus top's"},
        "8334": {"comment":"Equal"},
        "8335": {"comment":"Next smaller"},
        "8336": {"comment":"Next greater"},
        "8339": {"synopsis":"Parses a string expression without computing it (B bit 0 cleared); only ($0214) moves. The\nLD HL,$C0CB after it hides SET 0,B at $2096: EVAL_STRING's entry, inside that instruction.","comment":"Parse only"},
        "8341": {"comment":"Hides SET 0,B: EVAL_STRING ($2096)"},
        "8344": {"synopsis":"String expression with B bit 0 as set (computed when set): the terms (STR_TERM) joined by\n\"&\"\n(symbol $06), pushed as one string. EVAL_STRING ($2096, inside the instruction before)\nenters with SET 0,B. IY, HL' and DE' are kept. Run: \"AB\"&\"CD\" gave ABCD.","comment":"Keep IY, HL' and DE'"},
        "8350": {"comment":"First term"},
        "8353": {"synopsis":"Another \"&\"? Otherwise restores HL', DE' and IY and returns.","comment":"\"&\" follows?"},
        "8360": {"comment":"No: restore and return"},
        "8367": {"synopsis":"Joins the next term to the string so far. Computed: copies the left text below the right\none, writes the total length (error 1051 past 254 characters, STR_LEN_ERROR) and type 3\nunder it,\nthen moves the whole item up to end where the left string ended.","comment":"Past \"&\""},
        "8370": {"comment":"Next term"},
        "8373": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "8378": {"comment":"Top string (the new term)"},
        "8382": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "8385": {"comment":"Next string (the left part)"},
        "8388": {"comment":"DE = the left part's length"},
        "8392": {"comment":"Room for the left part (+2)"},
        "8395": {"comment":"Top string's length byte"},
        "8400": {"comment":"Plus top's length + 2"},
        "8404": {"comment":"BC = the left part's length"},
        "8405": {"comment":"Keep its length byte's address"},
        "8406": {"comment":"HL = the left part's last character"},
        "8407": {"comment":"Left part empty?"},
        "8409": {"comment":"A = the right part's length"},
        "8412": {"comment":"Copy the left text below the right"},
        "8414": {"synopsis":"Writes the joined length and type 3 under the copied text, then moves the item up over both\nstrings.","comment":"The left part's length byte"},
        "8415": {"comment":"Total length"},
        "8416": {"comment":"Its length byte"},
        "8418": {"comment":"Past 255: error 1051"},
        "8421": {"comment":"255: error 1051"},
        "8426": {"comment":"Type 3 below it"},
        "8430": {"comment":"C = the left part's length"},
        "8433": {"comment":"DE = below the left item"},
        "8437": {"comment":"End of the left item"},
        "8438": {"comment":"HL = the new item's last byte"},
        "8439": {"comment":"Length + 2 bytes"},
        "8442": {"comment":"Moved up to end there"},
        "8444": {"comment":"The new top"},
        "8450": {"comment":"More \"&\"?"},
        "8452": {"synopsis":"String term: a primary (STR_PRIMARY) followed by any number of slices \"(from:to)\". Computed,\neach\nslice replaces the top string by its part. Positions are clamped to 0-255; \"(n)\" is one\ncharacter, \"(:t)\" starts at 1, \"(f:)\" runs to the end; a part outside the string is empty.\nRun: \"HELLO\"(2:3) = EL, (4) = L, (:2) = HE, (3:) = LLO.","comment":"The primary"},
        "8455": {"synopsis":"Another slice \"(\" follows? Otherwise returns.","comment":"A slice?"},
        "8461": {"comment":"Past \"(\""},
        "8464": {"comment":"\":\" first?"},
        "8466": {"comment":"From 1"},
        "8470": {"comment":"From, clamped, in D"},
        "8473": {"comment":"E = from"},
        "8474": {"comment":"\":\" follows?"},
        "8476": {"comment":"No: to = from"},
        "8478": {"synopsis":"After \":\": the end position, 255 when \")\" follows at once.","comment":"Past \":\""},
        "8481": {"comment":"To the end"},
        "8483": {"comment":"\")\" at once?"},
        "8485": {"comment":"No: to, clamped, in D"},
        "8488": {"synopsis":"Expects \")\"; computed, cuts the top string to characters E..D.","comment":"Expect \")\""},
        "8493": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "8497": {"comment":"Top string"},
        "8501": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "8505": {"comment":"To past the end?"},
        "8508": {"comment":"No: keep to"},
        "8509": {"synopsis":"D = the last position (to, at most the length); empty when it is 0 or from is past the end.","comment":"D = the last position"},
        "8510": {"comment":"Zero: empty"},
        "8513": {"comment":"From past the end?"},
        "8515": {"comment":"Yes: empty"},
        "8517": {"comment":"From 0?"},
        "8521": {"comment":"Counts as 1"},
        "8522": {"synopsis":"Length of the part: to - from + 1; empty when to < from.","comment":"To - from"},
        "8524": {"comment":"Not negative: cut"},
        "8526": {"synopsis":"An empty part: a zero length written at the old string's end.","comment":"HL = the last character"},
        "8527": {"comment":"Length 0"},
        "8530": {"synopsis":"Moves characters from..to to the end of the old string's place.","comment":"New length"},
        "8532": {"comment":"HL = the last character"},
        "8533": {"comment":"DE = the destination, C = to"},
        "8536": {"comment":"HL = character \"to\""},
        "8537": {"comment":"Count"},
        "8538": {"comment":"Move the part up"},
        "8540": {"comment":"HL = below it"},
        "8541": {"synopsis":"Writes the new length and type 3, makes it the top and looks for another slice.","comment":"Length"},
        "8543": {"comment":"Type 3"},
        "8545": {"comment":"The new top"},
        "8549": {"comment":"Another slice?"},
        "8551": {"synopsis":"Evaluates a slice position (a numeric expression, B as set).\nExit: computed, D = the value clamped to 0-255 (popped); A = the symbol after it."},
        "8552": {"comment":"The position"},
        "8556": {"comment":"A = the next symbol"},
        "8559": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "8563": {"comment":"HL = the value"},
        "8567": {"comment":"D = 0 for a negative value"},
        "8571": {"comment":"D = 255 for 256 or more"},
        "8574": {"comment":"Else its low byte"},
        "8576": {"synopsis":"Pushes a string primary, computed (B bit 0 set; falls into STR_PRIMARY). Called at $07BD,\n$07E9,\n$0A1C and $0C9A.","comment":"Compute"},
        "8578": {"synopsis":"String primary from the current token, computed when B bit 0 is set; B is kept.\n1. A string name: a string function keyword (flags $0D) runs through KEYFN_CALL; an entry\n   with\n   flags 5 through FN_CALL_USER; anything else is a variable or array element\n(VAR_ADDRESS_NEXT), pushed\n   (STR_PUSH_AT). Parsing only, the name and its parenthesised list are skipped\n(ARGS_SKIP_NEXT).\n2. A string literal ($80) is pushed from its text; another token is error 20034 \"Type\n   mismatch\".","comment":"Keep B"},
        "8579": {"comment":"A string name?"},
        "8586": {"comment":"Computing? (B bit 0 into carry)"},
        "8588": {"comment":"No: skip it"},
        "8590": {"comment":"Find the name"},
        "8593": {"comment":"A = its flags"},
        "8596": {"comment":"A string function?"},
        "8600": {"comment":"Call it"},
        "8605": {"synopsis":"Not a string function: flags 5 go to FN_CALL_USER (FN_CALL_USER, a DEF function's call);\nothers are variables.","comment":"C = the flags"},
        "8606": {"comment":"Flags 5?"},
        "8610": {"comment":"Through FN_CALL_USER"},
        "8615": {"synopsis":"A string variable or array element: pushes its value.","comment":"Past the name; an array: HL = the element"},
        "8618": {"comment":"Push its value"},
        "8621": {"comment":"Carry: skip the next call"},
        "8622": {"synopsis":"Parsing only: skips the name and its parenthesised list.","comment":"Past the name and any ( )"},
        "8627": {"synopsis":"Not a name: a string literal ($80) is pushed when computed; other tokens are error 20034.","comment":"A string literal?"},
        "8629": {"comment":"No: error 20034"},
        "8632": {"comment":"Its text"},
        "8635": {"comment":"HL = the byte before its length"},
        "8636": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "8638": {"comment":"Push it"},
        "8642": {"comment":"Past the literal"},
        "8645": {"synopsis":"Pushes a string: HL + 1 holds its length, then its characters (for a string variable HL is\nthe maximum-length byte). Error 20040 \"Variable not initialised\" when the length is $FF, a\nvariable never assigned; memory is checked first (MEM_ENSURE_DE).","comment":"At the length"},
        "8647": {"comment":"$FF: never assigned?"},
        "8648": {"comment":"Yes: error 20040"},
        "8651": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "8656": {"comment":"Room for it (+2)"},
        "8661": {"comment":"HL = the last character"},
        "8662": {"comment":"The length byte too"},
        "8663": {"comment":"Below the top"},
        "8668": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "8670": {"comment":"HL = the new top"},
        "8671": {"comment":"Type 3"},
        "8673": {"synopsis":"Entry: sets ($0228) = HL, the new top (called at $0445).","comment":"The new top"},
        "8677": {"synopsis":"+ and - level: an optional sign, a term from the multiplicative level (EVAL_TERM; a \"-\"\nnegates\nit), then any + or - terms (NUM_ADD, NUM_SUB). HL', DE' and B are kept. Called by the\nrelation level and by many routines ($2361, $2596, $27CD, ...).","comment":"Keep HL' and DE'"},
        "8682": {"comment":"No sign: as \"+\""},
        "8684": {"comment":"Unary \"+\"?"},
        "8691": {"comment":"Unary \"-\"?"},
        "8695": {"comment":"E = \"-\""},
        "8696": {"synopsis":"Past the sign.","comment":"Past the sign"},
        "8699": {"synopsis":"The first term, negated after a \"-\".","comment":"B back"},
        "8700": {"comment":"First term"},
        "8703": {"comment":"Keep B"},
        "8704": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "8708": {"comment":"Was the leading sign \"-\" (symbol $0D)?"},
        "8711": {"comment":"Then negate the first term (NUM_NEGATE)"},
        "8714": {"synopsis":"Loop of the additive level: another \"+\" (symbol $0B) or \"-\" (symbol $0D) adds or subtracts\nthe next term; any other symbol ends the sum.","comment":"Symbol after the term"},
        "8717": {"comment":"\"+\"?"},
        "8721": {"comment":"\"-\"?"},
        "8725": {"comment":"No: the sum ends; restore BC, HL', DE'"},
        "8731": {"synopsis":"Reads the term after a \"+\" or \"-\" (operator kept in E) and, when computing, adds it\n(NUM_ADD) or subtracts it (NUM_SUB) from the value below it.","comment":"E = the operator"},
        "8732": {"comment":"Past the operator"},
        "8736": {"comment":"Next term (multiplicative level)"},
        "8740": {"comment":"Only parsing: no arithmetic"},
        "8744": {"comment":"\"+\"?"},
        "8747": {"comment":"Yes: next + top (flags kept, so the SUB call is skipped)"},
        "8750": {"comment":"No: next - top"},
        "8755": {"synopsis":"Multiplicative level of the numeric evaluator: a factor (EVAL_POWER), then any number of \"*\"\n(symbol $0A) or \"/\" (symbol $0F) and further factors, worked left to right with NUM_MUL /\nNUM_DIV when B bit 0 (compute) is set.\nEntry: current token at the term's start; B bit 0 = compute.\nExit: the term's value pushed (when computing); the current token is the first one after it.","comment":"First factor"},
        "8758": {"synopsis":"Loop of the multiplicative level: another \"*\" or \"/\" brings the next factor; any other\nsymbol returns.","comment":"Symbol after the factor"},
        "8761": {"comment":"\"*\"?"},
        "8765": {"comment":"\"/\"?"},
        "8767": {"comment":"Neither: the term ends"},
        "8768": {"synopsis":"Reads the factor after a \"*\" or \"/\" (operator kept in D) and, when computing, multiplies or\ndivides the value below it by it.","comment":"D = the operator"},
        "8769": {"comment":"Past the operator"},
        "8772": {"comment":"Next factor"},
        "8775": {"comment":"Only parsing: no arithmetic"},
        "8781": {"comment":"\"*\"?"},
        "8784": {"comment":"Yes: next * top (flags kept, so the DIV call is skipped)"},
        "8787": {"comment":"No: next / top"},
        "8794": {"synopsis":"Power level of the numeric evaluator: a primary (EVAL_PRIMARY), then any number of \"^\"\n(symbol $1B) and further primaries, worked left to right with segment 1's FP_POWER (byte\n$B0) when computing.\nEntry: current token at the factor's start; B bit 0 = compute.\nExit: the factor's value pushed (when computing).","comment":"First primary"},
        "8797": {"synopsis":"Loop of the power level: each \"^\" raises the value so far to the next primary; any other\nsymbol returns.","comment":"Symbol after the primary"},
        "8800": {"comment":"\"^\"?"},
        "8803": {"comment":"Past the \"^\""},
        "8806": {"comment":"The exponent"},
        "8809": {"comment":"Only parsing: no arithmetic"},
        "8815": {"comment":"Next raised to top"},
        "8816": {"comment":"(IS-BASIC call: FP_POWER, next ^ top)"},
        "8817": {"comment":"End of the call list"},
        "8822": {"synopsis":"Primary of the numeric evaluator, by the class of the current token in ($0202):\n1. Class 0, a symbol: it must be \"(\" (else error 20000 \"Not understood\"); the bracketed\n   expression is evaluated in full and \")\" expected.\n2. Class $20, a numeric name: found with segment 1's VAR_FIND_ANY (byte $8B); flags $0C is a\n   keyword function (KEYFN_CALL), flags $04 a defined function (FN_CALL_USER), anything else\na\n   variable or array element, whose 6-byte value is pushed (NUM_PUSH_VAR). When only\n   parsing, the name and any bracketed arguments are skipped.\n3. Class $C0, a numeric constant: the work item at $0595 is pushed (NUM_PUSH_WORK).\nAny other class is error 20040.\nEntry: B bit 0 = compute.\nExit: the value pushed (when computing), the next token read; BC and DE kept (the exit at\nEVAL_RESTORE is pushed as the return address)."},
        "8824": {"comment":"Every path returns through EVAL_RESTORE"},
        "8828": {"comment":"Token class"},
        "8831": {"comment":"A symbol?"},
        "8835": {"comment":"The symbol"},
        "8838": {"comment":"\"(\"?"},
        "8840": {"comment":"No: error 20000 \"Not understood\""},
        "8843": {"comment":"Past \"(\" and evaluate the whole expression"},
        "8846": {"comment":"Then expect \")\" and read on"},
        "8851": {"synopsis":"Primary that is not a symbol: a numeric name (class $20) is looked up here; others go on to\nPRIM_CONSTANT.","comment":"A numeric name?"},
        "8855": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "8857": {"comment":"No: skip the name and any bracketed arguments"},
        "8861": {"comment":"Look the name up: HL = its value field, C = its flags"},
        "8862": {"comment":"(IS-BASIC call: VAR_FIND_ANY)"},
        "8863": {"comment":"End of the call list"},
        "8864": {"comment":"The entry's flags"},
        "8865": {"comment":"$0C: a numeric keyword function?"},
        "8870": {"comment":"Call it"},
        "8872": {"synopsis":"A numeric name that is not a keyword function: flags $04 is a defined function, run by\nFN_CALL_USER\nwith B shifted right twice; others go on to PRIM_VARIABLE.","comment":"$04: a defined function?"},
        "8877": {"comment":"C = the flags"},
        "8878": {"comment":"B shifted right twice for FN_CALL_USER"},
        "8882": {"comment":"Run the function's definition"},
        "8885": {"synopsis":"A numeric variable: past its name, an array's subscripts are read (VAR_ADDRESS_NEXT,\nARRAY_ELEMENT) and\nthe 6-byte value at HL is pushed (NUM_PUSH_VAR).","comment":"C = the flags, B restored"},
        "8888": {"comment":"Past the name; an array's subscripts give the element"},
        "8891": {"comment":"Push the value (NUM_PUSH_VAR)"},
        "8894": {"synopsis":"A numeric constant (class $C0): pushes the work item at $0595 when computing and reads the\nnext token; any other class is error 20040.","comment":"A numeric constant?"},
        "8896": {"comment":"No: error 20040"},
        "8899": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "8901": {"comment":"Push the constant read into $0595"},
        "8904": {"comment":"Past the constant"},
        "8907": {"synopsis":"Common exit of EVAL_PRIMARY, pushed as its return address: restores BC and DE."},
        "8910": {"synopsis":"Calls a keyword function found by name. Past the name, B is shifted right one (its compute\nbit goes to carry); when computing, the function's routine is called: the entry's value\nfield holds the routine's address and a segment byte, 0 for a routine of this cartridge\n(jumped to with JP (HL) at JUMP_TO_HL), else the segment called through the RST 08h gate.\nWhen\nonly parsing, its bracketed arguments are skipped (ARGS_SKIP_PARENS).\nEntry: HL = the entry's value field; B bit 0 = compute.","comment":"Past the function's name"},
        "8913": {"comment":"Compute bit to carry; only parsing?"},
        "8917": {"comment":"DE = the routine's address"},
        "8921": {"comment":"A = its segment"},
        "8922": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "8923": {"comment":"Segment 0: in this cartridge?"},
        "8924": {"comment":"Yes: jump to it"},
        "8927": {"comment":"Call HL in segment A through the gate"},
        "8929": {"synopsis":"Reads the next token, then skips a bracketed argument list (ARGS_SKIP_PARENS).","comment":"Past the name"},
        "8932": {"synopsis":"When the current symbol is \"(\", skips a bracketed argument list without computing it: each\nargument is parsed as a string expression (it starts with a string name, class $40, or a\nstring literal, class $80) or as a numeric one; arguments are separated by \",\" (symbol $0C),\nsymbol $10 or the word TO (the text at $FB3D); \")\" ends the list and the next token is read.\nOtherwise it returns at once.\nEntry: current token.\nExit: the token after \")\".","comment":"Current symbol"},
        "8935": {"comment":"\"(\"?"},
        "8938": {"synopsis":"Loop over the arguments: reads the next token, passes over symbol $10, stops at \")\", else\nskips one argument.","comment":"Next token"},
        "8941": {"comment":"Symbol $10: passed over"},
        "8945": {"comment":"\")\": past it and done"},
        "8950": {"comment":"Token class"},
        "8953": {"comment":"A string name?"},
        "8957": {"comment":"A string literal?"},
        "8961": {"synopsis":"Skips a string argument (SKIP_STR_EXPR); Z then stops the numeric skip below.","comment":"Parse a string expression without computing"},
        "8964": {"comment":"Z: no numeric skip"},
        "8965": {"synopsis":"Skips a numeric argument (SKIP_NUM_EXPR, NZ), then looks at the separator after it.","comment":"Parse a numeric expression without computing"},
        "8968": {"comment":"Symbol after the argument"},
        "8971": {"comment":"\",\": another argument"},
        "8975": {"comment":"Symbol $10: another argument"},
        "8979": {"comment":"The word TO?"},
        "8982": {"comment":"Z when the current name is that word"},
        "8987": {"comment":"Else it must be \")\""},
        "8992": {"synopsis":"Pops two integer-form numbers for a bitwise operation: BC = the top item's word (+2/+3), the\ntop is popped (($0228) up 9), DE = the new top's word and HL = the address of its high byte\n(+3), where the caller writes the result back. Called for the bitwise operators BOR ($DF12)\nand BAND ($DF5E).","comment":"Top item"},
        "8997": {"comment":"BC = its integer word"},
        "9000": {"comment":"From +3 to the next item (+9)"},
        "9004": {"comment":"Top popped"},
        "9007": {"comment":"DE = the next item's word, HL at its +3"},
        "9013": {"synopsis":"Prints the top number without popping it: a space when it is not negative (where a \"-\" would\nbe), its text (NUM_TO_TEXT) and a space. Entry PRINT_NUM_AT ($2338) prints the item at HL.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, IY (HL, HL' and DE' kept).","comment":"The top item"},
        "9016": {"synopsis":"PRINT_NUMBER for the number item at HL (used at $D8C1 and $ED7E).","comment":"IY = the item"},
        "9019": {"comment":"Keep HL' and DE'"},
        "9023": {"comment":"Negative?"},
        "9026": {"comment":"No: a space in the sign's place"},
        "9032": {"comment":"Its text to $059E"},
        "9035": {"comment":"Print the counted text"},
        "9041": {"comment":"Trailing space"},
        "9052": {"synopsis":"Formats the top number (not popped) as counted text at $059E: length byte, then the\ncharacters from $059F. Entry NUM_TO_TEXT_AT ($2360) formats the item at IY. Steps:\n1. The item is copied to $05B2 and worked on there; zero gives \"0\".\n2. An integer is turned into float form; a negative number gets \"-\" and is made positive;\n   the mantissa is rounded to 10 digits (NUM_ROUND10).\n3. Trailing zero digits are dropped, then the layout is chosen (NTT_LAYOUT): plain digits\n   with a \".\" where needed, or one digit, \".\", the rest and \"E\" with the exponent (\"-\" and\n   two digits) for 1E10 and above or for a fraction that would need more than 10 digits\n   after the point. Numbers below 1 have no leading \"0\".\nExit: $059E = the length; IY = the item again.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The top item"},
        "9056": {"synopsis":"NUM_TO_TEXT for the number item at IY."},
        "9059": {"comment":"Keep the item's address"},
        "9060": {"comment":"Work on a copy at $05B2"},
        "9064": {"comment":"Copy its 9 bytes"},
        "9067": {"comment":"IY = the copy"},
        "9069": {"comment":"Text starts after the length byte"},
        "9072": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "9077": {"comment":"Yes: \"0\""},
        "9083": {"synopsis":"A number other than zero: float form, the sign, rounding.","comment":"Integer form to float form"},
        "9086": {"comment":"Negative?"},
        "9091": {"comment":"\"-\""},
        "9094": {"comment":"Then make it positive"},
        "9097": {"synopsis":"Rounds the mantissa to 10 digits before the digits are written.","comment":"Round to 10 digits"},
        "9100": {"comment":"From past the last digit position (13)"},
        "9102": {"synopsis":"Loop: steps B down from position 13 while the digit there is 0 and B is not below 4, leaving\nB at the last significant digit."},
        "9104": {"comment":"Down to the leading digit?"},
        "9108": {"comment":"Digit B"},
        "9111": {"comment":"Zero: try the one before"},
        "9113": {"synopsis":"Chooses the layout from the exponent byte E: D = E - $3B is the digit position the \".\" goes\nbefore, C the position where the digits stop. 1E10 and above, or a fraction needing more\nthan 10 digits after the point, takes the E form (carry set); 1 to 1E10 shows its integer\ndigits (padded with zeros); below 1 the digits start at position D, below the leading one,\nwhich writes the zeros after the point.","comment":"C = last significant digit's position"},
        "9114": {"comment":"Start at the leading digit"},
        "9116": {"comment":"E = exponent byte (positive now)"},
        "9120": {"comment":"D = position the \".\" goes before"},
        "9124": {"comment":"1E10 or more?"},
        "9128": {"comment":"1 or more?"},
        "9132": {"comment":"Below 1: E - C, carry if it underflows"},
        "9133": {"comment":"Too small: E form"},
        "9135": {"comment":"Over 10 digits after the point?"},
        "9137": {"comment":"Yes: E form"},
        "9139": {"comment":"Start at D (zeros after the point)"},
        "9142": {"synopsis":"Number from 1 to 1E10: when the digits stop before the point, they run on to it (zeros),\nwith no \".\"; otherwise up to the last digit.","comment":"Digits past the point?"},
        "9144": {"comment":"Yes: up to the last digit"},
        "9146": {"comment":"No: up to the point, padded with zeros"},
        "9147": {"comment":"NC: no exponent"},
        "9150": {"synopsis":"E form for 1E10 and above: carry set, then the shared setting below.","comment":"Carry: E form"},
        "9151": {"synopsis":"E form: the \".\" goes after the leading digit (before position 5).","comment":"\".\" before position 5"},
        "9153": {"synopsis":"Makes C the position after the last digit to write.","comment":"Stop after the last digit"},
        "9154": {"synopsis":"Writes the digits from position B to C - 1, with \".\" before position D; the layout's carry\n(E form) is kept on the stack.","comment":"Keep the E form flag"},
        "9156": {"synopsis":"Loop entry with A = B: a \".\" goes in when B reaches D.","comment":"Point before this digit?"},
        "9159": {"comment":"\".\""},
        "9162": {"synopsis":"Writes digit B as a character; positions below 4 (zeros after the point) are \"0\".","comment":"Below the leading digit?"},
        "9167": {"comment":"No: digit B, else 0"},
        "9170": {"comment":"As a character"},
        "9174": {"comment":"Next position"},
        "9176": {"comment":"Past the last?"},
        "9179": {"comment":"E form?"},
        "9182": {"comment":"\"E\""},
        "9185": {"comment":"Exponent = E - $40"},
        "9190": {"comment":"Negative: \"-\" and its size"},
        "9195": {"synopsis":"Writes the exponent A as two digits: B counts its tens.","comment":"B = tens, counted from -1"},
        "9197": {"synopsis":"Loop: subtracts 10 until it underflows, B counting the tens and C keeping the units."},
        "9198": {"comment":"C = what is left before this 10"},
        "9203": {"comment":"Tens digit"},
        "9208": {"comment":"A = \"0\" + units"},
        "9212": {"synopsis":"Ends the text: writes its length at $059E and restores IY to the item.","comment":"Length = end - $059F"},
        "9219": {"comment":"Into the length byte"},
        "9220": {"comment":"IY = the original item"},
        "9223": {"synopsis":"Pushes the 9-byte work item at $0595 (where a numeric constant is built) as a number on the\nvalue stack. Checks 12 bytes are free first (MEM_ENSURE_12).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Room for the item"},
        "9226": {"comment":"Below the current top"},
        "9231": {"comment":"Copy $0596-$059D downwards"},
        "9240": {"comment":"Type 2: a number"},
        "9242": {"comment":"The new top"},
        "9246": {"synopsis":"Reads a decimal number at ($0214) into the work item at $0595: optional sign, digits with at\nmost one \".\", then optionally \"E\" (either case), a sign and exponent digits. Up to 10\nsignificant digits are kept (leading zeros skipped, later digits dropped). A number of at\nmost 4 digits with no \".\" or exponent is made integer form; zero becomes integer 0. ($0214)\nis moved past the number. Error 1001 when the exponent is out of range. Uses D as flags (bit\n0 \".\" seen, 1 a significant digit seen, 2 negative, 3 negative exponent), E as the exponent\nbyte and B as the next digit position.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY = $0595.","comment":"The text"},
        "9249": {"comment":"Build into the work item"},
        "9253": {"comment":"Zero mantissa, exponent byte $3F"},
        "9256": {"comment":"Flags 0, exponent byte $3F"},
        "9259": {"comment":"First digit goes to position 4"},
        "9262": {"comment":"\"+\"?"},
        "9266": {"comment":"\"-\"?"},
        "9270": {"comment":"Negative"},
        "9272": {"synopsis":"Past the sign character."},
        "9273": {"synopsis":"Loop over the mantissa's characters: \".\", digits; anything else ends it.","comment":"Next character"},
        "9275": {"comment":"\".\"?"},
        "9279": {"comment":"Carry when not a digit"},
        "9282": {"comment":"Not a digit: the mantissa ends"},
        "9284": {"comment":"Digit value; zero?"},
        "9288": {"comment":"After a significant digit: kept"},
        "9292": {"comment":"Before the point: leading zero dropped"},
        "9296": {"comment":"After the point: exponent one lower"},
        "9299": {"synopsis":"A nonzero digit: marks that a significant digit has been seen.","comment":"Significant digits from here"},
        "9301": {"synopsis":"A kept digit: one before the point raises the exponent.","comment":"Before the point?"},
        "9305": {"comment":"Yes: one more integer digit"},
        "9306": {"synopsis":"Writes the digit at position B unless 10 digits are already kept, then moves B on."},
        "9307": {"comment":"Past the 10th digit?"},
        "9311": {"comment":"No: write it (DIGIT_PUT at IY)"},
        "9314": {"comment":"Next position"},
        "9317": {"synopsis":"A \".\": the first one is noted, a second one ends the number.","comment":"A second point?"},
        "9321": {"comment":"Point seen"},
        "9325": {"synopsis":"End of the mantissa: an \"E\" (either case) brings an exponent, otherwise TTN_NO_EXP.","comment":"Back on the character that ended it"},
        "9326": {"comment":"C = it in upper case"},
        "9330": {"comment":"\"E\"?"},
        "9334": {"comment":"Past the \"E\""},
        "9336": {"comment":"\"+\"?"},
        "9340": {"comment":"\"-\"?"},
        "9344": {"comment":"Negative exponent"},
        "9346": {"synopsis":"Past the exponent's sign."},
        "9347": {"synopsis":"Reads the exponent's digits into DE, keeping the flags and the exponent byte on the stack."},
        "9348": {"comment":"Exponent value 0"},
        "9351": {"synopsis":"Loop: value = value * 10 + digit while the low byte stays below 128."},
        "9352": {"comment":"A digit?"},
        "9355": {"comment":"No: the exponent ends"},
        "9360": {"comment":"Value times 10"},
        "9365": {"comment":"Plus the digit"},
        "9367": {"comment":"Below 128: next digit"},
        "9370": {"synopsis":"Raises error 1001: the exponent is out of range.","comment":"Error 1001"},
        "9374": {"synopsis":"End of the exponent: adds it (negated for \"-\") to the exponent byte from the digits; $7F or\nmore is error 1001."},
        "9375": {"comment":"Flags and the exponent byte back"},
        "9376": {"comment":"Negative exponent?"},
        "9382": {"synopsis":"Adds the exponent to the exponent byte and checks it is below $7F.","comment":"Plus the digits' exponent"},
        "9383": {"comment":"$7F or more?"},
        "9385": {"comment":"Yes: error 1001"},
        "9388": {"comment":"The exponent byte"},
        "9391": {"comment":"Past the number"},
        "9394": {"synopsis":"Finishes a float: negates it when a \"-\" led, then turns zero into integer 0 (zero test at\nZERO_TEST_IY).","comment":"Negative?"},
        "9399": {"comment":"Zero becomes integer 0"},
        "9405": {"synopsis":"No exponent: a number with no \".\" whose integer digits (at most 4) are all the digits kept\nis rebuilt in integer form; others stay float.","comment":"Past the number"},
        "9408": {"comment":"The exponent byte"},
        "9412": {"comment":"A point: stays float"},
        "9416": {"comment":"A = 4 + integer digits"},
        "9418": {"comment":"5 or more digits: stays float"},
        "9422": {"comment":"Every kept digit an integer digit?"},
        "9425": {"comment":"C = position past the last digit"},
        "9426": {"comment":"From the leading digit"},
        "9428": {"comment":"HL = 0 (no carry here)"},
        "9430": {"synopsis":"Loop: HL = HL * 10 + digit B for each kept digit."},
        "9431": {"comment":"All digits?"},
        "9434": {"comment":"Digit B"},
        "9438": {"comment":"HL times 10"},
        "9442": {"comment":"Plus the digit"},
        "9449": {"synopsis":"Stores HL (negated for a \"-\") as the integer form of the work item.","comment":"Negative?"},
        "9451": {"comment":"HL = -HL"},
        "9454": {"comment":"Integer form, 0"},
        "9457": {"comment":"The value"},
        "9464": {"synopsis":"Pops top and next and pushes next - top: negates the top and falls into NUM_ADD. AF kept."},
        "9465": {"comment":"Top item"},
        "9469": {"comment":"Negate it"},
        "9473": {"synopsis":"Pops two numbers and pushes their sum. Two integers are added as words while the sum fits;\notherwise both are made float, the one with the smaller exponent has its mantissa shifted\nright to align, and the mantissas are added in BCD (a negative one in ten's complement when\nthe signs differ), then the result is normalised. AF kept.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL, IY = the result."},
        "9474": {"comment":"Both integers? HL = top, BC = next, DE at next+3"},
        "9477": {"comment":"No: float add"},
        "9480": {"comment":"Word sum"},
        "9482": {"comment":"Overflow: float add"},
        "9485": {"synopsis":"Writes the integer result DE into the next item (HL = its +3), pops the top, restores AF and\nreturns. Shared by NUM_ADD, NUM_MUL and NUM_DIV.","comment":"HL = next+3, DE = the result"},
        "9489": {"comment":"Down to the next item's type byte"},
        "9491": {"comment":"Top popped"},
        "9496": {"synopsis":"Float addition: both items in float form, exponents aligned, mantissas added.","comment":"Top to float form"},
        "9499": {"comment":"Keep the top's address"},
        "9501": {"comment":"The next item"},
        "9506": {"comment":"Next to float form"},
        "9509": {"comment":"IY = top, the next on the stack"},
        "9511": {"comment":"Top's exponent"},
        "9517": {"comment":"Next's exponent"},
        "9522": {"comment":"Next's exponent minus top's"},
        "9523": {"comment":"Next not smaller: shift the top"},
        "9526": {"comment":"Next is smaller: IY = next"},
        "9529": {"comment":"Shift it right by the difference"},
        "9535": {"comment":"IY = top again"},
        "9537": {"comment":"Raise the next's exponent to match"},
        "9544": {"comment":"Z: no second shift"},
        "9545": {"synopsis":"Shifts the top's mantissa right by A digits when A is not 0, then adds the mantissas:\ndirectly for equal signs, else both turned to ten's complement form first.","comment":"Top's mantissa right A digits"},
        "9548": {"comment":"Signs differ?"},
        "9555": {"comment":"Same sign: add the mantissas"},
        "9558": {"comment":"IY = next"},
        "9560": {"comment":"Same sign: done"},
        "9562": {"comment":"Negative next to ten's complement"},
        "9565": {"comment":"IY = top"},
        "9567": {"comment":"Negative top to ten's complement"},
        "9570": {"comment":"Add them"},
        "9573": {"comment":"IY = next, the result"},
        "9575": {"comment":"Byte +7 not 0: the sum is negative"},
        "9579": {"comment":"Complement it back and make it negative"},
        "9582": {"synopsis":"Pops the top (the result is in the next item), normalises it and returns.","comment":"Drop the top's address"},
        "9583": {"comment":"Top popped"},
        "9587": {"synopsis":"Normalises the number at IY, restores AF and returns. Shared exit of NUM_ADD, NUM_MUL and\nNUM_DIV.","comment":"Normalise (NUM_NORMALISE at IY)"},
        "9592": {"synopsis":"Adds the top item's mantissa bytes +1..+7 into the next item's in BCD, starting with the\ncarry flag as it is. AF kept."},
        "9593": {"comment":"DE = top"},
        "9596": {"comment":"HL = next"},
        "9601": {"comment":"7 mantissa bytes"},
        "9603": {"synopsis":"Loop: next byte += top byte + carry, decimal adjusted."},
        "9613": {"synopsis":"Replaces the top float's mantissa by its ten's complement (MANT_TENS_COMP) only when the top\nnumber is negative; Z and nothing done otherwise.","comment":"Negative?"},
        "9617": {"synopsis":"Replaces the top float's mantissa bytes +1..+7 by their BCD ten's complement (0 - m). Entry\nMANT_COMP_AT ($2595) works on the item at IY."},
        "9621": {"synopsis":"MANT_TENS_COMP for the item at IY."},
        "9624": {"comment":"7 bytes, D = 0"},
        "9627": {"comment":"No borrow in"},
        "9628": {"synopsis":"Loop: byte = 0 - byte - borrow, decimal adjusted."},
        "9637": {"synopsis":"Pops two numbers and pushes their product. Two integers are multiplied as words when the\nproduct fits in 15 bits (sign applied after); otherwise both are made float: a zero factor\ngives integer 0, the exponents are added (below range gives 0, above it error 1002 \"Overflow\nin numeric expression\") and the mantissas are multiplied digit by digit with the product\ntable at $0016, then the result is normalised. AF kept.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL, IY = the result."},
        "9638": {"comment":"Both integers? HL = top, BC = next"},
        "9641": {"comment":"No: float multiply"},
        "9643": {"comment":"Sign of the product"},
        "9646": {"comment":"Top's size"},
        "9649": {"comment":"Swap: BC = it, HL = next"},
        "9652": {"comment":"Next's size"},
        "9655": {"comment":"DE = it, HL = next+3"},
        "9657": {"comment":"HL = BC * DE; carry on overflow"},
        "9662": {"comment":"$8000 or more?"},
        "9666": {"comment":"DE = next+3"},
        "9668": {"comment":"Negative product?"},
        "9670": {"comment":"HL = -HL"},
        "9673": {"comment":"Store it, pop the top"},
        "9676": {"synopsis":"Result 0: pops the top and makes the next item integer 0. Also the product of an\nunderflowing exponent.","comment":"The next item"},
        "9681": {"comment":"Top popped"},
        "9685": {"comment":"Integer 0"},
        "9690": {"synopsis":"The integer product did not fit: the kept values are dropped and the float multiply follows.","comment":"Drop next+3 and the sign"},
        "9692": {"synopsis":"Float multiply: zero tests, the result's sign and exponent, then the digit loops.","comment":"Keep the top"},
        "9694": {"comment":"The next item"},
        "9699": {"comment":"Float form; zero?"},
        "9705": {"comment":"IY = top"},
        "9707": {"comment":"Next is 0: the product is 0"},
        "9709": {"comment":"Float form; zero?"},
        "9715": {"comment":"Top is 0: the product is 0"},
        "9717": {"comment":"Next's exponent byte"},
        "9720": {"comment":"Top's exponent byte"},
        "9723": {"comment":"H bit 7 = the product's sign"},
        "9725": {"comment":"L = next's exponent"},
        "9729": {"comment":"Top's exponent"},
        "9734": {"comment":"Sum minus the bias"},
        "9738": {"comment":"Below range: the product is 0"},
        "9740": {"comment":"Above range: error 1002"},
        "9743": {"comment":"$7F would read as integer form"},
        "9744": {"comment":"Error 1002 too"},
        "9747": {"comment":"Keep the sign and exponent"},
        "9748": {"comment":"HL = top"},
        "9751": {"comment":"DE = top: the digits go down from there"},
        "9753": {"comment":"From the next's byte +7"},
        "9757": {"comment":"Next's mantissa to 14 digit bytes"},
        "9760": {"comment":"Keep where the top's digits start"},
        "9761": {"comment":"The next item is the stack's top now"},
        "9764": {"comment":"Clear its type byte and the top's +8"},
        "9768": {"comment":"Top's mantissa to 14 digit bytes"},
        "9771": {"comment":"BC = 2 digits below the top's leading one"},
        "9777": {"comment":"HL = the result row (top+1 up)"},
        "9781": {"comment":"DE = the next's digits, from the low end"},
        "9784": {"comment":"A' = the column counter, starts at 2"},
        "9788": {"comment":"C' = 12 digits of the next"},
        "9791": {"synopsis":"Outer loop, 12 passes: takes the next number's digit at DE (low end first), and unless it is\n0 runs 16 columns, adding digit x the top's digit at BC (from the table at $0016) and the\ncarry into the result row at HL. Each pass reaches one digit further down the top's\nmantissa.","comment":"HL = the result row's start"},
        "9793": {"comment":"Keep the top's digit pointer"},
        "9794": {"comment":"Digit of the next"},
        "9796": {"comment":"Keep the column counter"},
        "9799": {"comment":"Digit 0: nothing to add"},
        "9802": {"comment":"D' = digit * 10, the table row"},
        "9807": {"comment":"The product table at $C000"},
        "9809": {"comment":"Carry digit 0"},
        "9811": {"comment":"16 columns"},
        "9814": {"synopsis":"Inner loop over 16 columns: a counter between 0 and 11 means a column with a digit of the\ntop to multiply; outside it only the carry is added, and a negative counter with no carry\nends the pass.","comment":"Counter not negative?"},
        "9817": {"comment":"Carry left?"},
        "9819": {"comment":"No: the pass ends"},
        "9821": {"synopsis":"A column with no product: only the carry is added."},
        "9822": {"comment":"Product 0"},
        "9825": {"synopsis":"A column inside the top's 12 digits?","comment":"Past the top's digits?"},
        "9831": {"comment":"Top's digit"},
        "9833": {"comment":"Row + column + $0C: $000C + 10a + b"},
        "9837": {"comment":"Their product (BCD)"},
        "9838": {"synopsis":"Adds the product, the carry and the result digit at HL in BCD: the units are written back to\nHL, the tens become the carry.","comment":"Plus the carry"},
        "9841": {"comment":"Plus the result digit"},
        "9843": {"comment":"Units to the result digit, tens to A"},
        "9847": {"comment":"Next column"},
        "9850": {"comment":"Tens to the low nibble: the carry"},
        "9856": {"comment":"Column counter down"},
        "9859": {"synopsis":"End of a pass: the column counter starts one higher next time; moves to the next digit of\nthe next number and repeats 12 times, then packs the result into the next item with its sign\nand exponent and normalises it."},
        "9860": {"comment":"One column higher next pass"},
        "9862": {"comment":"Passes left"},
        "9865": {"comment":"Top's digits one step down, next's one up"},
        "9869": {"comment":"Result row's start"},
        "9870": {"comment":"Its top digit (row + 15)"},
        "9876": {"comment":"Pack 14 digits into the next's +7..+1"},
        "9879": {"comment":"IY = the next item, the result"},
        "9882": {"comment":"Sign and exponent"},
        "9887": {"comment":"The result's exponent byte"},
        "9890": {"comment":"Type 2: a number"},
        "9894": {"comment":"Normalise and return"},
        "9897": {"synopsis":"Packs 14 digit bytes, read downwards from DE, into 7 BCD bytes written downwards from HL\n(the first digit as the high nibble).\nExit: DE and HL past them.","comment":"7 bytes"},
        "9899": {"synopsis":"Loop: two digits rotated into the byte at HL."},
        "9911": {"synopsis":"Unpacks 7 BCD bytes, read downwards from HL, into 14 digit bytes written downwards from DE\n(high nibble first), clearing the source bytes.\nExit: DE and HL past them, A = 0.","comment":"7 bytes"},
        "9913": {"synopsis":"Loop: the byte's high digit, then its low digit, rotated out into A."},
        "9914": {"comment":"High digit out"},
        "9919": {"comment":"Low digit out, the byte left 0"},
        "9928": {"synopsis":"Pops top (the divisor) and next and pushes next / top. A zero divisor is error 3001; a zero\ndividend gives it back. Two integers are divided as words, and the quotient kept when\nnothing remains; otherwise both are made float and the mantissas divided by repeated BCD\nsubtraction into 12 quotient digits, the exponents subtracted, and the result normalised. AF\nkept.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL, IY = the result."},
        "9929": {"comment":"The divisor"},
        "9933": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "9936": {"comment":"Yes: error 3001"},
        "9939": {"comment":"The dividend"},
        "9944": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "9949": {"comment":"Yes: pop the top, the 0 is the result"},
        "9955": {"synopsis":"Both numbers nonzero: integer division when both are integers, else float division."},
        "9957": {"comment":"Both integers? HL = top, BC = next"},
        "9962": {"comment":"No: float division"},
        "9964": {"comment":"Sign of the quotient"},
        "9967": {"comment":"Divisor's size"},
        "9970": {"comment":"Swap: BC = it, HL = next"},
        "9973": {"comment":"Dividend's size"},
        "9976": {"comment":"DE = it, HL = next+3"},
        "9978": {"comment":"DE = DE / BC, HL = the remainder"},
        "9981": {"comment":"Anything left?"},
        "9984": {"comment":"Yes: float division"},
        "9986": {"comment":"HL = the quotient, DE = next+3"},
        "9988": {"comment":"Negative quotient?"},
        "9993": {"comment":"Store it, pop the top"},
        "9996": {"synopsis":"The integer division left a remainder: the sign is dropped and the float division follows."},
        "9997": {"synopsis":"Float division: both made float, a quotient item made at top - 9, then 12 digits found by\nsubtracting the divisor's mantissa from the dividend's as many times as it goes.","comment":"Dividend (IY = next) to float"},
        "10000": {"comment":"Keep its address"},
        "10006": {"comment":"Divisor to float"},
        "10009": {"comment":"L = divisor's exponent"},
        "10012": {"comment":"H = dividend's exponent"},
        "10015": {"comment":"Exponents kept, HL = next"},
        "10017": {"comment":"IY = a new item below the top"},
        "10022": {"comment":"The quotient, integer 0 for now"},
        "10025": {"comment":"First quotient digit at position 4"},
        "10027": {"synopsis":"Per quotient digit: sets up the dividend (DE'), divisor (HL) and a scratch item at top - 18\n(HL').","comment":"HL = divisor"},
        "10031": {"comment":"BC' = -9"},
        "10039": {"comment":"DE' = dividend (top + 9)"},
        "10043": {"comment":"HL' = scratch, top - 18"},
        "10045": {"synopsis":"Subtracts the divisor's mantissa from the dividend's into the scratch item; when it does not\ngo (borrow), the digit is done.","comment":"7 bytes, no borrow in"},
        "10048": {"synopsis":"Loop: scratch byte = dividend byte - divisor byte - borrow, decimal adjusted."},
        "10049": {"comment":"Dividend byte"},
        "10052": {"comment":"Minus the divisor byte"},
        "10059": {"comment":"Borrow out of the top byte?"},
        "10061": {"comment":"Yes: it did not go"},
        "10064": {"comment":"Quotient digit B"},
        "10067": {"comment":"Plus 1"},
        "10071": {"comment":"HL = divisor again"},
        "10075": {"comment":"The difference is the new dividend"},
        "10080": {"comment":"Subtract again"},
        "10082": {"synopsis":"The digit is done: the dividend's mantissa is shifted one digit left and the next quotient\ndigit is worked, up to position 15; then the quotient is copied into the next item, the top\npopped, the exponent set to next - top + $40 (underflow gives 0) and the sign applied.","comment":"IY = the dividend"},
        "10084": {"comment":"Its mantissa one digit left"},
        "10087": {"comment":"IY = the quotient"},
        "10090": {"comment":"Next quotient digit"},
        "10092": {"comment":"All 12?"},
        "10097": {"comment":"The quotient's byte +7"},
        "10102": {"comment":"Copy it over the next item"},
        "10107": {"comment":"IY = the next item"},
        "10109": {"comment":"Top popped"},
        "10113": {"comment":"The two exponent bytes"},
        "10114": {"comment":"Sign of the quotient"},
        "10117": {"comment":"Signs off"},
        "10121": {"comment":"Dividend's minus divisor's"},
        "10123": {"comment":"Plus the bias"},
        "10128": {"comment":"Out of range (minus): integer 0"},
        "10132": {"comment":"Negative quotient?"},
        "10134": {"comment":"Make it negative"},
        "10137": {"comment":"Normalise and return"},
        "10140": {"synopsis":"Writes BCD digit A at mantissa position B of the top number. Positions count from 4 (the\nleading digit, +6 high nibble) down the mantissa: byte +8 - B/2, an odd B the low nibble.\nEntry DIGIT_PUT_AT ($27A0) works on the item at IY. BC and HL kept.","comment":"The top item"},
        "10144": {"synopsis":"DIGIT_PUT for the item at IY."},
        "10146": {"comment":"HL = digit B's byte, C = A, carry if odd"},
        "10149": {"comment":"Odd: keep the high nibble"},
        "10153": {"comment":"Even: the digit to the high nibble"},
        "10159": {"comment":"Keep the low nibble"},
        "10162": {"synopsis":"Merges the digit into the byte at HL, keeping the other nibble (mask B)."},
        "10167": {"synopsis":"A = the BCD digit at mantissa position B of the top number (positions as for DIGIT_PUT).\nEntry DIGIT_GET_AT ($27BB) reads the item at IY. BC and HL kept.","comment":"The top item"},
        "10171": {"synopsis":"DIGIT_GET for the item at IY."},
        "10173": {"comment":"A = digit B's byte, carry if odd"},
        "10176": {"comment":"Odd: the low nibble"},
        "10178": {"comment":"Even: the high nibble down"},
        "10183": {"synopsis":"Keeps the low nibble: the digit."},
        "10185": {"synopsis":"Common exit of DIGIT_PUT and DIGIT_GET: restores BC and HL."},
        "10188": {"synopsis":"HL = the address of the byte holding digit position B in the item at IY (IY + 8 - B/2);\ncarry = B odd (the low nibble); C = A on entry; A = the byte.\nChanges: B (halved)."},
        "10191": {"comment":"Carry = B odd"},
        "10194": {"comment":"Byte offset 8 - B/2"},
        "10202": {"comment":"C = the caller's A"},
        "10205": {"synopsis":"Rounds the number at IY to 10 digits: a guard byte (+1) of $50 or more adds 1 to the digits\nabove it (MANT_ROUND_UP); the guard byte is cleared and the number normalised. An integer is\nleft\nalone. HL kept.","comment":"Integer form?"},
        "10215": {"comment":"Guard byte"},
        "10217": {"comment":"$50 or more?"},
        "10219": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "10221": {"comment":"Yes: round up"},
        "10224": {"comment":"Normalise"},
        "10229": {"synopsis":"Reads the next token, evaluates a numeric expression and pops it as a 16-bit integer into HL\n(falls into the LD A,$F6 / SCF entries below). The LD A,$F6 hides NUM_POP_INT at $27F9: OR\n$37 there clears carry, so the number already on top is popped without evaluating.","comment":"Past the current token"},
        "10232": {"comment":"$27F9: OR $37, carry clear (NUM_POP_INT)"},
        "10234": {"synopsis":"Evaluates a numeric expression from the current token and pops it into HL as a 16-bit\ninteger: sets carry and goes on as POP_INT_CF.","comment":"Carry: evaluate first"},
        "10235": {"synopsis":"Pops the top number into HL as a 16-bit integer (a float truncated toward zero; error 1000\n\"Unexpected value given\" for 6 or more integer digits); with carry set it first evaluates a\nnumeric expression (EVAL_NUMERIC). BC and DE kept."},
        "10237": {"comment":"Carry: evaluate the expression"},
        "10240": {"comment":"The top item; IY keeps it after the pop"},
        "10246": {"comment":"DE = the integer form's word at +2/+3"},
        "10251": {"comment":"To byte +8: $7F or sign and exponent"},
        "10256": {"comment":"Pop the item (its bytes stay where they are)"},
        "10260": {"comment":"HL = the word, for the integer form"},
        "10261": {"comment":"Integer form? HL is the value"},
        "10265": {"comment":"Keep the sign"},
        "10266": {"comment":"Exponent alone"},
        "10268": {"comment":"HL = 0 (carry is clear here)"},
        "10270": {"comment":"Six or more integer digits?"},
        "10272": {"comment":"Error 1000: Unexpected value given"},
        "10275": {"comment":"Below 1? Then the value is 0"},
        "10279": {"comment":"C = past the last integer digit's position"},
        "10282": {"comment":"From the leading digit (position 4)"},
        "10284": {"comment":"D = 0 for the digit add"},
        "10285": {"synopsis":"Loop: HL = HL * 10 + the digit at position B, up to position C.","comment":"HL * 10"},
        "10288": {"comment":"DIGIT_GET at the popped item (IY)"},
        "10291": {"comment":"Add the digit"},
        "10294": {"comment":"Last integer digit done?"},
        "10298": {"comment":"Sign bit to carry"},
        "10300": {"comment":"Negative: HL = -HL (NEG_HL)"},
        "10303": {"comment":"Hides POP AF at $2840, the entry for a value below 1"},
        "10305": {"synopsis":"Common exit of NUM_POP_INT: restores DE and BC."},
        "10308": {"synopsis":"Reads the next token, evaluates a numeric expression and returns its value as a byte.\nThe LD A,$F6 hides OR $37 at $2848: that entry clears carry, so the number already on the\nstack is popped without evaluating anything. Falls into BYTE_ARG_EVAL.\nExit: A = the low byte of the integer (-256 to 255 accepted); the number is popped.\nChanges: AF; error 1000 for any other value.","comment":"TOKEN_NEXT"},
        "10311": {"comment":"Hides OR $37 at $2848: NC, pop without evaluating"},
        "10313": {"synopsis":"Evaluates a numeric expression from the current token, pops it as an integer and returns\nits low byte in A. The integer must be -256 to 255 (high byte $00 or $FF), else error 1000.\nExit: A = the byte.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Carry: evaluate first"},
        "10315": {"comment":"Inside NUM_POP_INT: EVAL_NUMERIC when carry, then pop HL"},
        "10318": {"comment":"High byte $FF?"},
        "10321": {"comment":"High byte not 0: error 1000 (Unexpected value given)"},
        "10325": {"synopsis":"A = the low byte; HL restored."},
        "10328": {"comment":"Not reached by any jump or call in this ROM"},
        "10329": {"synopsis":"Adds 1 (BCD) to the mantissa byte after HL and carries upward through six bytes.\nEntry: HL = the item's guard byte (+1): the add starts at +2.\nExit: NC once a byte\ntakes the carry.\nChanges: AF, B, HL."},
        "10331": {"synopsis":"Loop: next byte up, add the carry."},
        "10333": {"comment":"Add 1 in decimal"},
        "10337": {"comment":"No carry out: done"},
        "10341": {"synopsis":"Converts the top number from integer form to BCD float form; a float is left as it is.\n1. Keeps the word, clears the item (ITEM_ZERO_IY) and puts H OR L at +8: zero stays a\nzero mantissa with exponent byte 0.\n2. Takes the word's magnitude and shifts it left past its leading 1 bit, with a 1 put in\nbelow as an end marker.\n3. For every remaining bit the BCD bytes from +2 up are doubled with the bit added (ADC A,A\nthen DAA), a byte added when the top one carries; the end marker leaves HL zero.\n4. The exponent byte is $49 with the sign, then NORMALISE_IY shifts the digits up.\nChanges: AF, DE, IY; ($0DBB) = the item's +1.","comment":"Top item"},
        "10345": {"synopsis":"As NUM_TO_FLOAT for the item at IY."},
        "10348": {"comment":"Already float? Nothing to do"},
        "10355": {"comment":"HL = the item's +1"},
        "10357": {"comment":"Kept: where the BCD bytes start, less one"},
        "10361": {"comment":"DE = the integer"},
        "10365": {"comment":"Clear the item to integer 0, HL kept"},
        "10368": {"comment":"Zero? Exponent byte 0 and done"},
        "10375": {"comment":"Keep the sign (H)"},
        "10376": {"comment":"HL = its magnitude"},
        "10379": {"comment":"Shift a 1 in at the bottom"},
        "10380": {"synopsis":"Loop: shift left until the leading 1 bit is out in carry."},
        "10384": {"comment":"One BCD byte in use so far"},
        "10388": {"synopsis":"The top BCD byte overflowed: one more byte, which takes the carry."},
        "10390": {"comment":"Hides LD B,C at $2897: B = the byte count"},
        "10392": {"synopsis":"Loop: double one BCD byte and add the carry in."},
        "10394": {"comment":"Byte * 2 + carry"},
        "10395": {"comment":"Back to decimal"},
        "10399": {"comment":"Carry out of the top byte? Use one more"},
        "10401": {"comment":"Next bit to carry"},
        "10403": {"synopsis":"Next bit is in carry; HL zero (only the end marker left) ends it.","comment":"Back to the bottom BCD byte"},
        "10407": {"comment":"Bits left: double again"},
        "10409": {"comment":"The sign"},
        "10412": {"comment":"Exponent 10^9 for the digit at +6 high"},
        "10417": {"comment":"NORMALISE_IY: leading zeros shifted out"},
        "10420": {"synopsis":"Restores BC and HL."},
        "10423": {"synopsis":"Copies a 9-byte number item from HL to DE (LDIR).\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "10429": {"synopsis":"Pushes the 6-byte numeric variable at HL as a number item: its bytes +0..+4 become the\nitem's +2..+6, +5 its +8, and +1/+7 are zero.\nEntry: HL = the variable.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.\nError 5000 when there is no room; error 20040 for an integer form whose +4 is not 0."},
        "10433": {"comment":"MEM_ENSURE_12"},
        "10436": {"comment":"Integer form?"},
        "10443": {"comment":"Its byte +4 must be 0"},
        "10447": {"comment":"Error 20040"},
        "10450": {"synopsis":"Drops the second copy of HL and builds the item."},
        "10451": {"synopsis":"As NUM_PUSH_VAR without the memory and integer-form checks.\nEntry: HL = the variable.","comment":"To the variable's last byte"},
        "10455": {"comment":"DE = the new item's +8"},
        "10460": {"comment":"Exponent byte to +8"},
        "10462": {"comment":"+7 = 0"},
        "10465": {"comment":"The five value bytes to +6..+2"},
        "10470": {"comment":"HL = the item's +1"},
        "10471": {"comment":"+1 = 0"},
        "10473": {"comment":"Type 2: a number"},
        "10475": {"comment":"New top of stack"},
        "10479": {"synopsis":"Pushes HL as an integer item. Checks for room first (error 5000), then returns through\nSTACK_TOP_IY, which stores IY as the new stack top.\nEntry: HL = the value.\nChanges: AF, DE, IY."},
        "10480": {"comment":"MEM_ENSURE_12"},
        "10483": {"comment":"Return through STACK_TOP_IY (($0228) = IY); HL back"},
        "10487": {"comment":"The current top"},
        "10491": {"synopsis":"Builds an integer item of HL 9 bytes below IY and leaves IY on it; the caller stores IY in\n($0228). No memory check.","comment":"9 bytes below it"},
        "10496": {"comment":"Integer 0 there"},
        "10499": {"comment":"The value at +2/+3"},
        "10506": {"synopsis":"Rounds the top number to ten digits, stores it in the 6-byte numeric variable at HL and\npops it (returns through ITEM_DROP).\nEntry: HL = the variable.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"Return through ITEM_DROP"},
        "10510": {"synopsis":"As NUM_POP_VAR but the number stays on the stack (rounded in place)."},
        "10511": {"comment":"The top item"},
        "10515": {"comment":"Round to ten digits (NUM_ROUND10)"},
        "10518": {"comment":"From its +2"},
        "10523": {"comment":"DE = the variable"},
        "10524": {"comment":"+2..+6 to the variable's +0..+4"},
        "10529": {"comment":"Skip the overflow byte +7"},
        "10530": {"comment":"+8 to the variable's +5"},
        "10533": {"synopsis":"Pops the top string into the string variable at HL (byte 0 its maximum length, then the\nlength and the characters); returns through ITEM_DROP. Error 1106 when it is longer.\nEntry: HL = the variable.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Return through ITEM_DROP"},
        "10537": {"synopsis":"As STR_POP_VAR but the string stays on the stack.","comment":"C = the variable's maximum length"},
        "10539": {"comment":"DE = the string's length byte"},
        "10545": {"comment":"Shorter than the maximum?"},
        "10548": {"comment":"Longer: error 1106"},
        "10551": {"synopsis":"Copies the length byte and the characters."},
        "10554": {"comment":"Length + 1 bytes"},
        "10559": {"synopsis":"Normalises the top number.\n1. A zero mantissa becomes integer 0; an integer is left alone.\n2. A non-zero overflow byte (+7) is shifted down one digit and the exponent raised; error\n1002 (Overflow in numeric expression) when it is already $7E.\n3. Otherwise, while the leading digit (+6 high) is 0, the mantissa moves up a digit and the\nexponent falls; when the exponent runs out the item becomes integer 0 (falls into\nITEM_ZERO_IY).\nChanges: AF, B, HL, IY.","comment":"Top item"},
        "10563": {"synopsis":"As NUM_NORMALISE for the item at IY.","comment":"ZERO_TEST_IY: zero becomes integer 0"},
        "10566": {"comment":"Integer form? Nothing to do"},
        "10572": {"comment":"Overflow byte in use?"},
        "10578": {"comment":"Shift one digit down"},
        "10583": {"comment":"Exponent already the largest?"},
        "10590": {"comment":"Error 1002: Overflow in numeric expression"},
        "10593": {"comment":"Exponent + 1"},
        "10597": {"synopsis":"Loop: leading digit 0? Shift up one digit and lower the exponent.","comment":"Leading digit present?"},
        "10603": {"comment":"Digits up one place (MANT_SHL_IY)"},
        "10606": {"comment":"Exponent before the decrement"},
        "10612": {"comment":"Exponent left? Go on"},
        "10616": {"comment":"Underflow; hides LD IY,($0228) at NUM_SET_ZERO (NUM_SET_ZERO)"},
        "10617": {"synopsis":"Overwrites the top item with integer 0. Hidden in LD A,$FD at $2978 (FD 2A 28 02 is\nLD IY,($0228) from here); falls into ITEM_ZERO_IY.\nChanges: IY."},
        "10621": {"synopsis":"Writes integer 0 into the item at IY: type 2, seven zero bytes, $7F at +8.\nChanges: nothing else (HL, BC and the flags kept)."},
        "10626": {"comment":"Type 2: a number"},
        "10629": {"comment":"+1..+7 cleared"},
        "10631": {"synopsis":"Loop: clear one byte."},
        "10636": {"comment":"+8 = $7F: integer form"},
        "10641": {"synopsis":"Sign of the top number, not popped: A = $80 and NZ when negative, A = 0 and Z otherwise.\nChanges: AF, IY."},
        "10645": {"synopsis":"As NUM_SIGN for the item at IY."},
        "10648": {"comment":"Float: the sign is bit 7 of +8"},
        "10652": {"comment":"Integer: bit 7 of the word's high byte"},
        "10655": {"synopsis":"A = the sign bit; Z when positive."},
        "10658": {"synopsis":"When the item at IY is negative: replaces its mantissa by its ten's complement and makes\nthe sign positive (used by NUM_ADD on its float operands).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"Positive? Nothing to do"},
        "10662": {"synopsis":"Ten's complement of IY's mantissa (MANT_COMP_AT), then falls into NEGATE_IY."},
        "10665": {"synopsis":"Negates the item at IY: an integer becomes 0 - n, a float has its sign bit flipped.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"Float?"},
        "10675": {"comment":"To the integer's word"},
        "10681": {"comment":"NEG_HL"},
        "10684": {"comment":"Store it back"},
        "10689": {"synopsis":"Flips bit 7 of the exponent byte."},
        "10695": {"synopsis":"Makes the top number non-negative: NUM_NEGATE when NUM_SIGN says negative.\nChanges: AF, DE,\nHL, IY."},
        "10698": {"comment":"Not negative: done"},
        "10699": {"synopsis":"Negates the top number in place (NEGATE_IY).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IY."},
        "10705": {"synopsis":"Z when the top number is zero (bytes +1..+7 all 0, either form); then rewrites it as\ninteger 0. NZ otherwise.\nChanges: AF, B, IY."},
        "10709": {"synopsis":"As NUM_ZERO_TEST for the item at IY."},
        "10713": {"comment":"Seven bytes: +1..+7"},
        "10716": {"synopsis":"Loop: OR the bytes together; stop at the first non-zero one."},
        "10722": {"synopsis":"Not zero: return NZ; zero: ITEM_ZERO_IY keeps Z."},
        "10724": {"comment":"Rewrite as integer 0"},
        "10727": {"synopsis":"Pops the top two numbers and compares the second with the top.\n1. Both integers: HL = second - top (the sign flag does not allow for overflow).\n2. Otherwise both become floats: the signs, then the exponents (both swapped when both\nare negative), then the digits from +7 down, a nibble at a time.\nExit: Z equal; M second smaller; otherwise P with H = 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"IY = top, IY + 9 = the second"},
        "10731": {"synopsis":"As NUM_COMPARE for the item at IY and the one above it."},
        "10733": {"comment":"Top an integer?"},
        "10738": {"comment":"Second an integer?"},
        "10743": {"comment":"HL = the second's word"},
        "10749": {"comment":"BC = the top's word"},
        "10755": {"comment":"Pop both items"},
        "10764": {"comment":"HL = second - top"},
        "10769": {"synopsis":"Both as floats, then compare sign, exponent and digits.","comment":"Top to float (TO_FLOAT_IY)"},
        "10772": {"comment":"To the second item"},
        "10777": {"comment":"Second to float"},
        "10780": {"comment":"HL = the second; DE = the top's +8"},
        "10786": {"comment":"Pop both"},
        "10790": {"comment":"The second's +8"},
        "10791": {"comment":"Its sign as $40 or 0"},
        "10796": {"comment":"The top's sign the same way"},
        "10800": {"comment":"Signs differ? A gives the answer"},
        "10803": {"comment":"Both positive?"},
        "10806": {"comment":"Both negative: swap, the larger magnitude is smaller"},
        "10807": {"synopsis":"Compares the exponents (bits 0-6)."},
        "10814": {"comment":"Exponents differ? That decides"},
        "10817": {"comment":"Seven mantissa bytes, +7 down to +1"},
        "10819": {"synopsis":"Loop: compare the high digits, then the low digits, of one byte."},
        "10821": {"comment":"High digit, halved to keep the sign"},
        "10830": {"comment":"High digits differ?"},
        "10833": {"comment":"Low digit"},
        "10840": {"comment":"Low digits differ?"},
        "10845": {"synopsis":"H = the difference."},
        "10846": {"synopsis":"Z equal, M smaller; otherwise H = 1 and P.","comment":"Equal"},
        "10847": {"comment":"Second smaller"},
        "10848": {"comment":"Second larger: H = 1"},
        "10851": {"synopsis":"Overwrites the top item with a zero mantissa and exponent byte $3F, a float ready for\ndigits.\nChanges: IY."},
        "10855": {"synopsis":"As NUM_SET_ZERO_FLT for the item at IY (the number reader's $0595).","comment":"Integer 0 first (ITEM_ZERO_IY)"},
        "10858": {"comment":"Then float form, exponent $3F"},
        "10863": {"synopsis":"Overwrites the top item with integer 1.\nChanges: IY."},
        "10870": {"comment":"Word = 1"},
        "10875": {"synopsis":"Overwrites the top item with 1.0 in float form: exponent $40, digit 1 at +6 high.\nChanges: IY."},
        "10882": {"comment":"Exponent 10^0, positive"},
        "10886": {"comment":"Leading digit 1"},
        "10891": {"synopsis":"Pushes a copy of the top item: 9 bytes, or for a string (type 3) its length + 2.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "10894": {"comment":"DE = just below the top"},
        "10897": {"comment":"The type"},
        "10898": {"comment":"A number: 8 bytes after the type"},
        "10901": {"comment":"A string?"},
        "10905": {"comment":"Its length + 1 after the type"},
        "10909": {"synopsis":"Copies the item downward from its last byte.","comment":"HL = the item's last byte"},
        "10910": {"comment":"The whole item"},
        "10913": {"comment":"DE = the copy's type byte"},
        "10914": {"comment":"New top of stack"},
        "10919": {"synopsis":"Shifts the top number's mantissa (+1 to +7) up one decimal digit; 0 comes in at +1's low\ndigit, +7's high digit is lost.\nChanges: AF, B, HL, IY."},
        "10923": {"synopsis":"As MANT_SHIFT_LEFT for the item at IY."},
        "10926": {"comment":"Seven bytes, from +1 up"},
        "10928": {"comment":"0 comes in"},
        "10929": {"synopsis":"Loop: RLD moves one digit up into the next byte."},
        "10935": {"synopsis":"Shifts the top number's mantissa (+7 down to +1) right by A decimal digits; the exponent\nis not changed.\nEntry: A = the digit count (1 or more).\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL, IY."},
        "10939": {"synopsis":"As MANT_SHIFT_RIGHT for the item at IY."},
        "10943": {"comment":"HL = DE = the item's +7"},
        "10949": {"comment":"C = the digit count"},
        "10950": {"synopsis":"Loop: one digit per pass, from +7 down."},
        "10952": {"comment":"0 comes in at the top"},
        "10953": {"synopsis":"Loop: RRD moves one digit down into the next byte."},
        "10958": {"comment":"Back to +7"},
        "10960": {"comment":"More digits?"},
        "10965": {"synopsis":"Walks every program line; for each whose keyword (byte +5) is $0D or $0E (DEF) or $23\n(HANDLER) it points ($0214) after it, reads the name and has segment 1's VAR_DECLARE\ndeclare it, with ($0216) on the line. Ends at a zero length byte.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL; ($0214), ($0216).","comment":"The program's first line"},
        "10968": {"comment":"BC = 5: the keyword's offset"},
        "10971": {"synopsis":"Loop: one program line.","comment":"Length 0: the program's end"},
        "10974": {"comment":"Current line"},
        "10977": {"comment":"Its keyword"},
        "10979": {"comment":"DEF?"},
        "10983": {"comment":"DEF (the second form)?"},
        "10987": {"comment":"HANDLER?"},
        "10991": {"synopsis":"Reads the name after the keyword and declares it.","comment":"Read from after the keyword"},
        "10995": {"comment":"TOKEN_NEXT: the name"},
        "10999": {"comment":"Segment 1's VAR_DECLARE"},
        "11000": {"comment":"VAR_DECLARE: declare the name here"},
        "11003": {"synopsis":"Steps to the next line by its length byte.","comment":"Back to the line's start"},
        "11012": {"synopsis":"DIM statement (the keyword table gives this address): once per line (LINE_MARK_ONCE),\ndeclares each array of the list, numeric or string, with one or two bounds, and gives every\nelement its initial value (strings 132 characters long at most).\nErrors: 20041 (Identifier declared twice) for a name already in this scope, 2001 for a\nname without bounds, 20000 (Not understood) after the list.","comment":"Line done before? Nothing to do"},
        "11016": {"synopsis":"Loop: one name of the list; anything but a name ends the statement.","comment":"A name? A = its class"},
        "11021": {"comment":"Segment 1's VAR_SCOPE_TEST"},
        "11022": {"comment":"VAR_SCOPE_TEST: NC when already in this scope"},
        "11024": {"comment":"Already here: error 20041 (Identifier declared twice)"},
        "11029": {"comment":"Class $20 -> 0 (numeric), $40 -> 1 (string)"},
        "11033": {"comment":"Create it with its bounds; HL = elements"},
        "11036": {"comment":"No bounds: error 2001"},
        "11039": {"synopsis":"Loop: one initial value per element."},
        "11041": {"comment":"Numeric?"},
        "11045": {"comment":"Strings of 132 characters at most"},
        "11047": {"comment":"Segment 1's VAR_INIT_STR"},
        "11048": {"comment":"VAR_INIT_STR: a string of C characters"},
        "11052": {"synopsis":"A numeric element's initial value.","comment":"Segment 1's VAR_INIT_NUM"},
        "11053": {"comment":"VAR_INIT_NUM: a numeric value"},
        "11055": {"synopsis":"Counts the elements down."},
        "11061": {"comment":"Comma: next name; else the statement ends"},
        "11066": {"synopsis":"STRING statement (the keyword table gives this address): once per line, declares each\nstring name of the list, an array when bounds follow. \"*n\" after STRING sets the default\nmaximum length, \"*n\" after a name its own; 132 without one.\nErrors: 20041 for a name already in this scope, 1051 for a length outside 1-254,\n20000 after the list.","comment":"Line done before? Nothing to do"},
        "11070": {"comment":"Default maximum length 132"},
        "11072": {"comment":"\"*n\" here sets the default; C = the length"},
        "11075": {"synopsis":"Loop: one name of the list; a non-string name ends the statement.","comment":"A string name?"},
        "11079": {"comment":"Keep the default length"},
        "11080": {"comment":"Segment 1's VAR_SCOPE_TEST"},
        "11081": {"comment":"VAR_SCOPE_TEST: NC when already in this scope"},
        "11083": {"comment":"Already here: error 20041"},
        "11086": {"comment":"Create a string name; HL = elements"},
        "11091": {"comment":"DE = the element count"},
        "11092": {"comment":"L = the default length"},
        "11094": {"comment":"Its own \"*n\"; C = the length"},
        "11097": {"comment":"HL = the element count"},
        "11098": {"synopsis":"Loop: one string value of C characters per element."},
        "11099": {"comment":"Segment 1's VAR_INIT_STR"},
        "11100": {"comment":"VAR_INIT_STR: a string of C characters"},
        "11103": {"comment":"Elements left?"},
        "11109": {"comment":"Comma: next name; else the statement ends"},
        "11114": {"synopsis":"NUMERIC statement (the keyword table gives this address): once per line, declares each\nnumeric name of the list, an array when bounds follow, every element with its initial\nvalue. Errors: 20041 for a name already in this scope, 20000 after the list.","comment":"Line done before? Nothing to do"},
        "11118": {"synopsis":"Loop: one name of the list; a non-numeric name ends the statement.","comment":"A numeric name?"},
        "11122": {"comment":"Segment 1's VAR_SCOPE_TEST"},
        "11123": {"comment":"VAR_SCOPE_TEST: NC when already in this scope"},
        "11125": {"comment":"Already here: error 20041"},
        "11128": {"comment":"Create a numeric name; HL = elements"},
        "11132": {"synopsis":"Loop: one numeric value per element.","comment":"Segment 1's VAR_INIT_NUM"},
        "11133": {"comment":"VAR_INIT_NUM: a numeric value"},
        "11140": {"comment":"Comma: next name; else the statement ends"},
        "11145": {"synopsis":"After a declared name: a comma (symbol $0C) reads the next token and returns to go on;\notherwise drops the return address and leaves through EXPECT_LINE_END, which wants the\nline's end\n(error 20000 if anything else follows).","comment":"A comma?"},
        "11150": {"comment":"Yes: TOKEN_NEXT and go on"},
        "11153": {"comment":"No: leave the statement's loop"},
        "11154": {"comment":"TOKEN_EXPECT the line's end"},
        "11157": {"synopsis":"Reads an optional \"*n\" maximum string length: when the current symbol is $0A (\"*\") the\nnumber after it is taken, else L is kept.\nEntry: L = the default.\nExit: C = the length (1-254).\nChanges: AF, HL.\nError 1051 for 0 or more than 254.","comment":"\"*\"?"},
        "11162": {"comment":"No: C = the default"},
        "11165": {"comment":"TOKEN_NEXT: the number"},
        "11168": {"comment":"NUM_PUSH_WORK"},
        "11171": {"comment":"NUM_POP_INT: HL = the length"},
        "11174": {"comment":"TOKEN_NEXT past it"},
        "11179": {"comment":"Above 255?"},
        "11183": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "11187": {"comment":"255? Else it fits"},
        "11189": {"synopsis":"Error 1051: a string length outside 1-254."},
        "11193": {"synopsis":"Tests and sets bit 7 of the current line's byte +3 (the line at ($0216)): NZ when it was\nalready set, so the declaration was done before; Z and carry the first time.\nChanges: F, HL."},
        "11199": {"comment":"Done before?"},
        "11202": {"comment":"Mark the line"},
        "11206": {"synopsis":"Creates a name entry at ($0234) for the current name (segment 1's VAR_NEW_ENTRY, flags A)\nand reads the next token. Without \"(\" it returns NC with HL = 1.\nWith \"(\" it marks the entry an array (flag bit 1), builds the array head after it and\nreturns the element count:\n+0 the dimension count, +1 the total count (a 6-byte number), +7 and +19 one 12-byte\ndescriptor per dimension (DIM_BOUNDS: lower bound, element count); the second is left\nunused for one dimension. The \")\" is required (error 20000).\nExit: carry and HL = the element count; ($0234) past the head.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"Where the entry goes"},
        "11210": {"comment":"Segment 1's VAR_NEW_ENTRY"},
        "11211": {"comment":"VAR_NEW_ENTRY: the entry, flags A"},
        "11213": {"comment":"TOKEN_NEXT"},
        "11216": {"comment":"\"(\"?"},
        "11218": {"comment":"Not an array: one element, NC"},
        "11225": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "11228": {"comment":"Flag bit 1: an array"},
        "11230": {"comment":"Room for the head: 55 + 2 bytes (MEM_ENSURE_DE)"},
        "11236": {"comment":"The value field: the head starts here"},
        "11240": {"comment":"First descriptor after 7 bytes"},
        "11247": {"comment":"First bounds"},
        "11250": {"comment":"A comma: a second dimension?"},
        "11257": {"comment":"Two dimensions so far"},
        "11261": {"comment":"Second bounds"},
        "11264": {"comment":"NUM_MUL: total = count 1 * count 2"},
        "11269": {"synopsis":"One dimension: the count is 1 and the second descriptor's space is skipped."},
        "11270": {"comment":"Skip the unused second descriptor"},
        "11280": {"synopsis":"Wants \")\", stores the total count in the head and pops it into HL.","comment":"\")\" (TOKEN_EXPECT)"},
        "11285": {"comment":"The head's +1"},
        "11287": {"comment":"Total count kept there (NUM_STORE_VAR)"},
        "11290": {"comment":"NUM_POP_INT: HL = the element count"},
        "11295": {"synopsis":"Reads one dimension's bounds: \"n\" (lower 0) or \"m TO n\", each a numeric expression made\nwhole by segment 1's FP_INT. Stores the lower bound and the element count (n - m + 1) as\n6-byte numbers at ($0234) and ($0234) + 6, moves ($0234) past them and leaves the count on\nthe stack.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"TOKEN_NEXT and EVAL_NUMERIC ($DEE3)"},
        "11298": {"comment":"Segment 1's FP_INT"},
        "11299": {"comment":"FP_INT: made whole"},
        "11301": {"comment":"The word \"TO\" (counted text)"},
        "11304": {"comment":"Does the current name match it?"},
        "11309": {"comment":"Upper bound"},
        "11313": {"comment":"FP_INT: made whole"},
        "11317": {"synopsis":"No TO: the one value is the upper bound and 0 the lower.","comment":"ITEM_DUP"},
        "11320": {"comment":"The lower copy"},
        "11329": {"comment":"Set to integer 0"},
        "11332": {"synopsis":"Stores the bounds, then replaces the upper one with the count.","comment":"Lower bound at +0, upper at +6"},
        "11341": {"comment":"Upper bound to +6 (NUM_POP_VAR)"},
        "11347": {"comment":"Lower bound to +0"},
        "11353": {"comment":"Push upper"},
        "11358": {"comment":"Push lower"},
        "11361": {"comment":"NUM_SUB: upper - lower"},
        "11364": {"comment":"Plus 1"},
        "11370": {"comment":"NUM_ADD"},
        "11375": {"comment":"The count over the upper bound at +6"},
        "11379": {"comment":"Past the 12 bytes"},
        "11387": {"synopsis":"Finds the current name (segment 1's VAR_FIND_VISIBLE), reads the next token and, for an\narray, its subscripts (ARRAY_ELEMENT with B = 1, computing).\nExit: HL = the value's address.","comment":"Segment 1's VAR_FIND_VISIBLE"},
        "11388": {"comment":"VAR_FIND_VISIBLE: the name's entry"},
        "11390": {"comment":"Compute the subscripts"},
        "11392": {"synopsis":"Reads the next token, then ARRAY_ELEMENT."},
        "11395": {"synopsis":"When C bit 1 marks an array: parses \"(\" subscript [, subscript] \")\" and returns the\nelement's address.\n1. The first subscript (SUBSCRIPT_EVAL) less the lower bound, checked against the count.\n2. With two dimensions: times the second count, plus the second subscript's offset.\n3. Times the element size: 6 for a number (C bit 0 clear), maximum length + 2 for a\nstring; plus 31 for the head.\nWith B bit 0 clear (parse only) nothing is computed and the \")\" is not read.\nEntry: HL = the value field, C = the flags, B bit 0 = compute.\nExit: HL = the element.\nChanges: AF, DE. Error 2001 out of bounds; 20000 (Not understood).","comment":"Not an array: HL is the value"},
        "11400": {"comment":"Keep the other register set"},
        "11405": {"comment":"First descriptor"},
        "11409": {"comment":"Expects \"(\""},
        "11415": {"comment":"Two dimensions?"},
        "11420": {"comment":"Computing?"},
        "11426": {"comment":"The second dimension's count"},
        "11433": {"comment":"NUM_MUL: first offset * that count"},
        "11438": {"synopsis":"The second subscript, after a comma."},
        "11439": {"comment":"Second descriptor"},
        "11443": {"comment":"Expects \",\""},
        "11451": {"comment":"NUM_ADD: the offsets combined"},
        "11456": {"synopsis":"Turns the element offset into an address.","comment":"Only parsing? Done"},
        "11460": {"comment":"\")\" (TOKEN_EXPECT)"},
        "11465": {"comment":"A string array?"},
        "11469": {"comment":"NUM_POP_INT: the offset"},
        "11472": {"comment":"Offset * 6"},
        "11479": {"synopsis":"String elements: offset * (maximum length + 2).","comment":"The first element's maximum length"},
        "11483": {"comment":"BC = its size: length + 2"},
        "11488": {"comment":"NUM_POP_INT: the offset"},
        "11492": {"comment":"HL = offset * size (MUL_BC_DE)"},
        "11495": {"synopsis":"Adds the 31-byte head."},
        "11499": {"synopsis":"Restores the registers and adds the value field's address."},
        "11505": {"comment":"HL = the element"},
        "11507": {"synopsis":"Wants symbol A (\"(\" or \",\") and evaluates the subscript after it. When computing (B bit\n0): makes it whole (FP_INT) and leaves subscript - lower bound on the stack, checked to be\n0 to count - 1.\nEntry: A = the symbol, HL = the dimension's descriptor (lower bound, count).\nChanges: AF. Error 20000 for another symbol, 2001 out of bounds.","comment":"Wrong symbol: error 20000 (Not understood)"},
        "11516": {"comment":"TOKEN_NEXT and evaluate ($DEE7)"},
        "11522": {"comment":"Only parsing? Done"},
        "11527": {"comment":"Segment 1's FP_INT"},
        "11528": {"comment":"FP_INT: made whole"},
        "11534": {"comment":"Push the lower bound"},
        "11537": {"comment":"NUM_SUB: the offset"},
        "11540": {"comment":"Negative? Error 2001"},
        "11546": {"comment":"ITEM_DUP"},
        "11550": {"comment":"The count"},
        "11557": {"comment":"NUM_SUB: offset - count"},
        "11560": {"comment":"Not negative? Error 2001"},
        "11566": {"comment":"Drop it; the offset stays"},
        "11571": {"synopsis":"Before BASIC is left: when no program is running ((ix+0) bit 1 clear) prints \"Press ENTER\nto exit BASIC\" and reads a key from channel $69 (EXOS 5).\nExit: Z when the key is ENTER (B = $0D); Z and A = 0 at once when a program runs.\nChanges: AF, B. An EXOS error is raised (RST 18h).","comment":"A program running?"},
        "11577": {"comment":"Prints the counted text that follows"},
        "11580": {"comment":"Counted text: 27 characters"},
        "11608": {"comment":"Channel $69"},
        "11610": {"comment":"EXOS 5: read character"},
        "11612": {"comment":"EXOS error? Raise it"},
        "11613": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "11617": {"synopsis":"A program runs: Z without asking."},
        "11619": {"synopsis":"Reads the system status (EXOS 20) into the 8 bytes at $0E2C and returns its byte 5, the\nnumber of working RAM segments.\nExit: HL = the count, DE = $0E2C.\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"Status buffer"},
        "11622": {"comment":"EXOS 20: read system status"},
        "11624": {"comment":"Byte 5: working RAM segments"},
        "11632": {"synopsis":"Prints HL segments as bytes: HL * 16384, then \"bytes \" (INFO's memory lines).\nEntry: HL = a segment count.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, IY."},
        "11633": {"comment":"NUM_PUSH_INT: the count"},
        "11636": {"comment":"16384 bytes a segment"},
        "11640": {"comment":"NUM_PUSH_INT: 16384"},
        "11641": {"comment":"NUM_MUL: count * 16384"},
        "11643": {"comment":"The product"},
        "11646": {"comment":"Print it with its spaces (PRINT_NUM_AT)"},
        "11649": {"comment":"Prints the counted text that follows"},
        "11652": {"comment":"Counted text: \"bytes \""},
        "11659": {"comment":"ITEM_DROP"},
        "11664": {"synopsis":"Pages in the current program, number ($020A); falls into PROG_PAGE_IN.","comment":"C = the current program's number"},
        "11667": {"synopsis":"Makes program C the current one.\n1. Finds the segment tagged C (segment 1's SEG_TAG_FIND); for C other than 0 a missing one\nis allocated (SEG_ALLOC, error 5000 when there is none) and starts empty.\n2. Puts the segment in page 1; the program starts at $4000, program 0 at ($0220).\n3. ($021A) = the start, ($020A) = C.\n4. A segment tagged C + $80 is put in page 2 when there is one.\nEntry: C = the program number.\nExit: carry when there is no C + $80 segment.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.","comment":"Segment 1's SEG_TAG_FIND"},
        "11668": {"comment":"SEG_TAG_FIND: HL = the slot, carry if none"},
        "11670": {"comment":"Found?"},
        "11672": {"comment":"Program 0 has none: no new segment"},
        "11677": {"comment":"Segment 1's SEG_ALLOC, tagged C"},
        "11678": {"comment":"SEG_ALLOC: M when none"},
        "11681": {"comment":"No segment: error 5000 (Insufficient memory)"},
        "11684": {"comment":"New segment: carry"},
        "11685": {"synopsis":"Pages the slot's segment in at page 1 and sets the program start."},
        "11686": {"comment":"The slot's segment"},
        "11687": {"comment":"Page 1 = the program's segment"},
        "11689": {"comment":"A program in its own segment starts at $4000"},
        "11692": {"comment":"Program 0?"},
        "11696": {"comment":"Program 0's start"},
        "11699": {"synopsis":"Stores the program start and number.","comment":"The program's start"},
        "11702": {"comment":"Current program number"},
        "11706": {"comment":"Old segment: its program stays"},
        "11708": {"comment":"New segment: empty program (length 0)"},
        "11710": {"synopsis":"Looks for a second segment, tagged C + $80, for page 2."},
        "11712": {"comment":"Segment 1's SEG_TAG_FIND"},
        "11713": {"comment":"SEG_TAG_FIND: HL = the slot, carry if none"},
        "11715": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "11717": {"comment":"Page 2 = that segment"},
        "11720": {"synopsis":"PROG_SWITCH to program 0."},
        "11722": {"synopsis":"Leaves the current program for program C: resets the run state (RUN_STATE_RESET), frees the\ncurrent program's segment when the program is empty (SEG_FREE), selects program C\n(PROG_PAGE_IN) and resets the run state again.\nEntry: C = the program number."},
        "11723": {"comment":"RUN_STATE_RESET"},
        "11726": {"comment":"Is the current program empty?"},
        "11733": {"comment":"Its segment"},
        "11736": {"comment":"Segment 1's SEG_TAG_FIND"},
        "11737": {"comment":"SEG_TAG_FIND: HL = the slot, carry if none"},
        "11739": {"comment":"None: nothing to free"},
        "11741": {"comment":"C = the segment"},
        "11742": {"comment":"Segment 1's SEG_FREE"},
        "11743": {"comment":"SEG_FREE: free segment C"},
        "11745": {"synopsis":"Selects program C, then RUN_STATE_RESET."},
        "11746": {"comment":"PROG_PAGE_IN with C"},
        "11749": {"comment":"RUN_STATE_RESET"},
        "11752": {"synopsis":"Pops the top item when it is a value (types 1-3).\nExit: carry; A = the new top's type, HL = its address.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.\nError 30000 (BASIC data has been corrupted) when the top is not a value.","comment":"Drop it if a value"},
        "11756": {"synopsis":"Error 30000: BASIC data has been corrupted."},
        "11760": {"synopsis":"Pops the top item when its type is below C = 4; LD C,6 is hidden at $2DF3 and LD C,7 at\n$2DF6, the entries for types below 6 and below 7. The size comes from the table at\nITEM_SIZES\n(a string's also from its length byte).\nExit: carry and A = the new top's type when popped; NC when the type is 0 (the stack's\nbottom) or not below C.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL. (Its check for a type above 8, error 30000,\ncannot fire with C = 4, 6 or 7.)"},
        "11762": {"comment":"Hides LD C,$06 at $2DF3: types below 6"},
        "11765": {"comment":"Hides LD C,$07 at $2DF6: types below 7"},
        "11768": {"comment":"The top item's type"},
        "11772": {"comment":"Type 0: the bottom, NC"},
        "11774": {"comment":"Not below C? NC, kept"},
        "11776": {"comment":"Type 9 or more is no stack item"},
        "11778": {"comment":"Error 30000 (BASIC data has been corrupted)"},
        "11781": {"comment":"D = 0 for the additions"},
        "11783": {"comment":"Past the type byte"},
        "11784": {"comment":"A string?"},
        "11788": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "11789": {"comment":"Past the text"},
        "11790": {"synopsis":"Adds the type's entry of ITEM_SIZES to HL: HL becomes the next item, which is the new top;\nreturns A = its type and carry.","comment":"E = the type"},
        "11792": {"comment":"The size table"},
        "11796": {"comment":"Bytes still to skip"},
        "11798": {"comment":"HL = the next item"},
        "11799": {"comment":"It is the new top"},
        "11802": {"comment":"A = the new top's type"},
        "11803": {"comment":"C: an item was dropped"},
        "11805": {"synopsis":"The value stack's item sizes, one byte per type 0-8: the bytes that follow the type byte, a\nstring counting only its length byte (its text is added from the length). Type 0 (the bottom\nmark) 0, 1 0, 2 (number) 8, 3 (string) 1, 4 $18, 5 4, 6 2, 7 5, 8 $0B: items of 1, 9, length\n+ 2, 25, 5, 3, 6 and 12 bytes. Read by DROP_ADD_SIZE and by the error's stack walk\n(ERR_SKIP_SIZE, with 1 taken off)."},
        "11814": {"synopsis":"IS-BASIC call $0A: A = byte +8 of the top item; Z when it is $7F, the integer form of a\nnumber.\nChanges: A, IY.","comment":"The top item"},
        "11818": {"comment":"Its byte +8"},
        "11821": {"comment":"$7F marks the integer form"},
        "11824": {"synopsis":"Tells whether the current token is a string: Z for a string name (class $40) or a string\nliteral ($80); carry is clear only for a string name.\nChanges: A.","comment":"The token's class"},
        "11827": {"comment":"A string name?"},
        "11830": {"comment":"A string literal?"},
        "11832": {"comment":"Carry for anything but a string name"},
        "11834": {"synopsis":"Z when the current token is a name, numeric (class $20) or string ($40).\nChanges: A.","comment":"A numeric name?"},
        "11838": {"comment":"A string name?"},
        "11841": {"synopsis":"Z when the current token is a numeric name (class $20).\nChanges: A.","comment":"The token's class"},
        "11844": {"comment":"A numeric name?"},
        "11847": {"synopsis":"Z when the current symbol ends the statement: the line's end (1) or the separator $10.\nChanges: A.","comment":"The symbol code"},
        "11850": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "11853": {"comment":"The statement separator?"},
        "11856": {"synopsis":"NC when character C is a decimal digit, carry otherwise; A_IS_DIGIT tests A.\nExit: A = the character.","comment":"The character"},
        "11857": {"synopsis":"CHAR_IS_DIGIT for the character in A ($05EC, $243F and $2488 call it here).","comment":"Below '0': carry"},
        "11860": {"comment":"Past '9'?"},
        "11862": {"comment":"NC for '0'-'9'"},
        "11864": {"synopsis":"NC when character C is a capital letter A-Z, carry otherwise.\nExit: A = the character.","comment":"The character"},
        "11865": {"comment":"Below 'A': carry"},
        "11868": {"comment":"Past 'Z'?"},
        "11870": {"comment":"NC for 'A'-'Z'"},
        "11872": {"synopsis":"Z when A is '<' or '=', NZ otherwise. No caller of it was found in this ROM, and the profile\ndid not run it.","comment":"Below '<': NZ"},
        "11875": {"comment":"Past '=': NZ"},
        "11878": {"comment":"Z for '<' and '='"},
        "11880": {"synopsis":"Tells whether the top two numbers are both in integer form, and if so fetches them for the\ninteger arithmetic of NUM_ADD, NUM_MUL and NUM_DIV.\nExit: NZ when either is a float; Z with HL = the top's value, BC = the next one's (DE = the\ntop + 12).\nChanges: A, BC, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"The top item"},
        "11884": {"comment":"The integer form's mark"},
        "11886": {"comment":"Is the top an integer?"},
        "11890": {"comment":"And the item below it (9 bytes on)?"},
        "11894": {"comment":"The top's value at +2"},
        "11902": {"comment":"To the next item's value (+11)"},
        "11906": {"comment":"BC = its value"},
        "11909": {"comment":"HL = the top's value"},
        "11911": {"synopsis":"Multiplies BC by DE, shift-and-add from BC's top bit.\nExit: PO with HL = the product; PE as soon as it no longer fits 15 bits (a signed overflow),\nHL then meaningless.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"The product starts at 0"},
        "11914": {"comment":"16 bits of BC"},
        "11916": {"synopsis":"Next bit: doubles the product and adds DE when BC's next bit is set; stops with PO when all\n16 are done.","comment":"All done: PO from the DEC"},
        "11918": {"comment":"The product x 2"},
        "11920": {"comment":"Overflow: PE"},
        "11921": {"comment":"BC's next bit into carry"},
        "11925": {"comment":"Clear: nothing to add"},
        "11927": {"comment":"Clear carry"},
        "11928": {"comment":"Add DE"},
        "11930": {"comment":"Overflow: PE"},
        "11933": {"synopsis":"HL = HL x 10 (2 x HL + 8 x HL).\nChanges: F, HL."},
        "11934": {"comment":"x 2"},
        "11935": {"comment":"Kept in DE"},
        "11937": {"comment":"x 8"},
        "11939": {"comment":"x 10"},
        "11942": {"synopsis":"Divides DE by BC (unsigned), a quotient bit per round.\nExit: DE = the quotient, HL = the remainder.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"Remainder 0, carry clear"},
        "11945": {"comment":"17 rounds"},
        "11947": {"synopsis":"One round: the remainder takes the dividend's next bit and BC is subtracted when it goes.","comment":"Remainder x 2 + DE's top bit"},
        "11949": {"comment":"Does BC go?"},
        "11951": {"comment":"Yes: quotient bit 1"},
        "11953": {"comment":"No: undo, quotient bit 0"},
        "11955": {"synopsis":"Shifts the quotient bit (NOT carry) into DE, whose next dividend bit comes out.","comment":"The quotient bit"},
        "11956": {"comment":"Into DE; its next bit out"},
        "11960": {"comment":"All rounds done?"},
        "11964": {"synopsis":"C = the character at HL in upper case (CHAR_UPCASE with the range above $60: a-z).","comment":"The range above $60: a-z"},
        "11966": {"synopsis":"IS-BASIC call $26: C = the character at HL, its case flipped (bit 5) when it lies in A+1 to\nA+26; with A = $60 (CHAR_TO_UPPER) a-z become capitals.\nChanges: A, C, F.","comment":"The character"},
        "11967": {"comment":"At or below the range?"},
        "11969": {"comment":"The range's top"},
        "11971": {"comment":"Above it?"},
        "11973": {"comment":"The case bit flipped"},
        "11978": {"synopsis":"HL = abs(HL): a negative HL goes through NEG_HL.\nExit: Z when HL was not negative.","comment":"Not negative: Z, unchanged"},
        "11981": {"synopsis":"IS-BASIC call $04: HL = -HL (HL - 1, then every bit flipped).\nChanges: A, HL.","comment":"Minus 1"},
        "11982": {"comment":"Then every bit flipped"},
        "11989": {"synopsis":"Prints HL in decimal in 5 places, leading zeros as spaces (C = ' ', and the OR clears\ncarry); then PRINT_DECIMAL. Entry $2ED8, the LD C,0 hidden in OR $0E, prints with no leading\ncharacters and the caller's carry: the error report ($3491) enters there.","comment":"Leading zeros as spaces"},
        "11991": {"comment":"NC: 5 places; hides LD C,0 (entry $2ED8)"},
        "11994": {"synopsis":"IS-BASIC call $39: prints HL as an unsigned decimal number with PRINT_CHAR: dividing by the\npowers of DEC_POWERS from 10000 (from 1000 when carry is set: 4 places). Leading zeros print\nas character C, or not at all when C = 0; the last digit always prints.\nEntry: HL = the number, C = the fill character, carry = 4 places.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"The powers of ten"},
        "11998": {"comment":"The digit '0'"},
        "12000": {"comment":"NC: from 10000"},
        "12002": {"comment":"Carry: from 1000"},
        "12006": {"synopsis":"One place: DE = its power of ten; the last place (1) prints a 0 as '0' whatever C is.","comment":"DE = the power"},
        "12012": {"comment":"The last place (1)?"},
        "12015": {"comment":"Then a zero prints as '0'"},
        "12016": {"synopsis":"Moves on to the next power and counts how often this one goes into HL.","comment":"E back"},
        "12017": {"comment":"Next power"},
        "12021": {"comment":"Count from 0"},
        "12022": {"synopsis":"Subtracts the power until HL goes below zero.","comment":"Take the power once more"},
        "12027": {"comment":"A = the digit"},
        "12028": {"comment":"The last one undone"},
        "12029": {"comment":"A zero digit? (Z from the DEC)"},
        "12031": {"comment":"The digit's character"},
        "12032": {"comment":"Printed (PRINT_CHAR)"},
        "12035": {"comment":"Zeros print as '0' from now on"},
        "12038": {"synopsis":"A zero digit before the first other one: prints the fill character C, if any.","comment":"The fill character"},
        "12039": {"comment":"None?"},
        "12040": {"comment":"Printed (PRINT_CHAR)"},
        "12043": {"synopsis":"Ends after the place whose power's low byte is 1 (the last); otherwise the next place.","comment":"Was it the last place?"},
        "12047": {"synopsis":"The powers of ten PRINT_DECIMAL divides by: 10000, 1000, 100, 10, 1 (IY = DEC_POWERS at\nPRINT_DECIMAL).\nThe last one's low byte, 1, ends its loop."},
        "12057": {"synopsis":"IS-BASIC call $34: prints CR LF and STOP; when a program runs (bit 1 of ($0200)) also \" at\nline \" and the number of the current line ($0216) (through $09E4); then character $19 and CR\nLF (PRINT_CRLF). The texts follow the CALLs of $0E00, which prints the counted text after\nits\nCALL and returns past it.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"CR LF and STOP (the text after the CALL)"},
        "12060": {"synopsis":"The counted text that $0E00 prints for PRINT_STOP_MSG: length 6, CR LF and STOP."},
        "12067": {"comment":"The current line"},
        "12071": {"comment":"Is a program running?"},
        "12077": {"comment":"' at line ' (the text after the CALL)"},
        "12080": {"synopsis":"The counted text \" at line \" (length 9) that $0E00 prints for PRINT_STOP_MSG."},
        "12090": {"comment":"To its line number"},
        "12091": {"comment":"NC: no padding"},
        "12092": {"comment":"The number at HL printed ($09E4)"},
        "12095": {"synopsis":"Prints character $19 and CR LF, HL back as the current line.","comment":"Character $19"},
        "12100": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "12101": {"comment":"CR LF (PRINT_CRLF)"},
        "12104": {"synopsis":"Looks the current name (length ($0203), text at ($0347)) up in the keyword chain whose first\nblock is at ($0232); keywords are numbered from 0 through the blocks in order.\nExit: Z when it is no keyword; NZ when found, with C = the keyword's number and HL = its\ndescriptor + 4 (the flags; the name follows).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The first block"},
        "12107": {"comment":"Keyword number - 1"},
        "12109": {"synopsis":"The next block: the loop enters at $2F4E, the POP HL (the next block's address) hidden in\nthis LD A,$E1; coming from $2F4B the LD does nothing that matters. A zero address ends the\nchain: Z.","comment":"Hides POP HL ($2F4E): the next block"},
        "12111": {"comment":"End of the chain?"},
        "12113": {"comment":"Not a keyword: Z"},
        "12114": {"comment":"DE = the next block"},
        "12118": {"comment":"Kept for later"},
        "12119": {"comment":"This block's count"},
        "12121": {"comment":"DE = its first entry"},
        "12123": {"synopsis":"Next entry of the block (3 bytes: the descriptor's address, its segment); compares the\ndescriptor's name with the current one.","comment":"Entries left"},
        "12125": {"comment":"None: the next block"},
        "12129": {"comment":"The keyword's number"},
        "12131": {"comment":"DE = the descriptor's address"},
        "12134": {"comment":"Past the segment byte"},
        "12137": {"comment":"The flags at +4"},
        "12142": {"comment":"The name at +5"},
        "12143": {"comment":"The current name? (NAME_MATCH)"},
        "12148": {"comment":"No: next entry"},
        "12150": {"comment":"Found: NZ"},
        "12151": {"comment":"Drop the count and the next block"},
        "12154": {"synopsis":"IS-BASIC call $33: finds the first program line after the current one ($0216) whose nesting\ndepth (byte +3, low 7 bits) is the current line's, as a block's closing line has.\nExit: HL = that line, Z; error 20050 (Missing end of block) at the program's end.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.","comment":"The current line"},
        "12157": {"comment":"D = 1: the first line comes next"},
        "12162": {"synopsis":"The first line: its depth is the one to find (C is never 0 from LINE_FIND_LEVEL, so the DEC\nA is not used from there).","comment":"C = 0?"},
        "12166": {"comment":"Then one level less"},
        "12167": {"synopsis":"Keeps the depth to look for in C.","comment":"The depth to find"},
        "12168": {"synopsis":"Moves to the next line.","comment":"The next line"},
        "12169": {"synopsis":"Looks at a line: the program's end (length 0) is error 20050; otherwise compares its depth.","comment":"Its length"},
        "12170": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "12172": {"comment":"Program's end: error 20050"},
        "12176": {"comment":"To byte +3"},
        "12179": {"comment":"The depth (and bit 7)"},
        "12181": {"comment":"The depth only"},
        "12183": {"comment":"The first line?"},
        "12187": {"comment":"The same depth?"},
        "12188": {"comment":"No: go on"},
        "12191": {"synopsis":"LINE_FIND_LEVEL, then A = the keyword number of that line's first statement (byte +5).\nExit: HL = the line, DE = the line + 5, A = the keyword.","comment":"HL = the next line at this depth"},
        "12194": {"comment":"DE = 5 (D is 0)"},
        "12197": {"comment":"Its first statement's keyword"},
        "12199": {"comment":"HL = the line again"},
        "12201": {"synopsis":"LINE_LEVEL_KW, and that line becomes the current one ($0216)."},
        "12204": {"synopsis":"Stores HL as the current line ($0216).","comment":"The current line"},
        "12208": {"synopsis":"BLOCK_ENTER's first line: C = its depth; NZ (returned) when its first statement is not\nkeyword B. Otherwise the next line becomes the current one (SET_CUR_LINE through the CALL Z)\nand the scan goes on.","comment":"C = the block's depth"},
        "12209": {"comment":"To the first statement's keyword"},
        "12212": {"comment":"Keyword B?"},
        "12213": {"comment":"No: NZ"},
        "12215": {"comment":"Only rereads the keyword"},
        "12216": {"synopsis":"A line inside the block: byte +3 is written back without bit 7 (the flag RUN sets on\nexecuted declarations), then the next line.","comment":"Byte +3 without bit 7"},
        "12217": {"comment":"The line back"},
        "12218": {"comment":"The next line"},
        "12219": {"comment":"First line: the next becomes current"},
        "12222": {"synopsis":"Enters a block at line HL; callers come in at $2FBF, the LD D,1 hidden in this JP C (carry\nis clear after the ADD above, so the JP never jumps).\n1. The line's first statement must be keyword B (HANDLER from the error code, $33A4; DEF\n   from $1AC7): else it returns NZ.\n2. The next line becomes the current one ($0216).\n3. Clears bit 7 of byte +3 of every line up to the next one at the block's own depth, which\n   is returned.\nEntry: HL = the line, B = the keyword.\nExit: Z with HL = the closing line; error 20050 (Missing end of block) at the program's end.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.","comment":"Never jumps; hides LD D,1 (entry $2FBF)"},
        "12225": {"synopsis":"Looks at the next line: the program's end is error 20050; the first line goes to\nBLK_FIRST_LINE, a line at the block's depth ends the scan.","comment":"Its length"},
        "12228": {"comment":"Program's end: error 20050"},
        "12235": {"comment":"Byte +3"},
        "12236": {"comment":"The depth"},
        "12238": {"comment":"The first line?"},
        "12242": {"comment":"The block's depth: its end?"},
        "12243": {"comment":"No: clear its flag"},
        "12245": {"synopsis":"Returns HL = the line just examined.","comment":"HL = the line"},
        "12247": {"synopsis":"IS-BASIC call $35: E = the flags (byte +4) of keyword C's descriptor (KEYWORD_ENTRY).\nExit: HL = the descriptor + 4, A = its segment.","comment":"HL = keyword C's descriptor"},
        "12250": {"comment":"To +4"},
        "12254": {"comment":"E = the flags"},
        "12256": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine whose address is the word at +2 of keyword C's descriptor, in the keyword's\nsegment (KW_CALL_AT): the statement's syntax check, which runs when a line is entered and stored\n($0394, $071B) and may rewrite the line's tokens (CHK_IF, CHK_DEF ...).","comment":"HL = keyword C's descriptor"},
        "12259": {"comment":"The word at +2"},
        "12263": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine whose address is the word at +0 of keyword C's descriptor, in the\nkeyword's segment. Called when statements run ($03A9, $0DC5, $1264): the statement's action.","comment":"HL = keyword C's descriptor"},
        "12266": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine at the word at HL in segment A: segment 0 by a plain jump (JP (HL) at\n$0B8C), others through RST 08h.","comment":"The routine's address"},
        "12270": {"comment":"Segment 0?"},
        "12271": {"comment":"Jumped to directly"},
        "12274": {"comment":"Called in segment A"},
        "12276": {"synopsis":"Finds keyword C in the keyword chain ($0232): steps through the blocks, taking each one's\ncount off the number, then reads the 3-byte entry.\nExit: HL = the descriptor, A = its segment, DE = the entry's segment byte.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The first block"},
        "12280": {"synopsis":"C = the number within this block; on to the next block while it is not smaller than the\nblock's count.","comment":"C = the number in this block"},
        "12281": {"comment":"DE = the next block"},
        "12285": {"comment":"Less this block's count"},
        "12286": {"comment":"HL = the next block"},
        "12287": {"comment":"Not in this block: on"},
        "12289": {"comment":"The block's first entry"},
        "12290": {"comment":"3 x C"},
        "12296": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "12297": {"comment":"DE = the descriptor"},
        "12301": {"comment":"A = its segment"},
        "12302": {"comment":"HL = the descriptor"},
        "12304": {"synopsis":"IS-BASIC call $29: moves the value stack down to start $40 bytes above the variables' end\n($0234), and gives back the RAM it no longer needs.\n1. ($0238) = ($0228) = ($0234) + $40, the items copied there; ($0226) the new bottom.\n2. When the bottom is now below page 2 ($8000), frees the program's page-2 segment (tag\n   ($020A) + $80); below page 1 ($4000), also its page-1 segment (tag ($020A)).\n3. MEM_ENSURE_DE with no bytes asked (the room check).\n4. When the bottom's segment is the shared one ($020B), EXOS 23 sets the user boundary just\n   above the bottom.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The variables' end"},
        "12307": {"comment":"$40 bytes on"},
        "12311": {"comment":"The variables' new limit"},
        "12315": {"comment":"The old top"},
        "12319": {"comment":"The new top"},
        "12322": {"comment":"The bottom"},
        "12328": {"comment":"BC = the size - 1"},
        "12330": {"comment":"The size"},
        "12331": {"comment":"HL = the old top"},
        "12332": {"comment":"DE = the new top"},
        "12333": {"comment":"Moved down"},
        "12336": {"comment":"The new bottom"},
        "12341": {"comment":"Its bits 7 and 6; bit 5 stops the loop"},
        "12344": {"comment":"The program's tag"},
        "12347": {"comment":"Page 2 first: tag bit 7"},
        "12349": {"synopsis":"Next bit of the bottom's address: clear means the stack no longer reaches that page, so the\nsegment tagged C is freed.","comment":"Does the stack reach this page?"},
        "12350": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "12354": {"comment":"A segment tagged C? (SEG_TAG_FIND)"},
        "12355": {"comment":"SEG_TAG_FIND: is segment tag C held?"},
        "12356": {"comment":"End of list"},
        "12357": {"comment":"None"},
        "12359": {"comment":"Its number"},
        "12360": {"comment":"Freed (SEG_FREE)"},
        "12361": {"comment":"SEG_FREE: free segment C"},
        "12362": {"comment":"End of list"},
        "12363": {"synopsis":"Then the page-1 segment (tag without bit 7) and the next bit."},
        "12364": {"comment":"Page 1: tag without bit 7"},
        "12369": {"synopsis":"Checks the room (MEM_ENSURE_DE, no extra bytes), then moves the shared segment's user\nboundary when the stack's bottom lies in it.","comment":"No extra bytes: the room check only"},
        "12372": {"comment":"MEM_ENSURE_DE"},
        "12375": {"comment":"The bottom"},
        "12376": {"comment":"C = its segment"},
        "12379": {"comment":"DE = its offset in the page"},
        "12384": {"comment":"+ 1"},
        "12385": {"comment":"The shared segment"},
        "12388": {"comment":"The bottom's?"},
        "12389": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "12390": {"comment":"EXOS 23: the user boundary = DE"},
        "12393": {"synopsis":"Moves segment C (the highest held) into the one just got (SEG_MOVE), then SEG_COMPACT asks\nfor another.","comment":"Segment C moved into it"},
        "12396": {"synopsis":"Keeps the program's segments in the lowest numbers EXOS has: allocates a segment\n(SEG_ALLOC_PROG); while the one it gets is below the highest segment held, moves that one's\ncontents into it (SC_MOVE) and asks again. A new segment above the others, or the shared\none, is freed again. MEM_ENSURE_DE returns through here after it has claimed RAM.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"A new segment (SEG_ALLOC_PROG)"},
        "12399": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "12400": {"comment":"The new segment"},
        "12401": {"comment":"The shared one: freed again"},
        "12404": {"comment":"The segment table"},
        "12407": {"comment":"Its slots"},
        "12410": {"comment":"Highest so far"},
        "12412": {"synopsis":"Finds C = the highest segment number in the table.","comment":"A slot's segment"},
        "12413": {"comment":"An empty slot?"},
        "12416": {"comment":"Below the highest?"},
        "12419": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "12421": {"comment":"A new highest"},
        "12422": {"synopsis":"Next slot."},
        "12426": {"comment":"The new one's slot"},
        "12428": {"comment":"Below the highest?"},
        "12429": {"comment":"Yes: move the highest into it"},
        "12431": {"synopsis":"Frees segment A again (SEG_FREE): nothing lower to be had.","comment":"The segment"},
        "12432": {"comment":"Freed (SEG_FREE)"},
        "12433": {"comment":"SEG_FREE: free segment C"},
        "12434": {"comment":"End of list"},
        "12436": {"synopsis":"IS-BASIC call $27: MEM_ENSURE_DE for 12 bytes.","comment":"10, + 2 below"},
        "12439": {"synopsis":"IS-BASIC call $28: makes sure DE + 2 bytes fit between the variables ($0238) and the value\nstack ($0228), claiming RAM when they do not.\n1. ($022A) = DE + 2.\n2. While BASIC holds the shared segment ($020B): if EXOS no longer shares one it is\n   forgotten; if a segment of BASIC's own can be had, the shared segment's contents move\n   into it (SEG_MOVE).\n3. MEM_CHECK; enough: return.\n4. Otherwise (returning through SEG_COMPACT) the stack moves to the top of the RAM held\n   ($3FFF, $7FFF or $BFFF, by the program's page-1 and page-2 segments) and, still short, a\n   new segment is paged into page 1 or 2 and tagged; then again from 2.\n5. Holding only the shared segment, the program that owns it ((ix+$0D)) takes it up to the\n   EXOS boundary (EXOS 23) and moves the stack there.\nExit: NC, or error 5000 (Insufficient memory) / 5100 (Insufficient stack space).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"+ 2"},
        "12441": {"comment":"The bytes wanted"},
        "12445": {"synopsis":"With the shared segment held, tries to swap it for a segment of BASIC's own; then checks the\nroom.","comment":"Is the shared segment held?"},
        "12449": {"comment":"No"},
        "12451": {"comment":"EXOS 22: C = the shared segment"},
        "12453": {"comment":"Still shared?"},
        "12455": {"comment":"No: forget it"},
        "12457": {"comment":"A segment of our own? (SEG_ALLOC_PROG)"},
        "12460": {"comment":"Only the shared one again"},
        "12462": {"comment":"Shared contents moved into it (SEG_MOVE)"},
        "12466": {"synopsis":"No shared segment held any more: ($020B) = 0, and carry skips the check to claim RAM.","comment":"No shared segment now"},
        "12469": {"comment":"Carry: straight on to claim RAM"},
        "12470": {"synopsis":"Room enough (MEM_CHECK)? Then done; otherwise claims RAM, returning through SEG_COMPACT.","comment":"Room enough? (MEM_CHECK)"},
        "12473": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "12474": {"comment":"Return through SEG_COMPACT"},
        "12478": {"comment":"The program's tag"},
        "12481": {"comment":"Its page-2 segment"},
        "12483": {"comment":"Held? (SEG_TAG_FIND)"},
        "12484": {"comment":"SEG_TAG_FIND: is segment tag C held?"},
        "12485": {"comment":"End of list"},
        "12486": {"comment":"Then the stack ends at $BFFF"},
        "12490": {"comment":"Its page-1 segment"},
        "12493": {"comment":"SEG_TAG_FIND: is segment tag C held?"},
        "12494": {"comment":"End of list"},
        "12495": {"comment":"Then at $7FFF"},
        "12499": {"comment":"Else at $3FFF"},
        "12501": {"synopsis":"Moves the stack to end at H*256 + $FF (STACK_MOVE_TO) and checks the room again."},
        "12504": {"comment":"Stack moved there (STACK_MOVE_TO)"},
        "12507": {"comment":"Room now? (MEM_CHECK)"},
        "12511": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "12512": {"comment":"Up to $BFFF already?"},
        "12515": {"comment":"Error 5000"},
        "12517": {"comment":"Up to $7FFF?"},
        "12519": {"comment":"Page 2's port"},
        "12523": {"comment":"Else page 1's"},
        "12524": {"synopsis":"Gets a new segment (SEG_ALLOC_PROG; error 5000 if none) and pages it in through port C; in\npage 2 its tag gets bit 7. Then tries again (ME_RETRY).","comment":"A new segment (SEG_ALLOC_PROG)"},
        "12527": {"comment":"None: error 5000"},
        "12530": {"comment":"Paged in: (HL) to port C"},
        "12532": {"comment":"Page 1?"},
        "12534": {"comment":"Try again"},
        "12536": {"comment":"Page 2: tag bit 7"},
        "12538": {"comment":"Try again"},
        "12540": {"synopsis":"Only the shared segment is to be had: when the current program ($020A) owns it ((ix+$0D))\nand room is short, the user boundary goes up to the EXOS boundary and the stack is moved to\nend below it.","comment":"The current program"},
        "12543": {"comment":"Owns the shared segment?"},
        "12546": {"comment":"No: only the check"},
        "12548": {"comment":"Room enough? (MEM_CHECK)"},
        "12552": {"comment":"EXOS 22: C = it, DE = the EXOS boundary"},
        "12554": {"comment":"Its slot (SEG_SLOT_FIND)"},
        "12555": {"comment":"SEG_SLOT_FIND: HL = the slot of segment C"},
        "12556": {"comment":"End of list"},
        "12558": {"comment":"Tagged for page 2?"},
        "12560": {"comment":"Page 1: $4000"},
        "12565": {"comment":"Page 2: $8000"},
        "12566": {"synopsis":"Sets the user boundary to the EXOS boundary (EXOS 23) and moves the stack to end just below\nit; error 5000 if still short.","comment":"The boundary's address in the page"},
        "12567": {"comment":"EXOS 23: the user boundary = DE"},
        "12569": {"comment":"An EXOS error raised"},
        "12570": {"comment":"The last byte below it"},
        "12571": {"comment":"Stack moved there (STACK_MOVE_TO)"},
        "12574": {"comment":"Room now? (MEM_CHECK)"},
        "12578": {"synopsis":"Raises error 5000 (Insufficient memory).","comment":"Error 5000 (Insufficient memory)"},
        "12582": {"synopsis":"C = the segment paged into the page that holds address HL (read from port $B0-$B3).\nChanges: A, C.","comment":"HL's page, the top two bits"},
        "12587": {"comment":"Its port, $B0-$B3"},
        "12590": {"comment":"C = the segment there"},
        "12593": {"synopsis":"Allocates a segment tagged with the current program's number ($020A) through SEG_ALLOC\n(segment 1's routine); its flags returned, BC kept."},
        "12594": {"comment":"The program's tag"},
        "12598": {"comment":"SEG_ALLOC: a segment tagged C"},
        "12599": {"comment":"End of list"},
        "12602": {"synopsis":"Moves the value stack so that its bottom byte is at HL (copied from the top end down);\n($0226) and ($0228) follow.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL, F.","comment":"The new bottom"},
        "12603": {"comment":"The bottom"},
        "12606": {"comment":"The top"},
        "12613": {"comment":"BC = the size - 1"},
        "12615": {"comment":"The size"},
        "12616": {"comment":"HL = the old bottom"},
        "12617": {"comment":"DE = the new bottom"},
        "12618": {"comment":"Is the bottom now"},
        "12622": {"comment":"Moved, from the end down"},
        "12624": {"comment":"The new top"},
        "12630": {"synopsis":"Copies the 16K of segment C into the segment in slot HL of the segment table (both paged\nthrough page 1 in turn, a byte at a time), frees segment C (SEG_FREE) and gives its tag to\nslot HL.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, page 1 restored.","comment":"The new slot"},
        "12631": {"comment":"L = the new segment"},
        "12632": {"comment":"H = segment C"},
        "12633": {"comment":"Page 1's start"},
        "12636": {"comment":"Page 1's port"},
        "12638": {"comment":"B = what page 1 holds now"},
        "12640": {"synopsis":"Copies a byte from segment H to segment L through page 1, up to $7FFF.","comment":"Page 1 = segment C"},
        "12643": {"comment":"Page 1 = the new segment"},
        "12647": {"comment":"Past $7FFF?"},
        "12651": {"comment":"Page 1 back"},
        "12653": {"comment":"Segment C freed (SEG_FREE)"},
        "12655": {"comment":"SEG_FREE: free segment C"},
        "12656": {"comment":"End of list"},
        "12657": {"comment":"Its slot: the tag"},
        "12659": {"comment":"The new slot"},
        "12661": {"comment":"Takes the tag"},
        "12663": {"synopsis":"Checks that ($022A) bytes fit above the variables ($0238) below the stack's top ($0228), and\nthat SP is not below $05FB.\nExit: NC when they fit; carry when the stack is too close; error 5100 (Insufficient stack\nspace) for SP.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"The variables' end"},
        "12666": {"comment":"Plus the bytes wanted"},
        "12670": {"comment":"Past $FFFF: carry"},
        "12673": {"comment":"The stack's top"},
        "12676": {"comment":"Too close: carry"},
        "12679": {"comment":"HL = 0 (carry is clear)"},
        "12682": {"comment":"The lowest SP allowed"},
        "12687": {"comment":"Enough: NC"},
        "12688": {"comment":"Error 5100 (Insufficient stack space)"},
        "12692": {"synopsis":"Jumps to entry A (0-7) of the word table that starts 2 bytes after the CALL; those 2 bytes\n(a JR, or a RET and a filler) are what the routine returns to. Callers pass the token's\nclass in the low bits ($0433, $091D).\nChanges: BC.","comment":"HL = the return address"},
        "12694": {"comment":"Entry A + 1: the table"},
        "12700": {"comment":"BC = the routine"},
        "12704": {"comment":"HL back; it returns after the CALL"},
        "12705": {"comment":"Jump to it"},
        "12707": {"synopsis":"Parses the rest of a statement as FROM #n and TO #n in any order, up to the line's end\n(error 20000 otherwise; FROM and TO are the texts at $3A24 and $3B3D).\nExit: B = the FROM channel (0 when absent), C = the TO channel (104 when absent).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"TO channel 104 when absent"},
        "12709": {"comment":"FROM channel 0 when absent"},
        "12710": {"synopsis":"B = the FROM channel."},
        "12711": {"synopsis":"Is the current word FROM? Then its channel goes to B.","comment":"'FROM'"},
        "12714": {"comment":"The current name? (NAME_MATCH)"},
        "12719": {"comment":"A = its '#n' (CHAN_ARG)"},
        "12724": {"synopsis":"Is it TO? Then its channel goes to C; neither: the line must end here.","comment":"'TO'"},
        "12730": {"comment":"Neither: the line's end"},
        "12732": {"comment":"Expected (TOKEN_EXPECT)"},
        "12735": {"comment":"A = its '#n'"},
        "12738": {"comment":"C = the TO channel"},
        "12741": {"synopsis":"Reads past the current word, expects '#' (symbol 3) and evaluates the number after it\n(BYTE_ARG_EVAL).\nExit: A = the number.","comment":"Past the word"},
        "12744": {"comment":"'#' must follow"},
        "12749": {"comment":"A = the number (BYTE_ARG_EVAL)"},
        "12752": {"synopsis":"Makes sure channel 0 works by writing a 0 to it (EXOS 7). If it fails: RUN_STATE_RESET, then\nCHANNELS_REOPEN.","comment":"Channel 0, character 0"},
        "12754": {"comment":"EXOS 7"},
        "12756": {"comment":"It works"},
        "12757": {"comment":"RUN_STATE_RESET"},
        "12760": {"synopsis":"Closes every channel 0-255 and opens the standard ones (STD_CHANNELS). If that fails, an\nEXOS reset (C = $60) and STD_CHANNELS again; then back to the command loop ($02EC). If even\nthat fails the machine stops, the border changing colour for ever. Called at start-up too\n($0244, $02C7).","comment":"From channel 0"},
        "12762": {"synopsis":"Closes channel H (EXOS 3), for every H."},
        "12763": {"comment":"EXOS 3: closed"},
        "12765": {"comment":"Up to 255"},
        "12768": {"comment":"The standard channels"},
        "12771": {"comment":"Opened: done"},
        "12772": {"comment":"Reset flags $60"},
        "12774": {"comment":"EXOS 0"},
        "12776": {"comment":"The interpreter's stack"},
        "12780": {"comment":"The standard channels again"},
        "12783": {"comment":"Opened: the command loop ($02EC)"},
        "12786": {"comment":"Nothing works"},
        "12787": {"synopsis":"Writes R to the border colour port ($81) for ever: the machine stops.","comment":"Border colour (port 81h) from R, for ever"},
        "12793": {"synopsis":"Sets the EXOS variables of EXOS_VAR_DEFS, then opens the standard channels: 105 KEYBOARD:\n(and FKEYS_DEFAULT programs the function keys), the screen and editor through TEXT_MODE_OPEN\nwith A =\n0, 103 SOUND: and 104 PRINTER:.\nExit: Z when all opened; NZ with the EXOS error otherwise.","comment":"The variable settings"},
        "12796": {"comment":"Written (EXOS_VARS_SET)"},
        "12799": {"comment":"'KEYBOARD:'"},
        "12802": {"comment":"Channel 105"},
        "12804": {"comment":"EXOS 1"},
        "12806": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "12807": {"comment":"The function keys (FKEYS_DEFAULT)"},
        "12808": {"comment":"FKEYS_DEFAULT: the 16 function keys"},
        "12809": {"comment":"End of list"},
        "12810": {"comment":"Screen mode 0"},
        "12811": {"comment":"Screen and editor channels (TEXT_MODE_OPEN)"},
        "12814": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "12815": {"comment":"Channel 103"},
        "12817": {"comment":"'SOUND:'"},
        "12822": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "12823": {"comment":"Channel 104"},
        "12825": {"comment":"'PRINTER:'"},
        "12830": {"comment":"Z when it opened"},
        "12831": {"synopsis":"EXOS variable settings written by STD_CHANNELS through EXOS_VARS_SET: pairs of variable\nnumber and value, ended by 0. RATE_KEY (10) = 3, DELAY_KEY (11) = 30, BUF_SND (15) = 20,\nBUF_EDIT (31) = 8."},
        "12840": {"synopsis":"When bit 6 of ($0200) says the program opened channels, closes channels 99 down to 1 and\nclears the bit. Called by RUN_STATE_RESET ($0554).","comment":"Channels opened?"},
        "12845": {"comment":"From channel 99"},
        "12847": {"synopsis":"Closes channel H, down to 1."},
        "12848": {"comment":"EXOS 3: closed"},
        "12850": {"comment":"Down to 1"},
        "12853": {"comment":"None open now"},
        "12858": {"synopsis":"Writes EXOS variables from a list at HL: pairs of variable number and value, ended by 0\n(EXOS 16 with B = 1).\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL.","comment":"The variable"},
        "12859": {"comment":"0 ends the list"},
        "12863": {"comment":"D = the value"},
        "12865": {"comment":"Write"},
        "12867": {"comment":"EXOS 16"},
        "12869": {"comment":"Next pair"},
        "12871": {"synopsis":"Error 20000 (Not understood) unless the current name is the counted word at HL (NAME_MATCH);\nthen reads the next token. HL is kept."},
        "12872": {"comment":"The word at HL? (NAME_MATCH)"},
        "12878": {"synopsis":"Reads the next token, then EXPECT_LINE_END.","comment":"Past this token"},
        "12881": {"synopsis":"Error 20000 (Not understood) unless the current symbol is the line's end (1); then\nTOKEN_NEXT.","comment":"The line's end"},
        "12883": {"synopsis":"IS-BASIC call $22: error 20000 (Not understood) unless the current symbol ($0204) is A; then\nTOKEN_NEXT.","comment":"The symbol A?"},
        "12886": {"synopsis":"NZ: error 20000 (Not understood); Z: on into TOKEN_NEXT.","comment":"No: error 20000"},
        "12889": {"synopsis":"IS-BASIC call $20: reads the token at ($0214) and moves ($0214) past it.\n1. ($0203) = the first byte's low 5 bits, ($0202) its top 3 (the class), ($0347) = the\n   address after the first byte, ($0204) = $7F (no symbol), ($0218) = 0.\n2. $60 keyword: ($0203) = the next byte, the keyword's number. $20/$40 names: the name\n   (($0203) letters) is skipped. $A0: ($0218) = the word that follows (a line number). $C0\n   constant: into the work item $0595, integer form ($0203) = 2, the word also in ($0218))\n   or a 6-byte float. $80 string: ($0203) = its length, text skipped.\n3. Any other byte is a symbol: ($0204) = it; 0 (the line's end) becomes symbol 1 and is not\n   passed.\nExit: A = ($0204); Z at the line's end. BC, DE, HL kept."},
        "12892": {"comment":"No word operand"},
        "12898": {"comment":"The read pointer"},
        "12901": {"comment":"The token's first byte"},
        "12902": {"comment":"Low 5 bits: a length or a type"},
        "12908": {"comment":"The token's text follows"},
        "12913": {"comment":"Not a symbol"},
        "12918": {"comment":"Top 3 bits: the class"},
        "12923": {"comment":"A keyword?"},
        "12927": {"comment":"Its number"},
        "12932": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "12935": {"synopsis":"A name ($20 numeric, $40 string)?","comment":"A numeric name?"},
        "12939": {"comment":"A string name?"},
        "12943": {"synopsis":"A name: skipped, its letters counted by ($0203).","comment":"Past the name"},
        "12949": {"synopsis":"A word operand ($A0, a line number)?","comment":"A line number?"},
        "12954": {"comment":"Its word"},
        "12958": {"comment":"As the word operand"},
        "12964": {"synopsis":"A numeric constant ($C0)? It goes to the work item $0595 (IY): an integer (type 2) or a\nfloat.","comment":"A numeric constant?"},
        "12970": {"comment":"Into the work item"},
        "12974": {"comment":"Its byte count"},
        "12977": {"comment":"2: an integer"},
        "12982": {"comment":"Integer form at IY (ITEM_ZERO_IY)"},
        "12985": {"comment":"The value"},
        "12989": {"comment":"As the word operand"},
        "12993": {"comment":"And as the work item's value"},
        "13001": {"synopsis":"A 6-byte float: the five mantissa bytes go to +2..+6 of the work item, the exponent to +8.","comment":"A zero float at IY (ZERO_FLT_IY)"},
        "13005": {"comment":"The mantissa from +2"},
        "13008": {"comment":"5 bytes"},
        "13013": {"comment":"+7 skipped"},
        "13014": {"comment":"The exponent at +8"},
        "13020": {"synopsis":"A string literal ($80)? Its length goes to ($0203) and its text is skipped.","comment":"A string literal?"},
        "13025": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "13026": {"comment":"As the token's length"},
        "13031": {"comment":"Past the text"},
        "13035": {"synopsis":"A symbol: its code; the line's end (0) becomes symbol 1 and the pointer stays on it.","comment":"The symbol's code"},
        "13036": {"comment":"The line's end (0)?"},
        "13039": {"comment":"Symbol 1"},
        "13040": {"comment":"The pointer stays on it"},
        "13041": {"synopsis":"Past the symbol byte; ($0204) = the symbol."},
        "13042": {"comment":"The symbol code"},
        "13045": {"synopsis":"Stores the moved read pointer and returns A = ($0204), Z at the line's end.","comment":"The read pointer"},
        "13051": {"comment":"Z at the line's end"},
        "13057": {"synopsis":"IS-BASIC call $01 (RST 20h comes here): raises error HL.\n1. ($023C) = HL. Writes ($0213) zero bytes to channel ($0209) (bytes still owed to it),\n   clears ($0213), sends output back to channel 0 ($0209), closes channel 106 and clears the\n   STOP request (bit 2 of ($0200)). PROG_PAGE_CUR pages the program's segments back in.\n2. A 5000-5999 error (memory) calls $0CCC first. The current line ($0216, perhaps changed by\n   that) is kept as the error's line, ($023E).\n3. No program running (bit 1 of ($0200) clear): ERR_REPORT.\n4. In a program: drops the value items off the stack, then walks the stack down for the\n   innermost exception record (type 8, its +1 = ($0240) - 1), remembering the last type 7\n   record passed; none: ERR_NO_HANDLER, which reports the error. Found: ERR_RUN_HANDLER.","comment":"The error number kept"},
        "13058": {"comment":"The last error"},
        "13061": {"comment":"Bytes owed to the channel"},
        "13065": {"synopsis":"Writes the owed zero bytes, L of them, to channel ($0209).","comment":"Any (left)?"},
        "13068": {"comment":"The output channel"},
        "13071": {"comment":"A zero byte"},
        "13073": {"comment":"EXOS 7"},
        "13077": {"synopsis":"Nothing owed now; output back to channel 0; channel 106 closed; no STOP request; the\nprogram's segments paged in.","comment":"Nothing owed now"},
        "13080": {"comment":"Output to channel 0"},
        "13083": {"comment":"Channel 106"},
        "13085": {"comment":"EXOS 3: closed"},
        "13087": {"comment":"No STOP request"},
        "13091": {"comment":"The program's segments in (PROG_PAGE_CUR)"},
        "13094": {"comment":"The error number"},
        "13096": {"comment":"Count its thousands"},
        "13099": {"comment":"A = -1, carry clear"},
        "13101": {"synopsis":"A = how many times 1000 goes into the error number.","comment":"Take 1000"},
        "13104": {"comment":"Until below zero"},
        "13106": {"comment":"A 5000s error (memory)?"},
        "13108": {"comment":"The current line"},
        "13111": {"comment":"Yes: $0CCC first"},
        "13114": {"comment":"The error's line"},
        "13117": {"synopsis":"HL is the error's line, the current one. Not in a program: ERR_REPORT; in one: the search\nfor a handler. A handler that passes the error on comes back here with its line.","comment":"Is current"},
        "13120": {"comment":"Running a program?"},
        "13124": {"comment":"No: report it"},
        "13127": {"comment":"The line kept"},
        "13128": {"synopsis":"Drops value items (types 1-3, ITEM_DROP's entry ITEM_DROP_IFVAL) until the top is another\nkind; HL =\nit.","comment":"A value item dropped?"},
        "13131": {"comment":"Until none"},
        "13133": {"comment":"No type 7 record seen yet"},
        "13138": {"synopsis":"Looks at the stack item at HL: the bottom (type 0) means no handler; a type 7 record's words\nare remembered; a type 8 record of the innermost level is the handler's.","comment":"The item's type"},
        "13139": {"comment":"The bottom?"},
        "13140": {"comment":"Yes: no handler"},
        "13143": {"comment":"DE = bytes +1, +2"},
        "13147": {"comment":"A type 7 record?"},
        "13151": {"comment":"Forget the earlier one"},
        "13156": {"comment":"BC = its bytes +3, +4"},
        "13160": {"comment":"Both words remembered"},
        "13162": {"synopsis":"A type 8 exception record whose level (+1) is ($0240) - 1 is the innermost one; other items\nare skipped.","comment":"An exception record (type 8)?"},
        "13166": {"comment":"The innermost level"},
        "13170": {"comment":"Is it this one?"},
        "13171": {"comment":"No: skip it"},
        "13173": {"comment":"One level fewer active"},
        "13176": {"comment":"DE = +2, +3: the handler's line"},
        "13180": {"comment":"The type 7 words go in at +4..+7"},
        "13189": {"comment":"Run the handler"},
        "13191": {"synopsis":"A type 8 record of an outer level: A = 8 again (it held the level).","comment":"Type 8 again"},
        "13193": {"synopsis":"Skips the item: HL is at its +2; a string also its length + 1 (one byte more than\nITEM_DROP's size; not run in the profile).","comment":"A string?"},
        "13199": {"comment":"Plus its length + 1"},
        "13201": {"synopsis":"Adds the type's ITEM_SIZES entry less 1 and looks at the next item."},
        "13202": {"comment":"ITEM_SIZES"},
        "13208": {"comment":"Less the byte already passed"},
        "13211": {"comment":"The next item"},
        "13213": {"synopsis":"Runs the handler of the exception record found.\n1. ($0216) = the handler's line; BLOCK_ENTER with keyword $23 (HANDLER): error 20000 if the\n   line is not a HANDLER, else the line after it is current.\n2. Keeps the record's place as an offset from the stack's bottom, MEM_ENSURE_DE for 8 bytes,\n   SCOPE_PUSH (with carry), ($0207) = 1, then runs the handler's lines ($0D68).\n3. By ($0207) when it is done: 0 runs the error's line again, 1 goes on at the line after\n   it, 2 raises the error again for an outer handler (ERR_AT_LINE), 3 or more leaves the\n   record's block (the rest of this routine).","comment":"The record's +7 kept"},
        "13214": {"comment":"The handler's line"},
        "13215": {"comment":"Is current"},
        "13218": {"comment":"Keyword $23, HANDLER"},
        "13220": {"comment":"Enter its block (BLOCK_ENTER)"},
        "13223": {"comment":"Not a HANDLER: error 20000"},
        "13226": {"comment":"The record's +7"},
        "13227": {"comment":"Back 5 (the ADD sets carry for the SBC)"},
        "13231": {"comment":"Less the bottom and 1: +1's offset"},
        "13237": {"comment":"Kept: the stack may move"},
        "13238": {"comment":"6 (+ 2) bytes"},
        "13241": {"comment":"MEM_ENSURE_DE"},
        "13245": {"comment":"SCOPE_PUSH"},
        "13248": {"comment":"Going on after the line, by default"},
        "13252": {"comment":"The handler's lines run ($0D68)"},
        "13255": {"comment":"The record's +1 again"},
        "13260": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "13261": {"comment":"HL = the error's line"},
        "13262": {"comment":"How the handler ended"},
        "13266": {"comment":"0: the same line again"},
        "13269": {"comment":"1: the line after it"},
        "13272": {"comment":"2: the error again, further out"},
        "13275": {"comment":"3 or more: leave the block"},
        "13276": {"comment":"The record's level"},
        "13277": {"comment":"Is the active count again"},
        "13283": {"comment":"The type 7 words: +4, +5"},
        "13286": {"comment":"None?"},
        "13292": {"comment":"The scope's start"},
        "13296": {"comment":"SCOPE_NAMES"},
        "13301": {"comment":"The variables' end"},
        "13305": {"synopsis":"The record's +6/+7 word, when not 0, becomes ($0236)."},
        "13306": {"comment":"+6, +7"},
        "13309": {"comment":"None?"},
        "13313": {"comment":"The scope's start"},
        "13317": {"synopsis":"The record's +8/+9 word goes back to ($023A); DE = +10/+11, the line the program goes on\nafter."},
        "13318": {"comment":"+8, +9"},
        "13321": {"comment":"Back in ($023A)"},
        "13326": {"comment":"+10, +11: the line to go on after"},
        "13329": {"comment":"Past the record"},
        "13330": {"comment":"Z for the jump below"},
        "13331": {"synopsis":"Makes HL the stack's top (dropping everything above it) and runs on from the line after line\nDE. $1EC6 comes here too.","comment":"The stack's new top"},
        "13334": {"comment":"The line"},
        "13335": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "13338": {"comment":"The line after it"},
        "13341": {"synopsis":"Handler ended with 1: the line after the error's line.","comment":"The line's length"},
        "13342": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "13343": {"comment":"The line after it"},
        "13344": {"synopsis":"The record's level + 1 is the active count again: the handler stays in force.","comment":"The record's level"},
        "13345": {"comment":"+ 1: still in force"},
        "13349": {"synopsis":"Runs the program on from line HL ($0D74), Z set."},
        "13350": {"synopsis":"Makes HL the current line and runs on from it: $0D74 with Z, $0D68 otherwise.","comment":"The line to run"},
        "13353": {"comment":"Run on from it ($0D74)"},
        "13356": {"comment":"Not Z: $0D68"},
        "13359": {"synopsis":"No handler: drops the two words and the line, then ERR_REPORT.","comment":"The two words and the line dropped"},
        "13362": {"synopsis":"Reports the error on channel 0 (CHAN0_CHECK first), after CR LF.\n1. Error 9229 (EXOS's STOP error, $E5): EXOS 16 reads CODE_SOFT_IRQ; for ?STOP ($20) the\n   STOP message (PRINT_STOP_MSG), bit 0 of ($0200) set and the command loop ($02EF); for\n   ?KEY ($21), KEY_IRQ is set to $FF and the error is reported.\n2. Otherwise \"***\" and the text from ERR_TEXT_BUILD; when it is only the error's class, \"\n   error type \" and the number; then \".\", character $19, CR LF.\n3. In a program, the error's line is listed ($08B2) when it lies in the program; then back\n   to the command loop ($02EC).","comment":"Channel 0 working (CHAN0_CHECK)"},
        "13365": {"comment":"CR LF (PRINT_CRLF)"},
        "13368": {"comment":"The error number"},
        "13369": {"comment":"9229: STOP (EXOS error $E5)?"},
        "13376": {"comment":"No"},
        "13378": {"comment":"Read CODE_SOFT_IRQ"},
        "13381": {"comment":"EXOS 16"},
        "13383": {"comment":"The code"},
        "13384": {"comment":"?STOP ($20)?"},
        "13388": {"comment":"?KEY ($21)?"},
        "13392": {"comment":"Write KEY_IRQ"},
        "13395": {"comment":"$FF: keys interrupt no more"},
        "13401": {"synopsis":"STOP pressed in a program: prints the STOP message, sets bit 0 of ($0200) and runs the\ncommand loop ($02EF); if that returns, the program goes on at the line ($0216) (not run in\nthe profile).","comment":"STOP message (PRINT_STOP_MSG)"},
        "13404": {"comment":"Bit 0 of ($0200)"},
        "13408": {"comment":"The line"},
        "13412": {"comment":"The command loop ($02EF)"},
        "13415": {"comment":"Back: on from the line"},
        "13418": {"synopsis":"Prints the error's message: \"***\", the text ERR_TEXT_BUILD made at $0446 and, when that is\nonly the error's class, \" error type \" and the number.","comment":"The text at $0446 (ERR_TEXT_BUILD)"},
        "13419": {"comment":"ERR_TEXT_BUILD: the text of error HL"},
        "13420": {"comment":"End of list"},
        "13421": {"comment":"Carry: its own text"},
        "13422": {"comment":"DE = the error number (when NC)"},
        "13423": {"comment":"'***' (the text after the CALL)"},
        "13426": {"synopsis":"The counted text \"***\" (length 3) that $0E00 prints for ERR_MESSAGE."},
        "13430": {"comment":"A space, then the message"},
        "13433": {"comment":"PRINT_COUNTED"},
        "13436": {"comment":"Its own text?"},
        "13437": {"comment":"Yes: no number"},
        "13439": {"comment":"' error type ' (the text after the CALL)"},
        "13442": {"synopsis":"The counted text \" error type \" (length 12) that $0E00 prints for ERR_MESSAGE."},
        "13455": {"comment":"HL = the error number"},
        "13456": {"comment":"NC: 5 places"},
        "13457": {"comment":"No padding (PRINT_DEC_PAD entry $2ED8)"},
        "13460": {"synopsis":"Ends the message with \".\", character $19 and CR LF, clears bit 3 of ($0200), lists the\nerror's line when a program ran, and goes back to the command loop.","comment":"'.', $19, CR LF (the text after the CALL)"},
        "13463": {"synopsis":"The counted text of length 4 that ends an error message: \".\", character $19, CR, LF."},
        "13468": {"comment":"Bit 3 of ($0200) cleared"},
        "13472": {"comment":"Running a program?"},
        "13476": {"comment":"No"},
        "13478": {"comment":"The error's line"},
        "13482": {"comment":"The program's start"},
        "13486": {"comment":"Carry when the line is in the program"},
        "13489": {"comment":"Then it is listed ($08B2)"},
        "13492": {"synopsis":"Clears bit 0 of ($0200) and goes back to the command loop ($02EC).","comment":"Bit 0 of ($0200) cleared"},
        "13496": {"comment":"The command loop ($02EC)"},
        "13499": {"synopsis":"Raises error 1000 (Unexpected value given).","comment":"Error 1000 (Unexpected value given)"},
        "13503": {"synopsis":"Raises error 1002 (Overflow in numeric expression).","comment":"Error 1002 (Overflow in numeric expression)"},
        "13507": {"synopsis":"Raises error 1106 (Overflow in string assignment).","comment":"Error 1106 (Overflow in string assignment)"},
        "13511": {"synopsis":"Raises error 2001 (Array subscript out of bounds).","comment":"Error 2001 (Array subscript out of bounds)"},
        "13515": {"synopsis":"Raises a 3000s error: the entries are LD L,n instructions, all but the first hidden in LD\nDE,$nn2E, sharing the H set at $34D6. ERR_3001 3001 (Division by zero), $34CE 3004 (Invalid\nargument to LOG), $34D1 3005 (Invalid argument to SQR), $34D4 3007 (Invalid argument to ASIN\nor ACOS).","comment":"Error 3001 (Division by zero)"},
        "13517": {"comment":"Entry $34CE: 3004 (Invalid argument to LOG)"},
        "13520": {"comment":"Entry $34D1: 3005 (Invalid argument to SQR)"},
        "13523": {"comment":"Entry $34D4: 3007 (Invalid argument to ASIN...)"},
        "13526": {"comment":"High byte: $0B00 + L"},
        "13528": {"comment":"Raised"},
        "13529": {"synopsis":"Raises a 4000s error, entries as at ERR_3001 (H set at $34ED): ERR_4000 4000 (Error in DEF\nparameter), $34DC 4002 (Argument to CHR$ out of range), $34DF 4003 (Invalid argument to\nORD), $34E2 4004 (Index to SIZE out of range), $34E5 4005 (Argument to TAB out of range),\n$34E8 4008 (Index to LBOUND out of range), $34EB 4009 (Index to UBOUND out of range).","comment":"Error 4000 (Error in DEF parameter)"},
        "13531": {"comment":"Entry $34DC: 4002 (Argument to CHR$ out of range)"},
        "13534": {"comment":"Entry $34DF: 4003 (Invalid argument to ORD)"},
        "13537": {"comment":"Entry $34E2: 4004 (Index to SIZE out of range)"},
        "13540": {"comment":"Entry $34E5: 4005 (Argument to TAB out of range)"},
        "13543": {"comment":"Entry $34E8: 4008 (Index to LBOUND out of range)"},
        "13546": {"comment":"Entry $34EB: 4009 (Index to UBOUND out of range)"},
        "13549": {"comment":"High byte: $0F00 + L"},
        "13551": {"comment":"Raised"},
        "13552": {"synopsis":"Raises error 4301 (Error in CHAIN parameters).","comment":"Error 4301 (Error in CHAIN parameters)"},
        "13556": {"synopsis":"Raises error 5110 (Insufficient extension space).","comment":"Error 5110 (Insufficient extension space)"},
        "13560": {"synopsis":"Raises error 5120 (Insufficient ALLOCATE space).","comment":"Error 5120 (Insufficient ALLOCATE space)"},
        "13564": {"synopsis":"Raises error 7001 (Invalid channel number).","comment":"Error 7001 (Invalid channel number)"},
        "13568": {"synopsis":"Raises error 7003 (Channel already open).","comment":"Error 7003 (Channel already open)"},
        "13572": {"synopsis":"Raises error 7401 (TRACE channel not open).","comment":"Error 7401 (TRACE channel not open)"},
        "13576": {"synopsis":"Raises error 8101 (Numeric data expected).","comment":"Error 8101 (Numeric data expected)"},
        "13580": {"synopsis":"Raises error 8201 (Invalid USING string).","comment":"Error 8201 (Invalid USING string)"},
        "13584": {"synopsis":"Raises error 8203 (USING format item too short).","comment":"Error 8203 (USING format item too short)"},
        "13588": {"synopsis":"Raises error 10002 (RETURN without GOSUB).","comment":"Error 10002 (RETURN without GOSUB)"},
        "13592": {"synopsis":"Raises error 10005 (Program does not exist).","comment":"Error 10005 (Program does not exist)"},
        "13596": {"synopsis":"Raises a 20000s error, entries as at ERR_3001 (H set at $3557): ERR_20000 20000 (Not\nunderstood), $351F 20001 (Invalid line number), $3522 20003 (no text of its own: a syntax\nerror), $3525 20004 (Line number does not exist), $3528 20010 (Cannot do specified\nRENUMBER), $352B 20020 (CONTINUE not possible), $352E 20030 (Identifier expected), $3531\n20031 (String identifier expected), $3534 20034 (Type mismatch), $3537 20040 (Variable not\ninitialised), $353A 20041 (Identifier declared twice), $353D 20043 (Missing closing quotes),\n$3540 20050 (Missing end of block), $3543 20051 (Invalid end of block), $3546 20052 (Too\nmany nested blocks), $3549 20060 (Invalid machine option use), $354C 20071 (Statement in\nimmediate mode), $354F 20072 (Command in program), $3552 20073 (Statement not allowed after\nTHEN), $3555 20081 (Programs do not VERIFY).","comment":"Error 20000 (Not understood)"},
        "13598": {"comment":"$351F: 20001 (Invalid line number)"},
        "13601": {"comment":"$3522: 20003 (no text: a syntax error)"},
        "13604": {"comment":"$3525: 20004 (Line number does not exist)"},
        "13607": {"comment":"$3528: 20010 (Cannot do specified RENUMBER)"},
        "13610": {"comment":"$352B: 20020 (CONTINUE not possible)"},
        "13613": {"comment":"$352E: 20030 (Identifier expected)"},
        "13616": {"comment":"$3531: 20031 (String identifier expected)"},
        "13619": {"comment":"$3534: 20034 (Type mismatch)"},
        "13622": {"comment":"$3537: 20040 (Variable not initialised)"},
        "13625": {"comment":"$353A: 20041 (Identifier declared twice)"},
        "13628": {"comment":"$353D: 20043 (Missing closing quotes)"},
        "13631": {"comment":"$3540: 20050 (Missing end of block)"},
        "13634": {"comment":"$3543: 20051 (Invalid end of block)"},
        "13637": {"comment":"$3546: 20052 (Too many nested blocks)"},
        "13640": {"comment":"$3549: 20060 (Invalid machine option use)"},
        "13643": {"comment":"$354C: 20071 (Statement in immediate mode)"},
        "13646": {"comment":"$354F: 20072 (Command in program)"},
        "13649": {"comment":"$3552: 20073 (Statement not allowed after THEN)"},
        "13652": {"comment":"$3555: 20081 (Programs do not VERIFY)"},
        "13655": {"comment":"High byte: $4E00 + L"},
        "13657": {"comment":"Raised"},
        "13658": {"synopsis":"NAME_MATCH with the counted text's address in the word after the CALL; returns past that\nword, DE kept. No caller of it was found in this ROM, and the profile did not run it.","comment":"The inline word's address"},
        "13659": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "13660": {"comment":"DE = the text's address"},
        "13664": {"comment":"Return past the word; HL = DE"},
        "13665": {"comment":"HL = the text, DE back"},
        "13666": {"synopsis":"Compares the current name (length (ix+3), text at ($0347)) with the counted text at HL,\nlength byte first.\nExit: Z (A = 0) when they are the same, NZ otherwise; HL moved on. BC, DE kept."},
        "13668": {"comment":"The current name's text"},
        "13672": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "13675": {"comment":"Compared first with the length byte"},
        "13676": {"comment":"Length + 1 bytes"},
        "13677": {"synopsis":"Compares a byte; the next character of the name in A.","comment":"The same?"},
        "13678": {"comment":"No: NZ"},
        "13681": {"comment":"The name's next character"},
        "13683": {"comment":"All compared?"},
        "13685": {"comment":"Same: Z"},
        "13686": {"synopsis":"Returns with BC and DE restored."},
        "13689": {"synopsis":"Builds the first block of the keyword chain at HL ($0232 = HL): a zero next-block word, a\ncount byte (counted up from what is there), then a 3-byte entry (address, this ROM's segment\nfrom $00C5) for every descriptor of the table at STMT_KEYWORDS, which ends with a $0000\nword. Then\nFN_TABLE_INSTALL (segment 1) puts the function names after the block. Called from start-up\n($02A9).\nDescriptor: +0 the action's address, +2 the check's address, +4 flags, +5 the name (length\nfirst).","comment":"The chain's first block"},
        "13692": {"comment":"This ROM's keyword table"},
        "13697": {"comment":"No next block"},
        "13701": {"comment":"IY = the count byte"},
        "13704": {"comment":"To the entries"},
        "13705": {"synopsis":"Adds the descriptor at DE as an entry and finds the next one.","comment":"One more keyword"},
        "13708": {"comment":"The descriptor's address"},
        "13712": {"comment":"This ROM's segment (the gate's)"},
        "13717": {"comment":"HL = the descriptor"},
        "13718": {"comment":"To its name at +5"},
        "13721": {"comment":"The name's length"},
        "13723": {"comment":"The next descriptor"},
        "13724": {"comment":"Its first word"},
        "13726": {"comment":"Zero ends the table?"},
        "13728": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "13731": {"comment":"Function names after the block (FN_TABLE_INSTALL)"},
        "13732": {"comment":"FN_TABLE_INSTALL: the function names"},
        "13733": {"comment":"End of list"},
        "13735": {"synopsis":"The statement keyword table: 93 entries, one per token $00-$5C, ended by a zero word\n(EMPTY_STRING). KW_CHAIN_INIT walks it at start-up and links each entry into the keyword\nchain at\n($0232) as a 3-byte record (entry address, segment 4); KEYWORD_ENTRY finds entry C through\nthat\nchain. An entry is: +0 the routine that runs the statement (called through KW_CALL_ACTION\nfrom $03A9\nfor a typed command and from $0DC5 in a program), +2 the routine run when the statement is\nentered (through KW_CALL_CHECK from $0394 and from $071B while a line is tokenised: CHK_SKIP\njust skips\nto the statement's end, $0A9C sets ($0206) = 2), +4 flags, +5 the name's length, +6 the name\n(LIST prints it from +5, $0962). Flags: bit 0 allowed as a typed command (else error 20071\nat $0383); bit 1 allowed in a program line (else error 20072 at $0701); bits 2-3 the block\nnesting segment 1's LINES_REINDENT reads (bit 3 opens a block: the next lines go one level\ndeeper; bit 2 closes one: this line goes one level out; both: this line only goes one level\nout, as CASE and ELSE); bit 4 may share a line with other statements after ':' ($071F,\n$0738, $1246: error 20074 / 20073 otherwise); bit 5 the run state is reset ($054D) before\nthe typed command runs ($0399); bit 6 the rest of the statement is tokenised ($041D), clear\nfor DATA, IMAGE, REM and ! whose text is kept. Several names are also used as words by the\nparser: CASE, DEF, DO, ELSE, EXIT, FOR, GOSUB, GOTO, GRAPHICS, HANDLER, IF, INPUT, SOUND and\nTEXT are matched through their entry's +5.","comment":"$00 ALLOCATE: runs $0CF8, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "13749": {"comment":"$01 ASK: runs $0E06, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "13758": {"comment":"$02 AUTO: runs $0823, entry check $0A9C, flags $41"},
        "13768": {"comment":"$03 CALL: runs $0E34, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "13778": {"comment":"$04 CAPTURE: runs $0E53, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "13791": {"comment":"$05 CASE: runs STMT_CASE, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $4E"},
        "13801": {"comment":"$06 CAUSE: runs $0E5C, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "13812": {"comment":"$07 CLEAR: runs KW_CLEAR, entry check CHK_CHANNEL, flags $53"},
        "13823": {"comment":"$08 CLOSE: runs $0FE6, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "13834": {"comment":"$09 CODE: runs $0FF0, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "13844": {"comment":"$0A CONTINUE: runs $0D4E, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $43"},
        "13858": {"comment":"$0B COPY: runs KW_COPY, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "13868": {"comment":"$0C DATA: runs $0A9C, entry check $0A9C, flags $02"},
        "13878": {"comment":"$0D DEF: runs $0A9C, entry check CHK_DEF, flags $42"},
        "13887": {"comment":"$0E DEF: runs BLOCK_DEF_SKIP, entry check $0A9C, flags $4A"},
        "13896": {"comment":"$0F DELETE: runs $083D, entry check $0A9C, flags $61"},
        "13908": {"comment":"$10 DIM: runs STMT_DIM, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $42"},
        "13917": {"comment":"$11 DISPLAY: runs STMT_DISPLAY, entry check CHK_CHANNEL, flags $53"},
        "13930": {"comment":"$12 DO: runs STMT_DO, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $4A"},
        "13938": {"comment":"$13 CHAIN: runs $0EAC, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "13949": {"comment":"$14 EDIT: runs $0797, entry check $0A9C, flags $41"},
        "13959": {"comment":"$15 ELSE: runs ELSE_STMT, entry check ELSE_CHECK, flags $4E"},
        "13969": {"comment":"$16 ELSE IF: runs ELSE_STMT, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $4E"},
        "13982": {"comment":"$17 END: runs $0FAD, entry check CHK_END, flags $42"},
        "13991": {"comment":"$18 END DEF: runs END_DEF_STMT, entry check $0A9C, flags $46"},
        "14004": {"comment":"$19 END HANDLER: runs END_HANDLER_STMT, entry check $0A9C, flags $46"},
        "14021": {"comment":"$1A END IF: runs $0A9C, entry check $0A9C, flags $46"},
        "14033": {"comment":"$1B END SELECT: runs $0A9C, entry check $0A9C, flags $46"},
        "14049": {"comment":"$1C END WHEN: runs STMT_END_WHEN, entry check $0A9C, flags $46"},
        "14063": {"comment":"$1D ENVELOPE: runs STMT_ENVELOPE, entry check CHK_CHANNEL, flags $53"},
        "14077": {"comment":"$1E EXIT: runs KW_EXIT, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $52"},
        "14087": {"comment":"$1F FOR: runs STMT_FOR, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $4A"},
        "14096": {"comment":"$20 GOSUB: runs KW_GOSUB, entry check CHK_LINE_NUM, flags $52"},
        "14107": {"comment":"$21 GOTO: runs KW_GOTO, entry check CHK_LINE_NUM, flags $52"},
        "14117": {"comment":"$22 GRAPHICS: runs STMT_GRAPHICS, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "14131": {"comment":"$23 HANDLER: runs BLOCK_DEF_SKIP, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $4A"},
        "14144": {"comment":"$24 IMAGE: runs $0A9C, entry check $0A9C, flags $02"},
        "14155": {"comment":"$25 IF: runs KW_IF, entry check CHK_IF, flags $42"},
        "14163": {"comment":"$26 IF: runs IFBLOCK_STMT, entry check $0A9C, flags $4A"},
        "14171": {"comment":"$27 INPUT: runs INPUT_STMT, entry check CHK_INPUT, flags $52"},
        "14182": {"comment":"$28 LET: runs KW_LET, entry check CHK_LET, flags $53"},
        "14191": {"comment":"$29 LINE: runs LINPUT_STMT, entry check CHK_LINE, flags $52"},
        "14201": {"comment":"$2A LIST: runs $082E, entry check $0A9C, flags $41"},
        "14211": {"comment":"$2B LOAD: runs $0AB5, entry check $0A9C, flags $61"},
        "14221": {"comment":"$2C LOOP: runs STMT_LOOP, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $46"},
        "14231": {"comment":"$2D MERGE: runs $0B8D, entry check $0A9C, flags $61"},
        "14242": {"comment":"$2E NEW: runs $0CA7, entry check $0A9C, flags $61"},
        "14251": {"comment":"$2F NEXT: runs STMT_NEXT, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $46"},
        "14261": {"comment":"$30 NUMERIC: runs STMT_NUMERIC, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $42"},
        "14274": {"comment":"$31 OPEN: runs KW_OPEN, entry check $0A9C, flags $53"},
        "14284": {"comment":"$32 OPTION: runs KW_OPTION, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $43"},
        "14296": {"comment":"$33 OK: runs ERR_TO_COMMANDS, entry check $0A9C, flags $41"},
        "14304": {"comment":"$34 OUT: runs KW_OUT, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "14313": {"comment":"$35 PLOT: runs STMT_PLOT, entry check CHK_CHANNEL, flags $53"},
        "14323": {"comment":"$36 POKE: runs KW_POKE, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "14333": {"comment":"$37 SPOKE: runs KW_SPOKE, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "14344": {"comment":"$38 PRINT: runs $1408, entry check CHK_PRINT, flags $53"},
        "14355": {"comment":"$39 PROGRAM: runs $0A9C, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $42"},
        "14368": {"comment":"$3A RANDOMIZE: runs KW_RANDOMIZE, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $52"},
        "14383": {"comment":"$3B READ: runs READ_STMT, entry check CHK_READ, flags $52"},
        "14393": {"comment":"$3C REDIRECT: runs REDIRECT_STMT, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "14407": {"comment":"$3D REM: runs $0A9C, entry check $0A9C, flags $03"},
        "14416": {"comment":"$3E RENUMBER: runs $0827, entry check $0A9C, flags $41"},
        "14430": {"comment":"$3F RESTORE: runs RESTORE_STMT, entry check LINEREF_NEXT, flags $52"},
        "14443": {"comment":"$40 RETRY: runs RETRY_STMT, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $42"},
        "14454": {"comment":"$41 RETURN: runs RETURN_STMT, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $52"},
        "14466": {"comment":"$42 RUN: runs $0E7E, entry check LINEREF_NEXT, flags $53"},
        "14475": {"comment":"$43 SAVE: runs $09FC, entry check $0A9C, flags $61"},
        "14485": {"comment":"$44 SELECT: runs STMT_SELECT, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $4A"},
        "14497": {"comment":"$45 SET: runs SET_STMT, entry check CHK_CHANNEL, flags $53"},
        "14506": {"comment":"$46 SOUND: runs STMT_SOUND, entry check CHK_CHANNEL, flags $53"},
        "14517": {"comment":"$47 START: runs $0E78, entry check $0A9C, flags $61"},
        "14528": {"comment":"$48 STOP: runs STOP_STMT, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $52"},
        "14538": {"comment":"$49 INFO: runs INFO_STMT, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $51"},
        "14548": {"comment":"$4A STRING: runs STMT_STRING, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $42"},
        "14560": {"comment":"$4B TEXT: runs STMT_TEXT, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "14570": {"comment":"$4C TOGGLE: runs TOGGLE_STMT, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "14582": {"comment":"$4D TRACE: runs TRACE_STMT, entry check CHK_CHANNEL, flags $53"},
        "14593": {"comment":"$4E TYPE: runs STMT_TYPE, entry check $0A9C, flags $53"},
        "14603": {"comment":"$4F VERIFY: runs $0BD7, entry check $0A9C, flags $61"},
        "14615": {"comment":"$50 WHEN: runs STMT_WHEN, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $4A"},
        "14625": {"comment":"$51 !: runs $0A9C, entry check $0A9C, flags $13"},
        "14632": {"comment":"$52 LLIST: runs $082B, entry check $0A9C, flags $41"},
        "14643": {"comment":"$53 LPRINT: runs KW_LPRINT, entry check CHK_PRINT, flags $53"},
        "14655": {"comment":"$54 EXT: runs EXT_STMT, entry check CHK_SKIP, flags $53"},
        "14664": {"comment":"$55 GET: runs KW_GET, entry check CHK_CHANNEL, flags $53"},
        "14673": {"comment":"$56 FLUSH: runs KW_FLUSH, entry check $0A9C, flags $53"},
        "14684": {"comment":"$57 LOOK: runs KW_LOOK, entry check $0A9C, flags $43"},
        "14694": {"comment":"$58 PING: runs KW_PING, entry check $0A9C, flags $53"},
        "14704": {"comment":"$59 DATE: runs KW_DATE, entry check $0A9C, flags $53"},
        "14714": {"comment":"$5A TIME: runs KW_TIME, entry check $0A9C, flags $53"},
        "14724": {"comment":"$5B WAIT: runs WAIT_STMT, entry check $0A9C, flags $53"},
        "14734": {"comment":"$5C ON: runs KW_ON, entry check CHK_ON, flags $42"},
        "14742": {"synopsis":"The zero word that ends STMT_KEYWORDS ($359C stops on it). Its first byte doubles as an\nempty length-first string: $0A17, $0C95 and $1843 (EXT) point DE here when no argument was\ngiven."},
        "14744": {"synopsis":"Length-first words (a length byte, then the text) for the parser and for EXOS calls, in two\nruns: $3998-$3A28 and $3A7F-$3B5F. Each is reached by its own address: the statements match\nthe current name against one with NAME_MATCH (Z when equal) or WORD_EXPECT (error 20000\nunless equal),\nand the device names and command strings go to EXOS 1 and EXOS 26 in DE. \":\" ($39ED), TAB\nand USING have no reference in this ROM or in EXOS segment 1.","comment":"\"ACCESS\", used at $1342"},
        "14751": {"comment":"\"ALL\", used at $09FC, $0CAE"},
        "14755": {"comment":"\"ANGLE\", used at KW_OPTION, PLOT_TRY_ANGLE"},
        "14761": {"comment":"\"AT\", used at LOOK_AT, IO_OPT_AT, DISPLAY_WORD"},
        "14764": {"comment":"\"ATTRIBUTE\", used at STMT_GRAPHICS"},
        "14774": {"comment":"\"BACK\", used at PLOT_TRY_MOVE"},
        "14779": {"comment":"\"BAND\", used at $1F4B"},
        "14784": {"comment":"\"AND\", used at AND_LOOP"},
        "14788": {"comment":"\"BNOT\", used at $1F8A"},
        "14793": {"comment":"\"NOT\", used at EXPR_NOT_LEVEL"},
        "14797": {"comment":"\"BOR\", used at $1EFB"},
        "14801": {"comment":"\"OR\", used at OR_LOOP"},
        "14804": {"comment":"\"DEGREES\", used at $13A1"},
        "14812": {"comment":"\"DURATION\", used at SND_WORDS"},
        "14821": {"synopsis":"Length-first device name \"EDITOR:\" for EXOS 1 (open channel 0, TEXT_PAGE_OPEN $3D44).","comment":"\"EDITOR:\", used at $3D44"},
        "14829": {"comment":"\":\": no reference found"},
        "14831": {"comment":"\"ELLIPSE\", used at PLOT_TRY_ELL"},
        "14839": {"comment":"\"ENVELOPE\", used at $14C3, SND_WORDS"},
        "14848": {"comment":"\"EXCEPTION\", used at $0E5C, STMT_WHEN"},
        "14858": {"synopsis":"Length-first command string \"BASICX\", handed to the ROM extensions with EXOS 26 at $02B5.","comment":"\"BASICX\", used at $02B5"},
        "14865": {"comment":"\"FKEYS\", used at CLEAR_OPTION"},
        "14871": {"comment":"\"FONT\", used at CLEAR_FONT"},
        "14876": {"comment":"\"FORWARD\", used at $3E06"},
        "14884": {"comment":"\"FROM\", used at PFT_LOOP, DISPLAY_FROM"},
        "14889": {"synopsis":"\"BASIC version 2.1\", CR, LF: 19 bytes the extension entry writes with EXOS 8 for :HELP\n(action 3, DE set at $0082)."},
        "14908": {"synopsis":"The 60-byte banner written for :HELP BASIC (DE set at $0091): three spaces, \"Enterprise\nIS-BASIC\", CR LF, three spaces, character $80, \" 1985 Intelligent Software Ltd\", CR LF."},
        "14968": {"synopsis":"EXT statement, its end (jumped to from EXT_SCAN): hands the length-first command string at\nDE\nto the ROM extensions with EXOS 26, raises an EXOS error (RST 18h), then drops the top item\nwith call $16 (the argument string).\nEntry: DE = the string (EMPTY_STRING when EXT has no argument).","comment":"EXOS 26: offer the command to the extensions"},
        "14970": {"comment":"Error 9000 + A when an extension failed"},
        "14971": {"comment":"Drop the argument string"},
        "14975": {"synopsis":"The second run of NAME_WORDS (HIRES ... WP), after the texts and EXT_PASS_CMD.","comment":"\"HIRES\", used at $3CA6"},
        "14981": {"comment":"\"INTERRUPT\", used at SND_WORDS"},
        "14991": {"comment":"\"IS\", used at $1C41"},
        "14994": {"comment":"\"PAINT\", used at $3DAA"},
        "15000": {"synopsis":"Length-first device name \"KEYBOARD:\" for EXOS 1 (channel $69 at $31FF).","comment":"\"KEYBOARD:\", used at $31FF"},
        "15010": {"comment":"\"LEFT\", used at $3DBF, SND_WORDS"},
        "15015": {"comment":"\"LORES\", used at $3C9C"},
        "15021": {"comment":"\"MISSING\", used at $1543"},
        "15029": {"synopsis":"Length-first name \"BASIC\": the extension entry compares a command string with it at $00B5\n(action 2).","comment":"\"BASIC\", used at $00B5"},
        "15035": {"comment":"\"NAME\", used at $132C"},
        "15040": {"comment":"\"NET\", used at $142B"},
        "15044": {"comment":"\"NUMBER\", used at ENV_NUMBER"},
        "15051": {"comment":"\"OFF\", used at $1974"},
        "15055": {"comment":"\"ON\", used at TRACE_STMT"},
        "15058": {"comment":"\"OUTPUT\", used at $1353"},
        "15065": {"comment":"\"PITCH\", used at SND_WORDS"},
        "15071": {"synopsis":"Length-first device name \"PRINTER:\" for EXOS 1 (channel $68 at $3219).","comment":"\"PRINTER:\", used at $3219"},
        "15080": {"comment":"\"PROMPT\", used at IO_OPT_PROMPT"},
        "15087": {"comment":"\"QUEUE\", used at $14BF"},
        "15093": {"comment":"\"RADIANS\", used at $1399"},
        "15101": {"comment":"\"RELEASE\", used at $3EAE"},
        "15109": {"comment":"\"REF\", used at $1A3D"},
        "15113": {"comment":"\"RIGHT\", used at $3DB6, SND_WORDS"},
        "15119": {"comment":"\"SCREEN\", used at $14AF"},
        "15126": {"synopsis":"Length-first device name \"SOUND:\" for EXOS 1 (channel $67 at $3211).","comment":"\"SOUND:\", used at $3211"},
        "15133": {"comment":"\"SOURCE\", used at SND_WORDS"},
        "15140": {"comment":"\"STEP\", used at $1D8E"},
        "15145": {"comment":"\"STYLE\", used at SND_WORDS"},
        "15151": {"comment":"\"SYNC\", used at SND_WORDS"},
        "15156": {"comment":"\"TAB\": no reference found"},
        "15160": {"comment":"\"THEN\", used at $121A, $19B9"},
        "15165": {"comment":"\"TO\", used at $198B, $1C6F, $1D85, $2313, $2C25, PFT_TO, DISPLAY_TO"},
        "15168": {"comment":"\"UNTIL\", used at $1D3C"},
        "15174": {"comment":"\"USE\", used at $1E4E"},
        "15178": {"comment":"\"USING\": no reference found"},
        "15184": {"synopsis":"Length-first device name \"VIDEO:\" for EXOS 1 (channels $66 at $3D3E and $65 at $3D61).","comment":"\"VIDEO:\", used at $3D3E, $3D61"},
        "15191": {"comment":"\"WHILE\", used at $1D46"},
        "15197": {"synopsis":"Length-first command string \"WP\", handed to the ROM extensions with EXOS 26 by STMT_TYPE\n($3C02).","comment":"\"WP\", used at $3C02"},
        "15200": {"synopsis":"Writes ESC and then character B to the current channel: falls into PRINT_CHAR with A = B.\nEntry: B = the escape letter.","comment":"ESC"},
        "15205": {"comment":"The letter; into PRINT_CHAR"},
        "15206": {"synopsis":"Writes character A to channel ($0209), or stores it at ($0242)++ when ($0209) = $FF; an EXOS\nerror is raised (RST 18h). The EXOS call is hidden in LD HL,$07F7: its operand bytes are RST\n30h and function 7 (write character), entered at $3B7C.\nEntry: A = the character.\nChanges: nothing (all registers kept).","comment":"Keep every register"},
        "15211": {"comment":"Current channel"},
        "15214": {"comment":"Into memory?"},
        "15218": {"comment":"Yes: store at ($0242) and advance it"},
        "15226": {"comment":"A = 0: no error"},
        "15227": {"comment":"Skips; from $3B70 enters at $3B7C: RST 30h, EXOS 7 (write char)"},
        "15230": {"comment":"Error 9000 + A on an EXOS error"},
        "15234": {"synopsis":"PRINT_COUNTED's exit: restores BC and returns.","comment":"Restore BC"},
        "15236": {"synopsis":"Prints the length-first string at HL through PRINT_CHAR.\nEntry: HL = the length byte.\nExit: HL = the string's last byte.\nChanges: A, HL."},
        "15237": {"comment":"B = the length"},
        "15238": {"synopsis":"Prints B characters from HL + 1 (B may be 0); $095A enters here with BC saved.\nEntry: B = the count, HL = one before the text.","comment":"Into the counting loop"},
        "15239": {"synopsis":"Loop: prints the next character until B runs out.","comment":"All printed?"},
        "15249": {"synopsis":"Prints A spaces (none when A is 0).\nEntry: A = the count.\nChanges: A.","comment":"Count down; done when below 0"},
        "15258": {"synopsis":"Prints one space through PRINT_CHAR.","comment":"Space"},
        "15262": {"synopsis":"Reads a key from the keyboard channel $69 if one is waiting: EXOS 9 (channel status) first,\nthen EXOS 5 (read character).\nExit: A = the character (also in ($0205)) and NZ; A = 0 and Z when no key or on an error.","comment":"Keyboard channel"},
        "15266": {"comment":"Error: no key"},
        "15268": {"comment":"Status C = 0 means a character is ready"},
        "15271": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "15277": {"comment":"The key, kept in ($0205)"},
        "15283": {"synopsis":"No key: A = 0, Z.","comment":"No key"},
        "15285": {"synopsis":"Reads a line from channel ($0209) into the buffer at $0248 with EXOS 5: a zero byte and\ncontrol characters other than CR are dropped, characters past 248 are dropped, CR ends it.\nThe text goes from $0249 and ends in 00h; ($0248) = the text's length + 2 (the length byte\nand the 00h counted, as in a program line).\nExit: NC with the line; C with ($0248) = 0 when EXOS returned .EOF ($E4).\nChanges: A, DE, HL.","comment":"Carry: no character read yet"},
        "15286": {"synopsis":"INPUT_LINE's body; $03D7 enters here with carry set itself. Entered with carry clear it\nwould start with character B already read.","comment":"Line buffer: length byte, then the text"},
        "15289": {"comment":"E = the length so far, the length byte counted"},
        "15293": {"synopsis":"Loop: reads the next character into B.","comment":"Current channel"},
        "15297": {"comment":"Read character into B"},
        "15302": {"comment":".EOF?"},
        "15306": {"comment":"Another EXOS error: error 9000 + A"},
        "15307": {"synopsis":"End of file: empties the buffer and returns carry.","comment":"Empty line"},
        "15314": {"synopsis":"Sorts one character: zero and control characters are skipped, CR ends the line.","comment":"The character"},
        "15315": {"comment":"Zero: skip it"},
        "15318": {"comment":"Printable?"},
        "15322": {"comment":"CR? (A = 0 then)"},
        "15326": {"comment":"CR: the 00h stored next is not text"},
        "15327": {"synopsis":"Stores character D after the text unless the buffer is full; 00h (from CR) ends the line.","comment":"D = the character, or 0 for CR"},
        "15330": {"comment":"Full (248 characters)? Drop it"},
        "15334": {"comment":"Count and store it"},
        "15337": {"comment":"The end (CR)?"},
        "15341": {"comment":"Count the 00h too"},
        "15342": {"comment":"Set the length byte"},
        "15346": {"comment":"NC: a line was read"},
        "15348": {"synopsis":"Prints CR and LF through PRINT_CHAR.","comment":"CR"},
        "15353": {"comment":"LF"},
        "15358": {"synopsis":"TYPE statement (keyword $4E): EXIT_CONFIRM asks \"Press ENTER to exit BASIC\" when typed at\nthe\nprompt (Z on ENTER, always Z in a program); then the command string \"WP\" (WP_CMD) is offered\nto the ROM extensions with EXOS 26. Returns at once when another key was pressed.","comment":"Confirm with ENTER (at the prompt)"},
        "15361": {"comment":"Another key: back"},
        "15362": {"comment":"WP_CMD"},
        "15365": {"comment":"Offer it to the extensions"},
        "15368": {"synopsis":"TEXT statement (keyword $4B): TEXT, TEXT 40 or TEXT 80. Sets ($020E) (MODE_VID for the text\npage: 0 for 40 columns, 2 for 80), closes the graphics page (channel $65), reopens the\n24-line text page (TEXT_OPEN) and raises its EXOS error. Any other width is error 1000.","comment":"No argument?"},
        "15373": {"comment":"A = the width"},
        "15376": {"comment":"80 columns?"},
        "15378": {"comment":"MODE_VID 2"},
        "15382": {"comment":"40 columns?"},
        "15384": {"comment":"Error 1000: Unexpected value given"},
        "15387": {"comment":"MODE_VID 0"},
        "15389": {"synopsis":"Keeps the text mode in ($020E).","comment":"Text page mode"},
        "15392": {"synopsis":"Closes the graphics page (errors ignored), then reopens the text page.","comment":"Graphics page channel"},
        "15398": {"synopsis":"DISPLAY TEXT: shows rows 1-24 of the text page (channel $66) from screen row 1; on an error\nreopens the text page.","comment":"Past TEXT"},
        "15401": {"comment":"Text page channel"},
        "15403": {"comment":"24 rows at screen row 1"},
        "15410": {"synopsis":"Reopens and shows the text page (TEXT_OPEN) and raises its EXOS error.","comment":"Reopen the text page"},
        "15413": {"comment":"Error 9000 + A"},
        "15415": {"synopsis":"DISPLAY statement (keyword $11): DISPLAY TEXT, DISPLAY GRAPHICS, or DISPLAY [#channel:] with\nAT row, FROM row and TO row in any order (defaults 1, 1 and 24): EXOS 11 @@DISP (B = 1)\nshows rows FROM to TO of the page (default channel $65) from screen row AT. The current\nchannel is put back at the end (CHAN_RESTORE).","comment":"TEXT? (the keyword table's name)"},
        "15423": {"comment":"GRAPHICS? (the keyword table's name)"},
        "15432": {"comment":"Optional #channel: Z when one was given"},
        "15435": {"comment":"Keep the current channel for CHAN_RESTORE"},
        "15438": {"comment":"Default: the graphics page"},
        "15440": {"synopsis":"Sets the defaults: AT 1, TO 24, FROM 1.","comment":"Keep the channel"},
        "15441": {"comment":"E = AT row 1"},
        "15443": {"comment":"D = TO row 24"},
        "15445": {"comment":"C = FROM row 1"},
        "15446": {"synopsis":"Loop: reads AT, TO or FROM and its value; anything else ends the list.","comment":"AT?"},
        "15454": {"comment":"E = the screen row"},
        "15460": {"synopsis":"TO n: the last row of the page.","comment":"TO?"},
        "15468": {"comment":"D = the last row"},
        "15474": {"synopsis":"FROM n: the first row of the page.","comment":"FROM?"},
        "15482": {"comment":"C = the first row"},
        "15488": {"synopsis":"Shows the rows: EXOS 11 @@DISP with C = first row, D = row count, E = screen row.","comment":"D = TO - FROM + 1 rows"},
        "15492": {"comment":"A = the channel"},
        "15493": {"comment":"@@DISP: show the page"},
        "15497": {"comment":"Error 9000 + A"},
        "15498": {"synopsis":"Puts back the current channel ($0209) the statement saved: pops the BC that followed $0C60\n(B = the channel before it). Many statements jump here to finish.\nEntry: the saved BC on the stack, under the return address.","comment":"A = the saved channel"},
        "15503": {"synopsis":"GRAPHICS statement (keyword $22): GRAPHICS [HIRES | LORES | ATTRIBUTE] [2 | 4 | 16 | 256].\n1. Picks the video mode: ATTRIBUTE 15 (2 colours), LORES 5, HIRES 1, none the last one\n   ($020F).\n2. Picks the colour mode from the number: 2 -> 0, 4 -> 1, 16 -> 2, 256 -> 3, none the last\n   one ($0210); others are error 1000.\n3. Keeps both, closes the graphics page (channel $65), reopens the text page 4 rows tall at\n   screen rows 21-24 (TEXT_OPEN_DE with DE = $0415) and opens and shows the 20-row graphics\n   page (GR_REOPEN).","comment":"ATTRIBUTE?"},
        "15509": {"comment":"MODE_VID 15: attribute graphics"},
        "15511": {"comment":"Colour mode 0: 2 colours"},
        "15513": {"comment":"Carry: read past the word at GR_STORE"},
        "15516": {"comment":"LORES?"},
        "15522": {"comment":"Video mode 5"},
        "15526": {"comment":"HIRES?"},
        "15532": {"comment":"MODE_VID 1: high resolution"},
        "15536": {"comment":"No word: the last video mode"},
        "15539": {"synopsis":"Reads the optional colour count.","comment":"Keep the mode"},
        "15540": {"comment":"The last colour mode"},
        "15543": {"comment":"Past HIRES or LORES"},
        "15546": {"comment":"No number?"},
        "15551": {"comment":"HL = the colour count"},
        "15554": {"comment":"256 colours?"},
        "15557": {"comment":"Colour mode 3"},
        "15561": {"comment":"Above 255?"},
        "15566": {"comment":"16 colours: mode 2"},
        "15571": {"comment":"4 colours: mode 1"},
        "15576": {"comment":"2 colours: mode 0"},
        "15578": {"synopsis":"Any other count: error 1000.","comment":"Error 1000: Unexpected value given"},
        "15581": {"synopsis":"Gets the video mode back.","comment":"D = the video mode"},
        "15582": {"synopsis":"Keeps the modes in ($020F)/($0210), closes the graphics page and rebuilds the screen.","comment":"Past ATTRIBUTE"},
        "15585": {"comment":"Video mode"},
        "15588": {"comment":"Colour mode"},
        "15591": {"comment":"Close the graphics page (errors ignored)"},
        "15595": {"comment":"Text page: 4 rows, shown at screen row 21"},
        "15601": {"comment":"Error 9000 + A"},
        "15604": {"synopsis":"DISPLAY GRAPHICS: shows rows 1-20 of the graphics page (channel $65) from screen row 1; on\nan error reopens the graphics page.","comment":"Past GRAPHICS"},
        "15607": {"comment":"Graphics page channel"},
        "15609": {"comment":"20 rows at screen row 1"},
        "15616": {"synopsis":"Reopens the graphics page in the kept modes and raises its EXOS error.","comment":"Video mode"},
        "15619": {"comment":"Colour mode"},
        "15625": {"comment":"Error 9000 + A"},
        "15627": {"synopsis":"Sets the text page's mode ($020E) and falls into TEXT_OPEN ($320B calls it with A = 0 at\nstart-up).\nEntry: A = the MODE_VID value (0 or 2).","comment":"Text page mode"},
        "15630": {"synopsis":"Opens the text page 24 rows tall and shows it from screen row 1.","comment":"24 rows at screen row 1"},
        "15633": {"synopsis":"Opens the text page (TEXT_PAGE_OPEN) D rows tall, then shows its D rows from screen row E.\nEntry: D = the height, E = the screen row.\nExit: Z and A = 0 when it worked, else the EXOS error.","comment":"Keep the height and the row"},
        "15638": {"comment":"Open failed"},
        "15639": {"comment":"Text page channel"},
        "15641": {"synopsis":"Shows a video page: EXOS 11 @@DISP from its row 1.\nEntry: A = the channel, D = the row count, E = the screen row.\nExit: A = the EXOS status, Z when it worked.","comment":"@@DISP (B = 1), first row 1"},
        "15644": {"comment":"EXOS 11: special function"},
        "15647": {"synopsis":"Opens the text page and the editor:\n1. Writes EXOS variables Y_SIZ_VID = D, MODE_VID = ($020E), then COLR_VID 0, X_SIZ_VID 40,\n   VID_EDIT $66, KEY_EDIT $69 (list TEXT_PAGE_VARS).\n2. Closes channel 0 and the text page $66, lets STACK_RELOCATE ($3010) rearrange BASIC's\n   RAM.\n3. Opens $66 as \"VIDEO:\" and channel 0 as \"EDITOR:\".\nEntry: D = the page height in rows.\nExit: Z when both opened, else NZ with the EXOS error in A.","comment":"Write Y_SIZ_VID (25) = D"},
        "15652": {"comment":"Text mode"},
        "15655": {"comment":"Write MODE_VID (22)"},
        "15660": {"comment":"COLR_VID, X_SIZ_VID, VID_EDIT, KEY_EDIT"},
        "15663": {"comment":"Write the list"},
        "15666": {"comment":"Close channel 0 (the editor)"},
        "15669": {"comment":"Close the text page"},
        "15673": {"comment":"Rearrange the RAM BASIC holds"},
        "15676": {"comment":"Open the text page"},
        "15678": {"comment":"VIDEO_DEVICE"},
        "15683": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "15684": {"comment":"Channel 0 (A = 0): EDITOR_DEVICE"},
        "15690": {"synopsis":"Opens the graphics page: writes MODE_VID = D and COLR_VID = B, X_SIZ_VID 40 and Y_SIZ_VID 20\n(GR_PAGE_VARS), lets STACK_RELOCATE ($3010) rearrange the RAM, opens channel $65 as \"VIDEO:\"\nand shows its 20 rows from screen row 1 (PAGE_DISPLAY).\nEntry: D = the video mode, B = the colour mode.\nExit: Z when it worked, else the EXOS error in A.","comment":"Keep the colour mode"},
        "15691": {"comment":"Write MODE_VID (22) = D"},
        "15698": {"comment":"COLR_VID (23)"},
        "15699": {"comment":"D = the colour mode"},
        "15702": {"comment":"X_SIZ_VID 40, Y_SIZ_VID 20"},
        "15708": {"comment":"Rearrange the RAM BASIC holds"},
        "15711": {"comment":"Graphics page channel"},
        "15713": {"comment":"VIDEO_DEVICE"},
        "15718": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "15721": {"comment":"20 rows at screen row 1"},
        "15726": {"synopsis":"EXOS variables for the graphics page, as (number, value) pairs ended by 0, written by\nEXOS_VARS_SET:\nX_SIZ_VID (24) = 40, Y_SIZ_VID (25) = 20."},
        "15731": {"synopsis":"EXOS variables for the text page, as (number, value) pairs ended by 0, written by\nEXOS_VARS_SET:\nCOLR_VID (23) = 0, X_SIZ_VID (24) = 40, VID_EDIT (29) = $66, KEY_EDIT (30) = $69."},
        "15740": {"synopsis":"Ends PLOT: sends the pending beam escape (ESC s, or ESC S after a final \";\") and puts the\nchannel back.","comment":"ESC B: the beam state"},
        "15746": {"synopsis":"PLOT statement (keyword $35), on the graphics page (channel $65) unless #channel is given.\nIt reads items until the statement ends: x,y moves the beam there (ESC A x y) and sends ESC\nS (beam on) when \";\" or the end follows, ESC s when \",\" follows; ELLIPSE x,y draws an\nellipse (ESC E x y); PAINT fills (ESC F); LEFT a / RIGHT a turn the heading kept at $0E19\n(radians, kept between 0 and 2pi; a is converted when OPTION ANGLE DEGREES is on); ANGLE a\nsets it; FORWARD d / BACK d move by d along it (ESC R dx dy with dx = d*COS, dy = d*SIN). At\nthe end the beam is switched off (ESC s) unless the last item ended with \";\".","comment":"Optional #channel: Z when one was given"},
        "15749": {"comment":"Keep the current channel for CHAN_RESTORE"},
        "15752": {"comment":"Default: the graphics page"},
        "15757": {"synopsis":"Next item; B = the beam escape pending ('s', beam off).","comment":"B = 's' after INC B, and NZ"},
        "15760": {"synopsis":"Reads past a separator (when Z) and looks at the next item.","comment":"Past the separator"},
        "15763": {"comment":"The symbol"},
        "15766": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "15770": {"comment":"Statement end (:)?"},
        "15774": {"comment":"\",\"?"},
        "15776": {"comment":"Beam off pending"},
        "15780": {"comment":"\";\"?"},
        "15782": {"comment":"Beam on pending"},
        "15786": {"comment":"PAINT?"},
        "15792": {"comment":"ESC F: fill"},
        "15795": {"comment":"Yes: past PAINT, send it"},
        "15798": {"comment":"RIGHT? (carry marks it)"},
        "15807": {"comment":"LEFT?"},
        "15815": {"synopsis":"LEFT a / RIGHT a: heading + a or heading - a (a in radians).","comment":"Carry: RIGHT"},
        "15816": {"comment":"Push the heading at $0E19, read the angle"},
        "15825": {"comment":"RIGHT?"},
        "15827": {"comment":"LEFT: heading + a"},
        "15830": {"comment":"NC: skip the subtraction"},
        "15831": {"synopsis":"RIGHT: heading - a.","comment":"RIGHT: heading - a"},
        "15834": {"synopsis":"Loop: adds 2pi while the heading is negative.","comment":"Negative?"},
        "15839": {"comment":"Add 2pi (constant $0A)"},
        "15846": {"synopsis":"Loop: subtracts 2pi while the heading is 2pi or more.","comment":"Compare a copy with 2pi"},
        "15852": {"comment":"Below 2pi: done"},
        "15855": {"comment":"Subtract 2pi"},
        "15862": {"synopsis":"Stores the heading at $0E19 and goes on to the separator.","comment":"Pop the heading into $0E19"},
        "15867": {"comment":"Look at the separator"},
        "15869": {"synopsis":"Tries BACK and FORWARD.","comment":"BACK? (carry marks it)"},
        "15878": {"comment":"FORWARD?"},
        "15886": {"synopsis":"FORWARD d / BACK d: sends a relative move (ESC R) of d*COS(heading), d*SIN(heading).","comment":"Carry: BACK"},
        "15887": {"comment":"Read the next token, evaluate d"},
        "15891": {"comment":"IY = the top item"},
        "15895": {"comment":"BACK: d = -d"},
        "15898": {"comment":"Copy d"},
        "15901": {"comment":"HL = INT(d * COS(heading))"},
        "15909": {"comment":"Keep dx"},
        "15910": {"comment":"HL = INT(d * SIN(heading))"},
        "15918": {"comment":"DE = dx, HL = dy"},
        "15919": {"comment":"ESC R: relative beam move"},
        "15923": {"synopsis":"ANGLE a: sets the heading.","comment":"ANGLE?"},
        "15931": {"comment":"Read a, to radians when DEGREES"},
        "15938": {"synopsis":"ELLIPSE x,y or a point x,y.","comment":"ELLIPSE?"},
        "15944": {"comment":"ESC A: absolute beam move"},
        "15948": {"comment":"Past ELLIPSE"},
        "15951": {"comment":"ESC E: ellipse"},
        "15953": {"synopsis":"Reads x,y.","comment":"Keep the escape letter"},
        "15954": {"comment":"DE = x, HL = y"},
        "15958": {"synopsis":"Sends ESC B with the two words DE and HL.","comment":"ESC B, DE, HL"},
        "15961": {"synopsis":"After an item: \",\" switches the beam off (ESC s), anything else on (ESC S).","comment":"The symbol"},
        "15964": {"comment":"\",\"?"},
        "15966": {"comment":"Beam off"},
        "15970": {"comment":"Beam on"},
        "15972": {"comment":"NC: no token to read"},
        "15973": {"synopsis":"Sends ESC B (reading past a word first when carry is set), then the next item.","comment":"Past the word"},
        "15976": {"comment":"Send ESC B"},
        "15979": {"comment":"Next item"},
        "15982": {"synopsis":"Reads two numbers separated by \",\".\nExit: DE = the first, HL = the second.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = the first number"},
        "15986": {"comment":"\",\" expected"},
        "15991": {"comment":"HL = the second number"},
        "15994": {"comment":"DE = the first"},
        "15996": {"synopsis":"Sends ESC B, then the word DE and the word HL (low byte first).","comment":"ESC B"},
        "16000": {"comment":"Word DE"},
        "16004": {"synopsis":"Writes HL to the current channel, low byte first.\nChanges: A.","comment":"Low byte"},
        "16008": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "16012": {"synopsis":"ENVELOPE statement (keyword $1D): ENVELOPE [#channel:] NUMBER n; phase; phase ... where a\nphase is c, l, r, d (pitch change in semitones, left and right amplitude change, duration)\nor RELEASE. Sends ESC E n, phases, release phase, then per phase c*512 (word), l, r, d\n(word) to the sound channel ($67 unless #channel is given).\n1. First pass (B bit 0 clear): the phases are parsed without computing, counting them in D\n   and keeping in E the count before RELEASE ($FF: none).\n2. Rewinds the text to the saved point, sends ESC E, n, D, E.\n3. Second pass (B = 'E', bit 0 set): evaluates each phase and sends it; the end goes to\n   CHAN_RESTORE.","comment":"Optional #channel: Z when one was given"},
        "16015": {"comment":"Keep the current channel for CHAN_RESTORE"},
        "16018": {"comment":"Default: the sound channel"},
        "16023": {"synopsis":"Expects NUMBER and reads the envelope number.","comment":"NUMBER expected (error 20000)"},
        "16029": {"comment":"Where to rewind for the second pass"},
        "16032": {"comment":"A = the envelope number"},
        "16037": {"comment":"No phases yet, no release phase ($FF)"},
        "16040": {"comment":"B = 0: parse without computing"},
        "16041": {"synopsis":"Loop: \";\" then RELEASE or a phase.","comment":"\";\" expected"},
        "16046": {"comment":"RELEASE?"},
        "16052": {"comment":"Yes: enters at $3EFD (LD E,D: release after D phases)"},
        "16055": {"comment":"Three values followed by \",\""},
        "16057": {"synopsis":"Loop: one value and the \",\" after it.","comment":"Evaluate (or parse) one value"},
        "16061": {"comment":"\",\" expected"},
        "16070": {"comment":"The fourth value: the duration"},
        "16074": {"comment":"One phase more"},
        "16075": {"comment":"Second pass?"},
        "16079": {"comment":"DE = the duration"},
        "16083": {"comment":"C = the right amplitude change"},
        "16087": {"comment":"B = the left amplitude change"},
        "16093": {"comment":"Pitch change times 512"},
        "16102": {"comment":"HL = INT(change * 512)"},
        "16105": {"comment":"Send it as a word"},
        "16110": {"comment":"Left change"},
        "16114": {"comment":"Right change"},
        "16118": {"comment":"Duration word"},
        "16122": {"comment":"Second pass flag back"},
        "16124": {"synopsis":"After a phase: OR $5A makes NZ so no token is read; from RELEASE the jump enters at $3EFD\n(LD E,D) with Z and reads past it.","comment":"NZ; from $3EB4 at $3EFD: E = D"},
        "16126": {"comment":"RELEASE: past it"},
        "16129": {"comment":"Statement end?"},
        "16134": {"comment":"Second pass done?"},
        "16139": {"comment":"Start the second pass"},
        "16141": {"comment":"Rewind the text"},
        "16148": {"comment":"ESC E (B = 'E' keeps bit 0 set)"},
        "16153": {"comment":"Envelope number"},
        "16157": {"comment":"Number of phases"},
        "16161": {"comment":"Phases before the release"},
        "16168": {"synopsis":"SOUND statement (keyword $46): SOUND [#channel:] then any of ENVELOPE n, PITCH p, LEFT l,\nRIGHT r, STYLE s, SOURCE s, DURATION d, SYNC n, INTERRUPT, separated by \",\" or \";\".\n1. Copies the 12-byte default sequence SND_DEFAULTS to $0E20.\n2. Looks each word up in SND_WORDS: its flags say whether a value follows, the field's size\n   and how it is stored; the value goes into the copy at $0E21 + the field's position.\n3. Sends the 12 bytes (ESC S env pitch left right style source duration flags) to the sound\n   channel ($67 unless #channel is given) and puts the channel back. An unknown word is\n   error 20000.","comment":"Optional #channel: Z when one was given"},
        "16171": {"comment":"Keep the current channel for CHAN_RESTORE"},
        "16174": {"comment":"Default: the sound channel"},
        "16179": {"synopsis":"Copies the defaults to $0E20.","comment":"SND_DEFAULTS"},
        "16190": {"comment":"B = 1: NZ, no token to read"},
        "16191": {"synopsis":"Loop: reads past a separator (when Z) and looks at the next word.","comment":"Past it"},
        "16194": {"comment":"Statement end: send"},
        "16200": {"comment":"\";\"?"},
        "16204": {"comment":"\",\"?"},
        "16208": {"comment":"C = the field's position"},
        "16210": {"comment":"SND_WORDS"},
        "16213": {"synopsis":"Loop: compares the current name with the next SND_WORDS entry.","comment":"Count the field"},
        "16214": {"comment":"B = the flags"},
        "16216": {"comment":"$FF: not found, error 20000"},
        "16221": {"comment":"DE = the word"},
        "16227": {"comment":"Is it this one?"},
        "16233": {"comment":"A two-byte field?"},
        "16237": {"comment":"It takes two positions"},
        "16240": {"synopsis":"Found: reads the value (flag bit 0) or uses $80 (INTERRUPT).","comment":"C = the field's position - 1"},
        "16241": {"comment":"A value follows?"},
        "16243": {"comment":"No: E = $80 (INTERRUPT)"},
        "16248": {"comment":"Position from $0E21"},
        "16250": {"comment":"Read the next token, evaluate the value"},
        "16254": {"comment":"Times 512 (PITCH)?"},
        "16259": {"comment":"Pitch in semitones times 512"},
        "16268": {"synopsis":"A two-byte field takes 0-65535: 32768 is subtracted before the integer pop and added back\nafter.","comment":"Two-byte field?"},
        "16272": {"comment":"No offset"},
        "16277": {"comment":"Minus 32768 (constant 3)"},
        "16282": {"comment":"Add $8000 back after the pop"},
        "16285": {"synopsis":"Pops the value into DE.","comment":"Keep the offset"},
        "16286": {"comment":"HL = the value"},
        "16291": {"comment":"DE = the value"},
        "16293": {"synopsis":"Stores E at $0E21 + C (ORed into the old byte with flag bit 2), D after it for a two-byte\nfield; a one-byte value must have D = 0 or $FF (else error 1000).","comment":"Flags"},
        "16294": {"comment":"OR into the old byte (INTERRUPT)?"},
        "16298": {"comment":"The field in the copy"},
        "16305": {"comment":"Not ORed: replace"},
        "16306": {"synopsis":"Stores the byte.","comment":"Merge in the value"},
        "16309": {"comment":"Two-byte field? Enters at $3FC1 (INC HL, LD (HL),D)"},
        "16313": {"comment":"High byte $FF?"},
        "16316": {"comment":"Or 0?"},
        "16317": {"comment":"Error 1000: Unexpected value given"},
        "16320": {"comment":"Skips; from $3FB7 enters at $3FC1: high byte stored"},
        "16323": {"synopsis":"Z: reads past the separator and goes on.","comment":"Z"},
        "16327": {"synopsis":"Sends the 12 bytes at $0E20 and puts the channel back.","comment":"The sequence"},
        "16332": {"synopsis":"Loop: sends the next byte.","comment":"Send a byte"},
        "16339": {"comment":"Put the channel back"},
        "16342": {"synopsis":"The default note STMT_SOUND copies to $0E20: ESC S, envelope $FF, pitch $4A00 (37 semitones\nin 1/512 units), left $FF, right $FF, style 0, source 0, duration $0032 (50), flags 0."},
        "16354": {"synopsis":"STMT_SOUND's words: 9 entries of a flag byte and a word's address (in NAME_WORDS), ended by\n$FF; the order gives the field's place in the sequence. Flags: bit 0 a value follows, bit 1\na two-byte field, bit 2 the value is ORed into the old byte, bit 3 the value is multiplied\nby 512. ENVELOPE $01, PITCH $0B, LEFT $01, RIGHT $01, STYLE $01, SOURCE $01, DURATION $03,\nSYNC $01, INTERRUPT $04 (ORs $80 into the flag byte).","comment":"ENVELOPE: the envelope field"},
        "16357": {"comment":"PITCH: the pitch field"},
        "16360": {"comment":"LEFT: the left amplitude field"},
        "16363": {"comment":"RIGHT: the right amplitude field"},
        "16366": {"comment":"STYLE: the style field"},
        "16369": {"comment":"SOURCE: the source field"},
        "16372": {"comment":"DURATION: the duration field"},
        "16375": {"comment":"SYNC: the flags (sync) field"},
        "16378": {"comment":"INTERRUPT: the flags bit 7 field"},
        "16381": {"comment":"End of SND_WORDS"},
        "16382": {"comment":"Not read by any code found"}
      }
    }
  },
